"celle d’un éclair."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4016
msgid ""
"This Pikachu wears its partner's cap, which\\nis proof of the strong bond "
"Pikachu and\\nits partner formed during adventures\\nacross the world "
"together."
msgstr ""
"Il stocke de l’électricité dans les poches\\nde ses joues. Quand il relâche "
"d’un coup\\ntoute l’énergie accumulée, la puissance\\nélectrique équivaut à "
"celle d’un éclair."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4093
msgid ""
"When it smashes its opponents with\\nits bolt-shaped tail, it delivers "
"a\\nsurge of electricity equivalent to a\\nlightning strike."
msgstr ""
"Quand il frappe ses ennemis avec sa\\nqueue en forme d’éclair, il libère "
"une\\ndécharge électrique aussi forte que\\nla foudre."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4243
msgid ""
"If it stores too much electricity, its\\nbehavior turns aggressive. To avoid"
" this,\\nit occasionally discharges excess energy\\nand calms itself down."
msgstr ""
"Il devient agressif s’il stocke trop\\nd’électricité. Pour éviter ça, il "
"relâche de\\ntemps en temps son surplus d’énergie\\net parvient ainsi à se "
"calmer."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4323
msgid "RAICHU-A"
msgstr "RAICHU-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4336
msgid ""
"It uses psychokinesis to control\\nelectricity. It focuses psychic "
"energy\\ninto its tail and rides it like it's surfing.\\nAnother name for "
"this Pokémon is 'hodad'."
msgstr ""
"Il devient agressif s’il stocke trop\\nd’électricité. Pour éviter ça, il "
"relâche de\\ntemps en temps son surplus d’énergie\\net parvient ainsi à se "
"calmer."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4413
msgid ""
"It resembles an X as it flies through\\nthe air with 50 million volts "
"of\\nelectricity sparking from its ears and\\nforked tail."
msgstr ""
"Il ressemble à un X lorsqu’il fend les\\nairs, ses oreilles et sa "
"queue\\nfourchue crépitant de 50 millions de\\nvolts."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4474
msgid ""
"It fires bolts of electricity from the\\ntip of its tail and from the spiky "
"tufts\\nof fur growing out of its temples. This\\nelectricity forms the "
"letter Y."
msgstr ""
"Il tire des éclairs du bout de sa queue\\net des touffes de poils pointues "
"de\\nses tempes. Cette électricité forme la\\nlettre Y."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4526
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4674
msgid "SANDSHREW"
msgstr "SABELETTE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4532
msgid ""
"When it curls up in a ball, it can make any\\nattack bounce off harmlessly. "
"Its hide has\\nturned tough and solid as a result of\\nliving in the desert."
msgstr ""
"Quand il se met en boule, il est capable\\nd’attaquer en rebondissant sans "
"se\\nblesser. Le désert a rendu sa peau\\ndure et résistante."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4605
msgid ""
"It curls up in a ball to protect itself from\\nenemy attacks. It also curls "
"up to prevent\\nheatstroke during the daytime when\\ntemperatures rise "
"sharply."
msgstr ""
"Il se roule sur lui-même pour se protéger\\ndes attaques de ses ennemis. "
"Cette\\ntechnique lui permet aussi de se protéger\\ndu soleil pendant la "
"journée."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4672
msgid "SANDSHREW-A"
msgstr "SABELETTE-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4685
msgid ""
"Life on mountains covered with deep snow\\nhas granted this Pokémon a body "
"of ice\\nthat's as hard as steel.\\nPredators go after its soft belly."
msgstr ""
"Quand il se met en boule, il est capable\\nd’attaquer en rebondissant sans "
"se\\nblesser. Le désert a rendu sa peau\\ndure et résistante."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4753
msgid "SANDSLASH-A"
msgstr "SABLAIREAU-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4766
msgid ""
"It uses large, hooked claws to cut a path\\nthrough deep snow as it "
"runs.\\nOn snowy mountains, this Sandslash\\nis faster than any other "
"Pokémon."
msgstr ""
"Il se roule sur lui-même pour se protéger\\ndes attaques de ses ennemis. "
"Cette\\ntechnique lui permet aussi de se protéger\\ndu soleil pendant la "
"journée."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4840
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4920
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5069
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5142
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:7477
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:7543
msgid "Poison Pin"
msgstr "Vénépic"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4843
msgid ""
"Its highly toxic barbs are thought to have\\ndeveloped as protection for "
"this small-\\nbodied Pokémon. When enraged, it releases\\na horrible toxin "
"from its horn."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon est couvert de pointes qui\\nsécrètent un poison puissant. Il "
"les\\nutilise pour se défendre. Quand il est en\\ncolère, une toxine sort de"
" sa corne."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:4923
msgid ""
"When it is with its friends or\\nfamily, its barbs are tucked away "
"to\\nprevent injury. It appears to become\\nnervous if separated from the "
"others."
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu’un Nidorina est avec ses amis ou\\nsa famille, il replie ses pointes "
"pour ne\\npas blesser ses proches. Il devient vite\\nnerveux lorsqu’il est "
"séparé de son groupe."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5002
msgid ""
"It is adept at sending foes flying with\\nharsh tackles using its tough, "
"scaly body.\\nThis Pokémon is at its strongest when\\nit is defending its "
"young."
msgstr ""
"Son corps est protégé par des écailles\\nextrêmement dures. Il envoie ses "
"ennemis\\nvoler en leur fonçant dessus. Il utilise\\ntoute sa force pour "
"protéger ses petits."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5072
msgid ""
"The male Nidoran has developed muscles\\nthat freely move its ears in any "
"direction.\\nEven the slightest sound does not escape\\nthis Pokémon's "
"notice."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon est couvert de pointes qui\\nsécrètent un poison puissant. Il "
"les\\nutilise pour se défendre. Quand il est en\\ncolère, une toxine sort de"
" sa corne."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5145
msgid ""
"Its horn is harder than a diamond.\\nIf it senses a hostile presence, all "
"the\\nbarbs on its back bristle up at once, and it\\nchallenges the foe with"
" all its might."
msgstr ""
"Il dispose d’une corne plus dure que du\\ndiamant. S’il sent une présence "
"hostile,\\ntoutes les pointes de son dos se hérissent\\nd’un coup, puis il "
"défie son ennemi."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5225
msgid ""
"A Nidoking's thick tail packs enormously\\ndestructive power capable of "
"toppling\\na metal transmission tower. Once it goes\\non a rampage, there is"
" no stopping it."
msgstr ""
"Son épaisse queue est d’une puissance\\nincroyable. En un seul coup, il "
"peut\\nrenverser une tour métallique. Lorsqu’il\\nse déchaîne, plus rien ne "
"peut l’arrêter."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5306
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16397
msgid "Star Shape"
msgstr "Étoile"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5309
msgid ""
"On nights with many shooting stars,\\nCleffa can be seen dancing in a "
"ring.\\nThey dance until daybreak, when they\\nquench their thirst with the "
"morning dew."
msgstr ""
"Les nuits où il y a des étoiles filantes, on\\npeut voir des Melo danser en "
"cercle. Ils\\ndansent toute la nuit et se désaltèrent\\navec la rosée du "
"matin."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5383
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5465
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5540
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5037
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5113
msgid "Fairy"
msgstr "Fée"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5386
msgid ""
"On every night of a full moon, they come\\nout to play. When dawn arrives, "
"the tired\\nClefairy go to sleep nestled up against\\neach other in deep and"
" quiet mountains."
msgstr ""
"Les nuits de pleine lune, ces Pokémon\\nsortent jouer. A l’aube, ils "
"rentrent dans\\nleur retraite montagneuse et dorment\\nblottis les uns "
"contre les autres."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5468
msgid ""
"A Clefable uses its wings to skip lightly \\nas if it were flying. Its "
"bouncy step\\nlets it even walk on water. On quiet,\\nmoonlit nights, it "
"strolls on lakes."
msgstr ""
"Ils se déplacent en sautant doucement,\\ncomme s’ils volaient. Cela leur "
"permet même\\nde marcher sur l’eau. Les soirs où la lune\\nest claire, ils "
"se promènent sur les lacs."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5543
msgid ""
"It flies by using the power of\\nmoonlight to control gravity within\\na "
"radius of over 32 feet around it."
msgstr ""
"Il vole en utilisant le pouvoir du\\nclair de lune pour contrôler "
"la\\ngravité dans un rayon de plus de\\n10 mètres autour de lui."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5324
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5595
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5744
msgid "VULPIX"
msgstr "GOUPIX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5598
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5672
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5752
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5834
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:300
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:373
msgid "Fox"
msgstr "Renard"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5601
msgid ""
"It can freely control fire, making fiery\\norbs fly like will-o'-the-wisps. "
"Just\\nbefore evolution, its six tails grow hot \\nas if on fire."
msgstr ""
"Il peut contrôler le feu à sa guise. Juste\\navant d’évoluer, ses six queues"
" deviennent\\nsi chaudes qu’on les croirait enflammées."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5675
msgid ""
"It has long been said that each of the\\nnine tails embody an enchanted "
"power.\\nA long-lived Ninetales will have fur that\\nshines like gold."
msgstr ""
"On raconte depuis longtemps que chacune\\nde ses neuf queues possède un "
"pouvoir\\nmagique. Un Feunard très âgé se\\nreconnaît à sa fourrure dorée."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5742
msgid "VULPIX-A"
msgstr "GOUPIX-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5755
msgid ""
"They live together in a skulk, helping\\none another. In hot weather, this "
"Pokémon\\nmakes ice shards with its six tails and\\nsprays them around to "
"cool itself off."
msgstr ""
"Il peut contrôler le feu à sa guise. Juste\\navant d’évoluer, ses six queues"
" deviennent\\nsi chaudes qu’on les croirait enflammées."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5824
msgid "NINETALES-A"
msgstr "FEUNARD-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5837
msgid ""
"While it will guide travelers who get lost\\non a snowy mountain down to "
"the\\nmountain's base, it won't forgive anyone\\nwho harms nature."
msgstr ""
"On raconte depuis longtemps que chacune\\nde ses neuf queues possède un "
"pouvoir\\nmagique. Un Feunard très âgé se\\nreconnaît à sa fourrure dorée."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5919
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5997
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6089
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5188
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5273
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3333
msgid "Balloon"
msgstr "Bouboule"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:5922
msgid ""
"Its soft and pliable body is very bouncy.\\nWhen it sings continuously with "
"all its\\nmight, its body steadily turns a deepening\\npink color."
msgstr ""
"Son corps doux et souple est très\\nélastique. Quand il chante de toutes "
"ses\\nforces, son corps se couvre d’un rose\\nprofond."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6000
msgid ""
"Nothing can avoid falling asleep hearing a\\nJigglypuff's song. The sound "
"waves of its\\nsinging voice match the brain waves of\\nsomeone in a deep "
"sleep."
msgstr ""
"Ceux qui entendent sa chanson ne\\npeuvent s’empêcher de dormir. Les "
"ondes\\nsonores de sa voix correspondent aux\\nondes cérébrales d’une "
"personne endormie."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6092
msgid ""
"Its fur is the ultimate in luxuriousness.\\nSleeping alongside a Wigglytuff "
"is simply\\ndivine. Its body expands seemingly without\\nend when it "
"inhales."
msgstr ""
"Sa fourrure soyeuse fait sa fierté. La\\ntouffe sur son front est si douce "
"que la\\ncaresser donne l’impression d’être sur un\\npetit nuage."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6160
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6253
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6360
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2574
msgid "Bat"
msgstr "Chovsouris"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6163
msgid ""
"While living in pitch-black caverns, their\\neyes gradually grew shut and "
"deprived\\nthem of vision. They use ultrasonic waves\\nto detect obstacles."
msgstr ""
"Il a perdu l’usage de ses yeux à force\\nde vivre dans des cavernes "
"obscures.\\nIl utilise les ultrasons pour détecter\\nles obstacles."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6256
msgid ""
"Its fangs easily puncture even thick\\nanimal hide. It loves to feast on the"
" blood\\nof people and Pokémon. It flits about in\\ndarkness and strikes "
"from behind."
msgstr ""
"Ses dents acérées peuvent transpercer\\nfacilement la peau d’un animal. Il "
"attaque\\npar derrière et dans le noir pour se\\nrassasier du sang de ses "
"victimes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6363
msgid ""
"Over the course of evolution, its hind legs\\nturned into wings. By "
"alternately resting\\nits front and rear wings, it can fly all day\\nwithout"
" having to stop."
msgstr ""
"Au cours de son évolution, ses pattes\\narrière se sont transformées en une "
"paire\\nd’ailes. En alternant entre ses ailes avant\\net arrière, il peut "
"voler sans s’arrêter."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6446
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6521
msgid "Weed"
msgstr "Racine"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6449
msgid ""
"This Pokémon grows by absorbing moonlight.\\nDuring the daytime, it buries "
"itself in the\\nground, leaving only its leaves exposed to\\navoid detection"
" by its enemies."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon grandit en absorbant la\\nlumière de la lune. La journée, il "
"s’enfouit\\nsous terre pour se cacher et ne laisse\\ndépasser que ses "
"feuilles."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5895
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6518
msgid "GLOOM"
msgstr "ORTIDE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6524
msgid ""
"A horribly noxious honey drools from its\\nmouth. One whiff of the honey can"
" result\\nin memory loss. Some fans are said to\\nenjoy this overwhelming "
"stink, however."
msgstr ""
"Un filet de miel nauséabond s’écoule\\nde sa bouche. Le sentir peut "
"entraîner\\nune perte de mémoire mais on raconte\\nque des gens raffolent de"
" cette odeur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6616
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6705
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9622
msgid "Flower"
msgstr "Fleur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6619
msgid ""
"In seasons when it produces more pollen,\\nthe air around a Vileplume turns "
"yellow\\nwith the powder as it walks. The pollen is\\nhighly toxic and "
"causes paralysis."
msgstr ""
"Les saisons où il produit le plus de pollen,\\nun nuage jaune se forme "
"autour de\\nlui lorsqu’il marche. Ce pollen est\\nhautement toxique et cause"
" la paralysie."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6708
msgid ""
"Its flower petals deepen in color through\\nexposure to sunlight. When "
"cloudy weather\\npersists, it does a dance that is thought\\nto be a ritual "
"for summoning the sun."
msgstr ""
"La couleur de ses pétales se renforce\\ns’ils sont exposés à la lumière. "
"Quand le\\ntemps est couvert, il pratique une danse\\nrituelle pour appeler "
"le soleil."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6791
msgid "PARAS"
msgstr "PARAS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6794
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6886
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3349
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3432
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8828
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8902
msgid "Mushroom"
msgstr "Champignon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6797
msgid ""
"A Paras has parasitic tochukaso\\nmushrooms growing on its back. They "
"grow\\nby drawing nutrients from the host. They\\nare valued as a medicine "
"for long life."
msgstr ""
"Des champignons parasites appelés\\ntochukaso poussent sur son dos "
"et\\ngrandissent grâce à ses nutriments. Ces\\nchampignons sont un élixir de"
" longue vie."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6889
msgid ""
"Parasect are known to infest the roots of\\nlarge trees en masse and drain "
"nutrients.\\nWhen an infested tree dies, they move\\nonto another tree all "
"at once."
msgstr ""
"En groupe, les Parasect infestent le tronc\\net les racines des grands "
"arbres pour se\\nnourrir de nutriments. Lorsqu’un arbre\\nmeurt, ils se "
"précipitent vers le prochain."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6960
msgid "VENONAT"
msgstr "MIMITOSS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6963
msgid "Insect"
msgstr "Vermine"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:6966
msgid ""
"Its coat of thin, stiff hair that covers\\nits entire body is said to have "
"evolved\\nfor protection. Its large eyes never fail\\nto spot even miniscule"
" prey."
msgstr ""
"On raconte qu’il a évolué avec une fourrure\\nde poils fins et drus qui "
"protège son\\ncorps. Ses grands yeux sont capables\\nde repérer ses proies, "
"même minuscules."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5826
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7039
msgid "VENOMOTH"
msgstr "AEROMITE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7042
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1830
msgid "Poison Moth"
msgstr "Papipoison"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7045
msgid ""
"Venomoth are nocturnal--they are only\\nactive at night. Their favorite prey"
" are\\ninsects that gather around streetlights,\\nattracted by the light in "
"the darkness."
msgstr ""
"C’est un Pokémon nocturne, il ne sort donc\\nque la nuit. Ses proies "
"préférées sont les\\npetits insectes qui se rassemblent autour\\ndes "
"réverbères, attirés par la lumière."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7129
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7288
msgid "DIGLETT"
msgstr "TAUPIQUEUR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7132
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7210
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7296
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7378
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2734
msgid "Mole"
msgstr "Taupe"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7135
msgid ""
"Diglett are raised in most farms.\\nThe reason is simple--wherever "
"they\\nburrow, the soil is left perfectly tilled\\nfor growing delicious "
"crops."
msgstr ""
"Il est élevé dans la plupart des fermes.\\nEn effet, lorsqu’il creuse "
"quelque part, le\\nsol est comme labouré. On peut alors y\\nplanter de "
"délicieux légumes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8878
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7207
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7370
msgid "DUGTRIO"
msgstr "TRIOPIKEUR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7213
msgid ""
"Because the triplets originally split from\\none body, they think exactly "
"alike.\\nThey work cooperatively to burrow\\nendlessly through the ground."
msgstr ""
"Ce sont des triplés qui ont émergé du même\\ncorps. Chacun pense exactement "
"comme les\\ndeux autres. Ils creusent inlassablement,\\ndans une coopération"
" parfaite."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7286
msgid "DIGLETT-A"
msgstr "TAUPIQUEUR-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7299
msgid ""
"The metal-rich geology of its habitat\\ncaused it to develop steel whiskers "
"on its\\nhead that change shape depending on its\\nmood and when "
"communicating with others."
msgstr ""
"Il est élevé dans la plupart des fermes.\\nEn effet, lorsqu’il creuse "
"quelque part, le\\nsol est comme labouré. On peut alors y\\nplanter de "
"délicieux légumes."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7368
msgid "DUGTRIO-A"
msgstr "TRIOPIKEUR-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7381
msgid ""
"Their beautiful, metallic whiskers create\\na sort of protective helmet "
"on\\nheir heads, and they also function\\nas highly precise sensors."
msgstr ""
"Ce sont des triplés qui ont émergé du même\\ncorps. Chacun pense exactement "
"comme les\\ndeux autres. Ils creusent inlassablement,\\ndans une coopération"
" parfaite."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7458
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7616
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7777
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7915
msgid "Scratch Cat"
msgstr "Chadégout"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7461
msgid ""
"Meowth withdraw their sharp claws into\\ntheir paws to silently sneak "
"about.\\nFor some reason, this Pokémon loves\\nshiny coins that glitter with"
" light."
msgstr ""
"Miaouss peut rentrer ses griffes dans ses\\npattes pour rôder gracieusement "
"sans\\nlaisser de traces. Il raffole des pièces\\nd’or qui brillent à la "
"lumière."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7538
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7697
msgid "Classy Cat"
msgstr "Chadeville"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7541
msgid ""
"A Persian's six bold whiskers sense air\\nmovements to determine what is in "
"its\\nvicinity. It becomes docile if grabbed\\nby the whiskers."
msgstr ""
"Ses six grosses vibrisses lui permettent\\nde sentir les mouvements de l’air"
" pour\\nsavoir ce qui se trouve à proximité. Il est\\ndocile si on l’attrape"
" par les moustaches."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7606
msgid "MEOWTH-A"
msgstr "MIAOUSS-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7619
msgid ""
"It's accustomed to luxury because it used\\nto live with Alolan royalty. "
"Highly smart\\nand proud, it's famously difficult to\\nhandle, but that also"
" makes it popular."
msgstr ""
"Miaouss peut rentrer ses griffes dans ses\\npattes pour rôder gracieusement "
"sans\\nlaisser de traces. Il raffole des pièces\\nd’or qui brillent à la "
"lumière."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7687
msgid "PERSIAN-A"
msgstr "PERSIAN-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7700
msgid ""
"It looks down on everyone other than\\nitself. In contrast to its lovely "
"face, it\\nis so brutal that it tortures its weakened\\nprey rather than "
"finishing them off."
msgstr ""
"Ses six grosses vibrisses lui permettent\\nde sentir les mouvements de l’air"
" pour\\nsavoir ce qui se trouve à proximité. Il est\\ndocile si on l’attrape"
" par les moustaches."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7767
msgid "MEOWTH-G"
msgstr "MIAOUSS-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7780
msgid ""
"Living with a savage, seafaring people has\\nhardened its body so much that "
"parts of it\\nturned to iron. Darker coins are harder\\nand garner more "
"respect among Meowth."
msgstr ""
"Sa vie parmi de féroces marins a tant durci\\nson corps qu’il s’est changé "
"en fer par\\nendroits. Plus sa pièce est sombre, plus il\\nest respecté."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7847
msgid "PERRSERKER"
msgstr "BERSERKATT"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7850
msgid "Viking"
msgstr "Viking"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7853
msgid ""
"What appears to be an iron helmet is\\nactually hardened hair. This "
"Pokémon\\nlives for the thrill of battle."
msgstr ""
"La fourrure sur sa tête s’est endurcie et a\\npris la forme d’un casque en "
"fer. Il est\\ntrès bagarreur."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7918
msgid ""
"The pattern that has appeared on\\nits giant coin is thought to be the\\nkey"
" to unlocking the secrets of the\\nDynamax phenomenon."
msgstr ""
"On pense que le motif apparu sur sa\\npièce géante est la clé des "
"secrets\\ndu phénomène Dynamax."

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7977
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8048
msgid "Duck"
msgstr "Canard"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:7980
msgid ""
"When its headache intensifies, it starts\\nusing strange powers. However, it"
" has no\\nrecollection of its powers, so it always\\nlooks befuddled and "
"bewildered."
msgstr ""
"Il utilise des pouvoirs étranges quand ses\\nmaux de tête s’intensifient. Il"
" n’en garde\\ncependant aucun souvenir et a toujours\\nl’air confus et "
"désorienté."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8051
msgid ""
"A Golduck is an adept swimmer.\\nIt sometimes joins competitive "
"swimmers\\nin training. It uses psychic powers when\\nits forehead shimmers "
"with light."
msgstr ""
"Il nage si bien qu’il rejoint souvent des\\nnageurs professionnels à "
"l’entraînement.\\nIl utilise ses pouvoirs psychiques quand\\nla lumière sur "
"son front s’allume."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8120
msgid "MANKEY"
msgstr "FEROSINGE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8123
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8201
msgid "Pig Monkey"
msgstr "Porsinge"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8126
msgid ""
"When it starts shaking and its nasal\\nbreathing turns rough, it's a sure "
"sign\\nof anger. However, since this happens\\ninstantly, there is no time "
"to flee."
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu’il commence à trembler et que sa\\nrespiration devient haletante, "
"cela veut\\ndire qu’il est en colère. Il s’énerve si vite\\nqu’il est "
"impossible de lui échapper."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8204
msgid ""
"When it becomes furious, its blood\\ncirculation becomes more robust, "
"and\\nits muscles are made stronger. But it\\nalso becomes much less "
"intelligent."
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu’il est furieux, sa circulation\\nsanguine s’accélère. Du coup, ses "
"muscles\\nsont encore plus puissants. En revanche, il\\ndevient bien moins "
"intelligent."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4066
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8274
msgid "ANNIHILAPE"
msgstr "COURROUSINGE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8277
msgid "Rage Monkey"
msgstr "Singe Furax"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8280
msgid ""
"When its anger rose beyond a\\ncritical point, this Pokémon gained "
"power\\nthat is unfettered by the limits of\\nits physical body."
msgstr ""
"Quand sa colère a dépassé un seuil\\ncritique, ce Pokémon a obtenu "
"une\\npuissance affranchie des limites\\nde son corps."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2105
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8340
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8486
msgid "GROWLITHE"
msgstr "CANINOS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8343
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1041
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:2080
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:2144
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:2049
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_9_families.h:1460
msgid "Puppy"
msgstr "Chiot"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8346
msgid ""
"Its superb sense of smell ensures that\\nthis Pokémon won't forget any "
"scent,\\nno matter what. It uses its sense of smell\\nto detect the emotions"
" of others."
msgstr ""
"Caninos a un odorat très développé qui lui\\npermet de ne jamais oublier un "
"parfum. Il\\nutilise son puissant sens olfactif pour\\ndeviner les émotions "
"des autres."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8417
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8574
msgid "Legendary"
msgstr "Légendaire"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8420
msgid ""
"This fleet-footed Pokémon is said to run\\nover 6,200 miles in a single day "
"and night.\\nThe fire that blazes wildly within its body\\nis its source of "
"power."
msgstr ""
"Arcanin serait capable de parcourir\\nplus de 10 000 km en 24 h. Le feu "
"qui\\nbrûle à l’intérieur de son corps est la\\nsource de son pouvoir."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8484
msgid "GROWLITHE-H"
msgstr "CANINOS-H"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8494
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:897
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:900
msgid "Scout"
msgstr "Espion"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8497
msgid ""
"They patrol their territory in pairs.\\nIt's believed the igneous rock "
"components\\nin the fur of this species are the result\\nof volcanic "
"activity in its habitat."
msgstr ""
"Ils patrouillent sur leur territoire par\\npaires. Les roches volcaniques de"
" leur\\npelage seraient dues à l’activité des\\nvolcans de leur habitat."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8564
msgid "ARCANINE-H"
msgstr "ARCANIN-H"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8577
msgid ""
"Snaps at its foes with fangs cloaked in\\nblazing flame. Despite its bulk, "
"it deftly\\nfeints every which way, leading opponents\\non a deceptively "
"merry chase."
msgstr ""
"Il mord ses ennemis de ses crocs nimbés de\\nflammes. Malgré sa carrure, il "
"feinte avec\\nagilité et mène ses adversaires en bateau."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8648
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8719
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8805
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3302
msgid "Tadpole"
msgstr "Têtard"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8651
msgid ""
"It is possible to see this Pokémon's spiral\\ninnards right through its thin"
" skin.\\nHowever, the skin is also very flexible.\\nEven sharp fangs bounce "
"right off it."
msgstr ""
"Ptitard a une peau si fine qu’on peut voir\\nses entrailles en spirale à "
"travers. Sa\\npeau est aussi très élastique. Même des\\ncrocs très acérés "
"rebondissent dessus."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8716
msgid "POLIWHIRL"
msgstr "TETARTE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8722
msgid ""
"Its body surface is always wet and slick\\nwith an oily fluid. Because of "
"this greasy\\ncovering, it can easily slip and slide out\\nof the clutches "
"of any enemy in battle."
msgstr ""
"Sa peau est lubrifièe par un liquide\\nhuileux. Grâce à cette "
"protection\\ngraisseuse, il peut facilement se glisser\\nhors de l’étreinte "
"de n’importe quel ennemi."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8808
msgid ""
"Its highly developed muscles never grow\\nfatigued, however much it "
"exercises.\\nThis Pokémon can swim back and forth\\nacross the Pacific Ocean"
" without effort."
msgstr ""
"Ses muscles solides et surdéveloppés ne\\nse fatiguent jamais, quels que "
"soient ses\\nefforts. Il peut traverser les océans les\\nplus grands avec "
"une étonnante facilité."

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8880
msgid "Frog"
msgstr "Grenouille"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8883
msgid ""
"The curled hair on its head proves its\\nstatus as a king. It is said that "
"the\\nlonger and curlier the hair, the more\\nrespect it earns from its "
"peers."
msgstr ""
"Le cheveu bouclé sur la tête de TARPAUD\\nest la preuve de son statut de "
"roi. On dit\\nque plus son cheveu est long et bouclé,\\nplus il est respecté"
" par ses semblables."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8971
msgid "ABRA"
msgstr "ABRA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8974
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9047
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9146
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9240
msgid "Psi"
msgstr "Psy"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:8977
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that sleeps 18 hours a day.\\nObservation revealed that it "
"uses\\nTeleport to change its location once\\nevery hour."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon dort 18 heures par jour. Des\\nétudes ont révélé qu’il utilise "
"Téléport\\npour changer de lieu toutes les heures."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9044
msgid "KADABRA"
msgstr "KADABRA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9050
msgid ""
"It is rumored that a boy with psychic\\nabilities suddenly transformed "
"into\\nKadabra while he was assisting research\\ninto extrasensory powers."
msgstr ""
"On dit que Kadabra était jadis un garçon.\\nSes pouvoirs psychiques "
"l’auraient fait se\\ntransformer alors qu’il participait à des\\nexpériences"
" extrasensorielles."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9149
msgid ""
"While it has strong psychic abilities and\\nhigh intelligence, an Alakazam's"
" muscles\\nare very weak. It uses psychic power to\\nmove its body."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon est doté de pouvoirs\\npsychiques et d’une grande "
"intelligence\\nqui compensent sa faiblesse physique.\\nIl utilise ses "
"pouvoirs pour se déplacer."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9243
msgid ""
"Having traded away its muscles, Alakazam's\\ntrue power has been unleashed. "
"With its\\npsychic powers, it can foresee all things."
msgstr ""
"Ayant troqué ses muscles, ALAKAZAM libère\\nson vrai pouvoir. Ses dons "
"psychiques lui\\npermettent de tout prévoir."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:741
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5252
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9320
msgid "MACHOP"
msgstr "MACHOC"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Colosse
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9323
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9400
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9482
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9561
msgid "Superpower"
msgstr "Surpuissance"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9326
msgid ""
"It continually undertakes strenuous\\ntraining to master all forms of "
"martial\\narts. Its strength lets it easily hoist\\na sumo wrestler onto its"
" shoulders."
msgstr ""
"Il s’entraîne sans cesse pour maîtriser\\ntoutes les formes d’arts martiaux."
" Il est\\nsi fort qu’il peut facilement porter un\\nlutteur de sumo sur ses "
"épaules."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5087
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9397
msgid "MACHOKE"
msgstr "MACHOPEUR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9403
msgid ""
"A belt is worn by a Machoke to keep its\\noverwhelming power under "
"control.\\nBecause it is so dangerous, no one has\\never removed the belt."
msgstr ""
"La ceinture de Machopeur lui sert à\\nmaintenir sa puissance phénoménale "
"sous\\ncontrôle. Par peur du danger, personne n’a\\njamais osé lui enlever."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9485
msgid ""
"It is impossible to defend against punches\\nand chops doled out by its four"
" arms.\\nIts fighting spirit flares up when it faces\\na tough opponent."
msgstr ""
"Il est impossible d’esquiver les prises et\\nles coups de poing de ses "
"quatre bras.\\nSon esprit de combattant s’enflamme quand\\nil rencontre un "
"adversaire à la hauteur."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9564
msgid ""
"One of these Pokémon once used\\nits immeasurable strength to lift a\\nlarge"
" ship that was in trouble. It\\nthen carried the ship to port."
msgstr ""
"L’un de ces Pokémon a un jour soulevé,\\nde sa force prodigieuse, un "
"grand\\lnavire en détresse, puis l’a porté\\ljusqu’au port."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9619
msgid "BELLSPROUT"
msgstr "CHETIFLOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9625
msgid ""
"A Bellsprout's thin and flexible body lets\\nit bend and sway to avoid any "
"attack,\\nhowever strong it may be. From its mouth,\\nit leaks a fluid that "
"melts even iron."
msgstr ""
"Son corps long et flexible lui permet de se\\ntordre et d’osciller pour "
"éviter tout type\\nd’attaque. Il crache un fluide corrosif qui\\npeut même "
"dissoudre le fer."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9689
msgid "WEEPINBELL"
msgstr "BOUSTIFLOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9692
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9782
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9861
msgid "Flycatcher"
msgstr "Carnivore"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9695
msgid ""
"At night, a Weepinbell hangs on to a tree\\nbranch with its hooked rear and "
"sleeps.\\nIf it moves around in its sleep, it may\\nwake up to find itself "
"on the ground."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon est doté d’un gros crochet.\\nLa nuit, il s’accroche à une "
"branche pour\\ns’endormir. Quand il a un sommeil agité,\\nil se réveille par"
" terre."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9785
msgid ""
"The long vine extending from its head is\\nwaved about as if it were a "
"living thing to\\nattract prey. When an unsuspecting victim\\napproaches, it"
" is swallowed whole."
msgstr ""
"Empiflor est doté d’une longue liane\\nqui part de sa tête. Elle se balance "
"et\\nremue comme un animal pour attirer\\nses proies. Les imprudents sont "
"avalés."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9864
msgid ""
"The volume of this Pokémon's acid\\nhas increased due to Mega "
"Evolution,\\nfilling its mouth. If not careful,\\nthe acid will overflow and"
" spill out."
msgstr ""
"Le volume d’acide de ce Pokémon a\\naugmenté avec la Méga-Évolution "
"et\\nemplit sa bouche. S’il ne fait pas\\nattention, l’acide déborde."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9916
msgid "TENTACOOL"
msgstr "TENTACOOL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9919
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9993
msgid "Jellyfish"
msgstr "Mollusque"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9922
msgid ""
"Its body is almost entirely composed of\\nwater. It ensnares its foe with "
"its two\\nlong tentacles, then stabs with the poison\\nstingers at their "
"tips."
msgstr ""
"Son corps est presque entièrement\\ncomposé d’eau. Il enlace ses "
"adversaires\\nde ses deux longs tentacules avant de\\nleur injecter du "
"poison."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:9996
msgid ""
"It lives in complex rock formations on\\nthe ocean floor and traps prey "
"using its\\n80 tentacles. Its red orbs glow when it\\ngrows excited or "
"agitated."
msgstr ""
"Il vit dans les formations rocheuses au\\nfond de l’océan et traque ses "
"proies avec\\nses 80 tentacules. Ses globes rouges\\nbrillent quand il "
"s’énerve ou s’agite."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10070
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10298
msgid "GEODUDE"
msgstr "RACAILLOU"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10073
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10145
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10306
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10388
msgid "Rock"
msgstr "ROCHE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10076
msgid ""
"It climbs mountain paths using only the\\npower of its arms. Because they "
"look just\\nlike boulders lining paths, hikers may step\\non them without "
"noticing."
msgstr ""
"Il grimpe les chemins de montagne à la\\nseule force de ses bras. Il se fait"
" souvent\\npiétiner par les promeneurs qui le\\nprennent pour un vulgaire "
"rocher."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10142
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10380
msgid "GRAVELER"
msgstr "GRAVALANCH"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10148
msgid ""
"They descend from mountains by tumbling\\ndown steep slopes. They are so "
"brutal,\\nthey smash aside obstructing trees and\\nmassive boulders with "
"thunderous tackles."
msgstr ""
"Il descend de la montagne en dévalant\\nles pentes abruptes. Il est si "
"violent\\nqu’il détruit les arbres et les rochers\\nse trouvant sur son "
"chemin."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10226
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10469
msgid "Megaton"
msgstr "Titanesque"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10229
msgid ""
"It is said to live in volcanic craters\\non mountain peaks. Once a year, it "
"sheds\\nits hide and grows larger. The shed hide\\ncrumbles and returns to "
"the soil."
msgstr ""
"On dit qu’il vit dans les cratères des\\nvolcans. Il mue une fois par an "
"pour\\ngrandir. Sa mue se désagrège alors\\net retourne à la terre."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10296
msgid "GEODUDE-A"
msgstr "RACAILLOU-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10309
msgid ""
"Its body is a magnetic stone. Iron sand\\nattach to parts of its body with "
"stronger\\nmagnetism. If you carelessly step on one,\\nit will headbutt and "
"shock you in anger."
msgstr ""
"Il grimpe les chemins de montagne à la\\nseule force de ses bras. Il se fait"
" souvent\\npiétiner par les promeneurs qui le\\nprennent pour un vulgaire "
"rocher."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10378
msgid "GRAVELER-A"
msgstr "GRAVALANCH-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10391
msgid ""
"When two Graveler smash each other over\\ndravite, their favorite food, they"
" cause\\nflashes of light and booming noises.\\nPeople call them “fireworks "
"of the earth.”"
msgstr ""
"Il descend de la montagne en dévalant\\nles pentes abruptes. Il est si "
"violent\\nqu’il détruit les arbres et les rochers\\nse trouvant sur son "
"chemin."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10459
msgid "GOLEM-A"
msgstr "GROLEM-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10472
msgid ""
"It fires rocks charged with electricity.\\nEven if the rock isn't fired "
"that\\naccurately, just grazing an opponent\\nwill cause numbness and "
"fainting."
msgstr ""
"On dit qu’il vit dans les cratères des\\nvolcans. Il mue une fois par an "
"pour\\ngrandir. Sa mue se désagrège alors\\net retourne à la terre."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: data/maps/Route25_BillsHouse_hns/scripts.inc:322
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10539
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10681
msgid "PONYTA"
msgstr "PONYTA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10542
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10612
msgid "Fire Horse"
msgstr "Cheval Feu"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10545
msgid ""
"A Ponyta is very weak at birth. It can\\nbarely stand up. Its legs become "
"stronger\\nas it stumbles and falls while trying to\\nkeep up with its "
"parent."
msgstr ""
"A sa naissance, Ponyta est très faible\\net peut à peine tenir debout. Il se"
" muscle\\nen trébuchant et en tombant, lorsqu’il\\nessaye de suivre ses "
"parents."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10615
msgid ""
"It usually canters casually in the fields\\nand plains. But once a Rapidash "
"turns\\nserious, its fiery manes flare and blaze\\nas it gallops its way up "
"to 150 mph."
msgstr ""
"On voit souvent Galopa trotter dans les\\nchamps et les plaines. Ce Pokémon "
"peut\\ngaloper à plus de 240 km/h et sa crinière\\nflamboyante s’embrase."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10679
msgid "PONYTA-G"
msgstr "PONYTA-G"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10689
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10769
msgid "Unique Horn"
msgstr "Unicorne"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10692
msgid ""
"Its small horn hides a healing power.\\nThis Pokémon will look into your "
"eyes and\\nread the contents of your heart. If it\\nfinds evil there, it "
"promptly hides away."
msgstr ""
"Sa petite corne recèle un pouvoir de\\nguérison. Il lit dans le cœur des "
"gens en\\nles fixant dans les yeux. S’il y voit le mal,\\nil se cache "
"aussitôt."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10759
msgid "RAPIDASH-G"
msgstr "GALOPA-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10772
msgid ""
"Little can stand up to its psycho cut.\\nUnleashed from this Pokémon's "
"horn,\\nthe move will punch a hole right\\nthrough a thick metal sheet."
msgstr ""
"Rien ne résiste à sa Coupe Psycho. Lancée\\ndepuis sa corne, elle perce une "
"épaisse\\nplaque de métal de part en part."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10843
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11139
msgid "Dopey"
msgstr "Crétin"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10846
msgid ""
"It catches prey by dipping its tail in\\nwater at the side of a river. But "
"it often\\nforgets what it is doing and spends entire\\ndays just loafing at"
" water's edge."
msgstr ""
"Ramoloss trempe sa queue dans l’eau au\\nbord des rivières pour attraper ses"
" proies.\\nIl oublie souvent ce qu’il fait là et passe\\ndes jours entiers à"
" traîner."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10919
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11060
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11225
msgid "Hermit Crab"
msgstr "Symbiose"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10922
msgid ""
"Its tail has a Shellder firmly attached\\nwith a bite. As a result, the tail"
" can't be\\nused for fishing anymore. This forces it\\nto reluctantly swim "
"and catch prey."
msgstr ""
"Flagadoss a un Kokiyas solidement\\nattaché à sa queue. Du coup, il ne "
"peut\\nplus l’utiliser pour pêcher et est donc\\nobligé de nager pour "
"attraper ses proies."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10989
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1849
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1937
msgid "Royal"
msgstr "Royal"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:10992
msgid ""
"It undertakes research every day to\\nsolve the mysteries of the "
"world.\\nHowever, it apparently forgets everything\\nif the Shellder on its "
"head comes off."
msgstr ""
"Tous les jours, Roigada entreprend des\\nrecherches pour résoudre les "
"mystères du\\nmonde. Cependant, il oublie tout si le\\nKokiyas qui se trouve"
" sur sa tête s’en va."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11063
msgid ""
"When bathed in the energy of Mega\\nEvolution, Shellder converts "
"into\\nimpregnable armor. There is virtually no\\nchange in Slowpoke."
msgstr ""
"Baigné dans l’énergie de la\\nMéga-Évolution, KOKIYAS se change en\\narmure "
"imprenable. RAMOLOSS, lui, ne\\nchange presque pas."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11129
msgid "SLOWPOKE-G"
msgstr "RAMOLOSS-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11142
msgid ""
"Although it is normally zoned out, its\\nexpression abruptly sharpens on "
"occasion.\\nThe cause seems to lie in Slowpoke's diet,\\nwhich also give "
"their tails a spicy flavor."
msgstr ""
"D’ordinaire dans la lune, il prend parfois un\\nair vif. Cela viendrait du "
"régime de\\nRamoloss, qui rend aussi sa queue épicée."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11215
msgid "SLOWBRO-G"
msgstr "FLAGADOSS-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11228
msgid ""
"A Shellder bite set off a chemical reaction\\nwith the spices inside "
"Slowbro's body,\\ncausing Slowbro to become a\\nPoison-type Pokémon."
msgstr ""
"La morsure d’un Kokiyas a provoqué une\\nréaction chimique avec les épices "
"du corps\\nde Flagadoss, qui est devenu de type\\nPoison."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11294
msgid "SLOWKING-G"
msgstr "ROIGADA-G"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11304
msgid "Hexpert"
msgstr "Sorcier"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11307
msgid ""
"A combination of toxins and the shock of\\nevolving has increased "
"Shellder's\\nintelligence to the point that Shellder\\nnow controls "
"Slowking."
msgstr ""
"Un mélange de toxines et le choc de\\nl’évolution ont tant accru "
"l’intelligence de\\nKokiyas qu’il contrôle désormais Roigada."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2237
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6727
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11378
msgid "MAGNEMITE"
msgstr "MAGNETI"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Magnétique
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11381
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11453
msgid "Magnet"
msgstr "Aimant"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11384
msgid ""
"The units at its sides are extremely\\npowerful magnets. They generate "
"enough\\nmagnetism to draw in iron objects from\\nover 300 feet away."
msgstr ""
"Ses extrémités sont des aimants très\\npuissants. Ils génèrent assez "
"d’énergie\\npour attirer des objets métalliques\\nse trouvant dans un rayon "
"de 100 mètres."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11456
msgid ""
"It is actually three Magnemite linked\\nby magnetism. It generates powerful "
"radio\\nwaves that raise temperatures by 3.6\\ndegrees F within a 3,300-foot"
" radius."
msgstr ""
"Il est composé de trois Magneti reliés\\nentre eux par magnétisme. Ses ondes"
" radio\\naugmentent la température de 2 degrés\\ndans un rayon d’un "
"kilomètre."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11535
msgid "MAGNEZONE"
msgstr "MAGNEZONE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11538
msgid "Magnet Area"
msgstr "Aimant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11541
msgid ""
"As it zooms through the sky, this\\nPokémon seems to be receiving "
"signals\\nof unknown origin, while transmitting its\\nown signals of unknown"
" purpose."
msgstr ""
"On raconte qu’il serait contrôlé par une\\nentité extraterrestre grâce à des"
" ondes\\nqu’il capterait avec l’antenne sur sa\\ntête."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11619
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11711
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11786
msgid "Wild Duck"
msgstr "Canard Fou"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11622
msgid ""
"It is always seen with a stick from a plant.\\nApparently, there are good "
"sticks and bad\\nsticks. This Pokémon occasionally fights\\nwith others over"
" choice sticks."
msgstr ""
"On le voit tout le temps avec une tige,\\nrécupérée sur une plante "
"quelconque.\\nIl y a des bonnes et des mauvaises tiges.\\nElles peuvent "
"faire l’objet de disputes."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11701
msgid "FARFETCH'D-G"
msgstr "CANARTICHO-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11714
msgid ""
"The stalks of leeks are thicker and longer\\nin the Galar region. Brave "
"Farfetch'd\\nwarriors that adapted to these stalks\\ntook on a unique form."
msgstr ""
"À Galar, les tiges de poireau sont plus\\nlongues et plus épaisses. Les "
"Canarticho\\nguerriers qui s’y sont adaptés ont pris une\\nforme unique."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11783
msgid "SIRFETCH'D"
msgstr "PALARTICHO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11789
msgid ""
"Only Farfetch'd that have survived many\\nbattles can attain this evolution."
" When\\nthis Pokémon's leek withers, it will\\nretire from combat."
msgstr ""
"Seuls les Canarticho ayant survécu à de\\nnombreux combats atteignent ce "
"stade. Si\\nson poireau se flétrit, il se retire du\\nchamp de bataille."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11850
msgid "DODUO"
msgstr "DODUO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11853
msgid "Twin Bird"
msgstr "Duoiseau"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11856
msgid ""
"Even while eating or sleeping, one of the\\nheads remains always vigilant "
"for any sign\\nof danger. When threatened, it flees at\\nover 60 miles per "
"hour."
msgstr ""
"Même en dormant ou en mangeant, une de\\nses têtes est toujours en train de "
"monter\\nla garde. S’il se sent menacé, il est\\ncapable de courir à 100 "
"km/h."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5491
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11943
msgid "DODRIO"
msgstr "DODRIO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11946
msgid "Triple Bird"
msgstr "Trioiseau"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:11949
msgid ""
"A peculiar Pokémon species with three\\nheads. It vigorously races across "
"grassy\\nplains even in arid seasons with little\\nrainfall."
msgstr ""
"Quand une des têtes de Doduo se divise, il\\ndevient un Dodrio capable de "
"courir à\\n60 km/h."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12034
msgid "SEEL"
msgstr "OTARIA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12037
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12111
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:513
msgid "Sea Lion"
msgstr "Otarie"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12040
msgid ""
"Seel hunt for prey in frigid, ice-covered\\nseas. When it needs to breathe, "
"it punches\\na hole through the ice with the sharply\\nprotruding section of"
" its head."
msgstr ""
"Otaria chasse ses proies dans l’eau gelée,\\nsous la couche de glace. "
"Lorsqu’il cherche\\nà respirer, il perce un trou en frappant la\\nglace avec"
" la partie saillante de sa tête."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12114
msgid ""
"It loves to snooze on bitterly cold ice.\\nThe sight of this Pokémon "
"sleeping on\\na glacier was mistakenly thought to be\\na mermaid by a "
"mariner long ago."
msgstr ""
"Lamantine adore piquer un roupillon à même\\nla glace. Il y a très "
"longtemps, un marin\\nayant aperçu ce Pokémon dormant sur\\nun glacier a cru"
" voir une sirène."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12178
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12328
msgid "GRIMER"
msgstr "TADMORV"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Dégueu
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12181
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12255
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12336
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12419
msgid "Sludge"
msgstr "Détritus"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12184
msgid ""
"Born from polluted sludge in the sea,\\nGrimer's favorite food is anything "
"filthy.\\nThey feed on wastewater pumped out from\\nfactories."
msgstr ""
"Né de la pollution des océans, Tadmorv\\nadore se nourrir de tout ce qui "
"est\\ncrasseux. On en voit souvent en train\\nd’avaler les eaux usées des "
"usines."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12258
msgid ""
"It prefers warm and humid habitats.\\nIn the summertime, the toxic "
"substances\\nin its body intensify, making Muk reek like\\nputrid kitchen "
"garbage."
msgstr ""
"Il préfère les habitats chauds et humides.\\nEn été, les substances toxiques"
" de son\\ncorps se développent et le font\\nressembler à un véritable tas "
"d’ordures."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12326
msgid "GRIMER-A"
msgstr "TADMORV-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12339
msgid ""
"There are a hundred or so of them living\\nin Alola's waste-disposal site. "
"They're all\\nhard workers who eat a lot of trash. Grimer\\nseems to relish "
"any and all kinds of trash."
msgstr ""
"Né de la pollution des océans, Tadmorv\\nadore se nourrir de tout ce qui "
"est\\ncrasseux. On en voit souvent en train\\nd’avaler les eaux usées des "
"usines."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12409
msgid "MUK-A"
msgstr "GROTADMORV-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12422
msgid ""
"While it's unexpectedly quiet and friendly,\\nif it's not fed any trash for "
"a while,,\\nit will smash its Trainer's furnishings,\\nand eat up the "
"fragments."
msgstr ""
"Il préfère les habitats chauds et humides.\\nEn été, les substances toxiques"
" de son\\ncorps se développent et le font\\nressembler à un véritable tas "
"d’ordures."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12495
msgid "SHELLDER"
msgstr "KOKIYAS"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12498
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12575
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11282
msgid "Bivalve"
msgstr "Bivalve"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12501
msgid ""
"At night, it burrows a hole in the seafloor\\nwith its broad tongue to make "
"a place to\\nsleep. While asleep, it closes its shell,\\nbut leaves its "
"tongue hanging out."
msgstr ""
"La nuit, KOKIYAS utilise sa grande langue\\npour creuser un trou dans les "
"fonds marins\\net y dormir. Une fois endormi, il referme sa\\ncoquille mais "
"laisse sa langue dépasser."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12578
msgid ""
"It swims in the sea by swallowing water,\\nthen jetting it out toward the "
"rear.\\nThe Cloyster shoots spikes from its\\nshell using the same system."
msgstr ""
"Crustabri est capable de se déplacer dans\\nles fonds marins en avalant de "
"l’eau et en\\nla rejetant vers l’arrière. Il envoie des\\npointes en "
"utilisant la même méthode."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12642
msgid "GASTLY"
msgstr "FANTOMINUS"

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main (le patch FR actuel donnait un morceau
#. d’un autre texte)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12645
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12719
msgid "Gas"
msgstr "Gaz"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12648
msgid ""
"When exposed to a strong wind, a Gastly's\\ngaseous body quickly dwindles "
"away.\\nThey cluster under the eaves of houses\\nto escape the ravages of "
"wind."
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu’il est exposé au vent, le corps\\ngazeux de Fantominus rapetisse et "
"se\\ndisperse. Ces Pokémon se rassemblent sous\\nles auvents des maisons "
"pour se protéger."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12722
msgid ""
"If a Haunter beckons you while it is\\nfloating in darkness, don't approach "
"it.\\nThis Pokémon will try to lick you with its\\ntongue and steal your "
"life away."
msgstr ""
"Spectrum est un Pokémon dangereux. Si\\nl’un d’entre eux fait signe "
"d’approcher, il\\nne faut pas l’écouter. Il risque de sortir\\nsa langue "
"pour essayer de voler votre vie."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12808
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12884
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12955
msgid "Shadow"
msgstr "Ombre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12811
msgid ""
"Deep in the night, your shadow cast by\\na streetlight may suddenly overtake"
" you.\\nIt is actually a Gengar running past\\nyou, pretending to be your "
"shadow."
msgstr ""
"Parfois, pendant les nuits noires, une\\nombre projetée par un réverbère "
"peut vous\\ndépasser. C’est un Ectoplasma qui court\\nen se faisant passer "
"pour votre ombre."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12887
msgid ""
"Gengar's relationships are warped. It\\ntries to take the lives of anyone "
"and\\neveryone. It will even try to curse the\\nTrainer who is its master!"
msgstr ""
"Les relations d’ECTOPLASMA sont\\nperverties. Il veut ôter la vie à "
"tout\\lle monde. Il tente même de maudire son\\lpropre Dresseur!"

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:12958
msgid ""
"Rumor has it that its gigantic\\nmouth leads not into its body, "
"filled\\nwith cursed energy, but instead\\ndirectly to the afterlife."
msgstr ""
"La rumeur dit que sa bouche géante ne\\nmène pas à son corps empli "
"d’énergie\\nmaudite, mais directement dans\\nl’au-delà."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13013
msgid "ONIX"
msgstr "ONIX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13016
msgid "Rock Snake"
msgstr "Serpenroc"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13019
msgid ""
"There is a magnet in its brain that\\nprevents an Onix from losing "
"direction\\nwhile tunneling. As it grows older, its body\\nbecomes steadily "
"rounder and smoother."
msgstr ""
"Onix a dans le cerveau un aimant qui lui\\nsert de boussole. Cela lui permet"
" de ne pas\\nse perdre pendant qu’il creuse. En prenant\\nde l’âge, son "
"corps s’arrondit et se polit."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13089
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13180
msgid "Iron Snake"
msgstr "Serpenfer"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13092
msgid ""
"Steelix live even further underground\\nthan Onix. This Pokémon is known to "
"dig\\ntoward the earth's core, reaching a depth\\nof over six-tenths of a "
"mile underground."
msgstr ""
"Il vit sous terre, encore plus profon-\\ndément qu’Onix. On dit qu’il creuse"
" vers le\\ncentre de la terre. On l’a déjà vu aller à\\nplus d’un kilomètre "
"de profondeur."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13183
msgid ""
"The cells within its body, crystallized by\\nthe energy produced from Mega "
"Evolution,\\nare stronger than any mineral and able\\nto withstand any "
"temperature."
msgstr ""
"Les cellules de son corps, cristallisées\\npar l’énergie de la Méga-"
"Évolution, sont\\nplus solides que tout minéral et\\nrésistent à toutes les "
"températures."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13254
msgid "DROWZEE"
msgstr "SOPORIFIK"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13257
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13334
msgid "Hypnosis"
msgstr "Hypnose"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13260
msgid ""
"If your nose becomes itchy while you are\\nsleeping, it's a sure sign that a"
" Drowzee is\\nstanding above your pillow and trying to\\neat your dream "
"through your nostrils."
msgstr ""
"Si jamais votre nez vous démange en\\ndormant, c’est sans doute que "
"ce\\nPokémon se tient au-dessus de vous\\npour manger vos rêves par les "
"narines."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13337
msgid ""
"The arcing movement and glitter of the\\npendulum in a Hypno's hand lull the"
" foe\\ninto deep hypnosis. While searching for\\nprey, it polishes the "
"pendulum."
msgstr ""
"Le mouvement de balancier et les reflets\\nbrillants de son pendule "
"hypnotisent\\nprofondément son ennemi. Lorsqu’il\\ncherche ses proies, il "
"nettoie son pendule."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13418
msgid "KRABBY"
msgstr "KRABBY"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13421
msgid "River Crab"
msgstr "Doux Crabe"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13424
msgid ""
"Krabby live in holes dug into beaches.\\nOn sandy shores with little in the "
"way\\nof food, they can be seen squabbling with\\neach other over territory."
msgstr ""
"Krabby vit sur les plages, enterré dans le\\nsable. Sur les plages où l’on "
"trouve peu de\\nnourriture, on peut voir ces Pokémon se\\ndisputer pour "
"défendre leur territoire."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13494
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13565
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17024
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17109
msgid "Pincer"
msgstr "Pince"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13497
msgid ""
"It waves its huge, oversized claw in the\\nair to communicate with "
"others.\\nBut since the claw is so heavy, this\\nPokémon quickly tires."
msgstr ""
"Il est doté d’une pince gigantesque,\\nsurdimensionnée. Il l’agite en l’air "
"pour\\ncommuniquer avec ses semblables. Sa\\npince est si lourde qu’il se "
"fatigue vite."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13568
msgid ""
"The flow of Gigantamax energy has\\nspurred this Pokémon's left pincer\\nto "
"grow to an enormous size. That\\nclaw can pulverize anything."
msgstr ""
"Le flux d’énergie Gigamax a fait\\ngrandir démesurément la pince gauche\\nde"
" ce Pokémon. Elle peut tout\\npulvériser."

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13626
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13704
msgid "Ball"
msgstr "Balle"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13629
msgid ""
"It bears an uncanny and unexplained\\nresemblance to a Poké Ball. Because "
"it\\nexplodes at the slightest shock, even\\nveteran Trainers treat it with "
"caution."
msgstr ""
"Nul ne sait d’où vient sa ressemblance\\navec une Poké Ball. Comme "
"il\\nexplose au moindre choc, les Dresseurs\\nle manipulent avec précaution."

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13707
msgid ""
"They appear in great numbers at electric\\npower plants. Because they feed "
"on\\nelectricity, they cause massive and\\nchaotic blackouts in nearby "
"cities."
msgstr ""
"Ils apparaissent en grand nombre près\\ndes centrales électriques. Comme "
"ils\\nse nourrissent d’électricité, ils causent\\nd’énormes pannes dans les "
"villes voisines."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13773
msgid "VOLTORB-H"
msgstr "VOLTORBE-H"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13783
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13862
msgid "Sphere"
msgstr "Sphère"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13786
msgid ""
"It resembles an ancient Poké Ball design.\\nWhen excited, it discharges the "
"electric\\ncurrent it has stored in its belly, then\\nlets out a great, "
"uproarious laugh."
msgstr ""
"Il ressemble à une Poké Ball d’antan.\\nExcité, il libère le courant stocké "
"dans son\\nventre, puis part d’un grand éclat de rire\\ntonitruant."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13852
msgid "ELECTRODE-H"
msgstr "ÉLECTRODE-H"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13865
msgid ""
"The tissue on the surface of its body is\\nsimilar in composition to an "
"Apricorn.\\nWhen irritated, it lets loose an electric\\ncurrent equal to 20 "
"lightning bolts."
msgstr ""
"Les tissus de sa surface ressemblent à\\nceux d’un Noigrume. Quand il est "
"irrité, il\\nlibère un courant électrique égal à vingt\\néclairs."

#. source : patch FR actuel (correspondance douteuse, à vérifier)
#. source : patch FR actuel (récupéré par pointeur)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13937
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15520
msgid "Egg"
msgstr "Œuf"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:13940
msgid ""
"It consists of six eggs that care for each\\nother. The eggs attract each "
"other and\\nspin around. When cracks increasingly\\nappear, it is close to "
"evolution."
msgstr ""
"Il est constitué de six œufs formant une\\ngrappe serrée qui s’attirent "
"mutuellement\\net pivotent. Des fissures apparaissent\\nquand il est sur le "
"point d’évoluer."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2668
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:9135
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14026
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14098
msgid "EXEGGUTOR"
msgstr "NOADKOKO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14029
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14106
msgid "Coconut"
msgstr "Fruitpalme"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14032
msgid ""
"Originally from the tropics, Exeggutor's\\nheads grow larger from exposure "
"to strong\\nsunlight. It is said that when the heads\\nfall, they group to "
"form an Exeggcute."
msgstr ""
"Noadkoko vient des tropiques. Grâce au\\nsoleil ardent, ses têtes ont "
"rapidement\\ngrandi. On raconte que lorsque ses têtes\\ntombent, elles "
"forment un Noeunoeuf."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14096
msgid "EXEGGUTOR-A"
msgstr "NOADKOKO-A"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14109
msgid ""
"Alola is the best environment for\\nthis Pokémon. Local people take "
"pride\\nin its appearance, saying this is how\\nExeggutor ought to look."
msgstr ""
"Noadkoko vient des tropiques. Grâce au\\nsoleil ardent, ses têtes ont "
"rapidement\\ngrandi. On raconte que lorsque ses têtes\\ntombent, elles "
"forment un Noeunoeuf."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6695
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7617
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14178
msgid "CUBONE"
msgstr "OSSELAIT"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Solitaire
#: data/scripts/debug.inc:724
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14181
msgid "Lonely"
msgstr "Solo"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14184
msgid ""
"It pines for the mother it will never see\\nagain. Seeing a likeness of its "
"mother in\\nthe full moon, it cries. The stains on the\\nskull it wears are "
"from its tears."
msgstr ""
"Sa maman lui manque terriblement et il ne la\\nreverra jamais. La lune le "
"fait pleurer, car\\nelle lui rappelle sa mère. Les taches sur\\nson crâne "
"sont les marques de ses larmes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14260
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14344
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14419
msgid "Bone Keeper"
msgstr "Gard’Os"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14263
msgid ""
"A Marowak is the evolved form of a Cubone\\nthat has grown tough by "
"overcoming the\\ngrief of losing its mother. Its tempered\\nand hardened "
"spirit is not easily broken."
msgstr ""
"Il est la forme évoluée d’Osselait. Il a\\nsurmonté le chagrin causé par la "
"perte de\\nsa maman et s’est endurci. Son tempérament\\nle rend très "
"difficile à amadouer."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14334
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14409
msgid "MAROWAK-A"
msgstr "OSSATUEUR-A"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14493
msgid "TYROGUE"
msgstr "DEBUGANT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14496
msgid "Scuffle"
msgstr "Bagarreur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14499
msgid ""
"Tyrogue become stressed out if they do\\nnot get to train every day. When "
"raising\\nthis Pokémon, the Trainer must establish\\na regular training "
"schedule."
msgstr ""
"Il devient nerveux s’il ne s’entraîne pas\\ntous les jours. Lorsqu’un "
"Dresseur élève\\nce Pokémon, il doit établir et appliquer un\\nprogramme "
"d’entraînement très complet."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14571
msgid "Kicking"
msgstr "Latteur"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14574
msgid ""
"Its legs freely stretch and contract.\\nUsing these springlike limbs, it "
"bowls over\\nfoes with devastating kicks. After battle,\\nit rubs down its "
"tired legs."
msgstr ""
"Il peut terrasser ses ennemis en les\\nrouant de coups de pied avec ses "
"jambes\\nqu’il contracte et étire à volonté. Il les\\nmasse ensuite pour les"
" reposer."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14642
msgid "Punching"
msgstr "Puncheur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14645
msgid ""
"A Hitmonchan is said to possess the\\nspirit of a boxer who aimed to become "
"the\\nworld champion. Having an indomitable\\nspirit means that it will "
"never give up."
msgstr ""
"On raconte qu’il a l’état d’esprit d’un\\nboxeur s’entraînant pour le "
"championnat\\ndu monde. Il a une ténacité à toute\\népreuve et n’abandonne "
"jamais."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14722
msgid "Handstand"
msgstr "Poirier"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14725
msgid ""
"Its technique of kicking while spinning is\\na remarkable mix of both "
"offense and\\ndefense. Hitmontop travel faster\\nspinning than they do "
"walking."
msgstr ""
"Il tournoie à toute vitesse sur sa tête\\nen donnant des coups de pied et "
"combine\\ndes attaques offensives et défensives. Il\\nva plus vite sur la "
"tête qu’en marchant."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14795
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14867
msgid "Licking"
msgstr "Lécheur"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14798
msgid ""
"Whenever it sees something unfamiliar,\\nit always licks the object because "
"it\\nmemorizes things by texture and taste.\\nIt is somewhat put off by sour"
" things."
msgstr ""
"Chaque fois qu’il découvre quelque chose\\nde nouveau, il le lèche. Sa "
"mémoire est\\nbasée sur le goût et la texture des objets.\\nIl n’aime pas "
"les choses acides."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1997
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14864
msgid "LICKILICKY"
msgstr "COUDLANGUE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14870
msgid ""
"The long tongue is always soggy with\\nslobber. The saliva contains a "
"solvent\\nthat causes numbness. Getting too close\\nto it will leave you "
"soaked with drool."
msgstr ""
"Sa langue a l’incroyable faculté de\\ns’allonger et d’atteindre plusieurs "
"fois\\nla taille de son corps. Ce mystère de la\\nnature reste entier."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14945
msgid "KOFFING"
msgstr "SMOGO"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Gaz Mortel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14948
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15030
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15112
msgid "Poison Gas"
msgstr "Gaz Toxik"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:14951
msgid ""
"Getting up close to a Koffing will give\\nyou a chance to observe, through "
"its thin\\nskin, the toxic gases swirling inside. It\\nblows up at the "
"slightest stimulation."
msgstr ""
"Il suffit de s’approcher d’un Smogo pour\\napercevoir les gaz toxiques qui "
"circulent\\ndans son corps. Il explose à la moindre\\nstimulation."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15033
msgid ""
"By diluting its toxic gases with a special\\nprocess, the highest grade of "
"perfume can\\nbe extracted. To Weezing, gases emanating\\nfrom garbage are "
"the ultimate feast."
msgstr ""
"Une technique spéciale diluant ses gaz\\ntoxiques permet d’obtenir un "
"parfum\\nformidable. Mais pour Smogogo,\\nrien ne vaut l’odeur d’une bonne "
"décharge."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15102
msgid "WEEZING-G"
msgstr "SMOGOGO-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15115
msgid ""
"Long ago, when droves of factories fouled\\nthe air with pollution, it "
"changed into this\\nform for some reason. It consumes air\\npollutant "
"particles, expelling clean air."
msgstr ""
"Jadis, quand les usines polluaient l’air, il a\\npris cette forme pour une "
"raison inconnue.\\nIl absorbe les particules polluantes et\\nrejette de "
"l’air pur."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6675
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15183
msgid "RHYHORN"
msgstr "RHINOCORNE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/battle_debug.c:401 src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15186
msgid "Spikes"
msgstr "Picots"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15189
msgid ""
"Once it starts running, it doesn't stop.\\nIts tiny brain makes it so stupid"
" that it\\ncan't remember why it started running in\\nthe first place."
msgstr ""
"Un RHINOCORNE qui commence à courir\\nne s’arrête jamais. Il est si stupide "
"qu’il\\noublie tout le temps pourquoi il a\\ncommencé à courir."

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15273
msgid ""
"Its horn, which rotates like a drill,\\ndestroys tall buildings with one "
"strike.\\nIt stands on its hind legs, and its brain\\nis well developed."
msgstr ""
"Sa corne qui pivote comme un foret est\\ncapable de détruire un immeuble "
"d’un \\nseul coup. Il se tient sur ses pattes\\narrière et son cerveau est "
"très développé."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15357
msgid "RHYPERIOR"
msgstr "RHINASTOC"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15363
msgid ""
"It can launch a rock held in its hand\\nlike a missile by tightening and "
"then\\nexpanding its muscles instantaneously.\\nGeodude are shot at rare "
"times."
msgstr ""
"Il met des rochers ou des Nodulithe\\ndans le creux de ses mains et les "
"tire\\ncomme des obus. Il peut ainsi en charger\\ntrois par bras."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15444
msgid "HAPPINY"
msgstr "PTIRAVI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15447
msgid "Playhouse"
msgstr "Maisonjouet"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15450
msgid ""
"It carries a round white rock in its\\nbelly pouch. If it gets along well "
"with\\nsomeone, it will sometimes give that\\nperson the rock."
msgstr ""
"Pour imiter Leveinard, il conserve un\\ncaillou en forme d’œuf dans sa "
"poche\\nventrale et en prend grand soin."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15523
msgid ""
"Chansey lay nutritionally excellent eggs\\nevery day. The eggs are so "
"delicious, they\\nare eagerly devoured by even those people\\nwho have lost "
"their appetite."
msgstr ""
"Leveinard pond tous les jours des œufs\\npleins de vitamines. Ces œufs "
"sont\\ntellement bons que les gens les mangent\\nmême quand ils n’ont pas "
"faim."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Bonheur
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15599
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1726
msgid "Happiness"
msgstr "JOIE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15602
msgid ""
"If it senses sadness with its fluffy fur,\\na Blissey will rush over to the "
"sad person,\\nhowever far away, to share an egg of\\nhappiness that brings a"
" smile to any face."
msgstr ""
"Leuphorie ressent la tristesse grâce à\\nson pelage duveteux. Si une "
"personne est\\ntriste, il partage avec elle un œuf rempli\\nde bonheur qui "
"fait sourire tout le monde."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7172
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15670
msgid "TANGELA"
msgstr "SAQUEDENEU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15673
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15745
msgid "Vine"
msgstr "Vigne"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15676
msgid ""
"Its vines snap off easily and painlessly\\nif they are grabbed, allowing it "
"to make a\\nquick getaway. The lost vines are replaced\\nby new growth the "
"very next day."
msgstr ""
"Ses lianes se brisent facilement lorsqu’on\\nles attrape. Cela ne lui fait "
"pas mal et lui\\npermet de s’échapper rapidement. Les\\nlianes cassées "
"repoussent le lendemain."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15742
msgid "TANGROWTH"
msgstr "BOULDENEU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15748
msgid ""
"It ensnares prey by extending arms made\\nof vines. Even if one of its arms "
"is eaten,\\nit's fine. The Pokémon regenerates quickly\\nand will go right "
"back to normal."
msgstr ""
"La science a récemment découvert que les\\ndeux bras qu’il peut allonger à "
"volonté\\nsont en fait des lianes entrelacées."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Maternel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15830
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15906
msgid "Parent"
msgstr "PARENTS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15833
msgid ""
"If you come across a young Kangaskhan\\nplaying by itself, never try to "
"catch it.\\nThe baby's parent is sure to be in the area,\\nand it will "
"become violently enraged."
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu’on rencontre un petit Kangourex\\nseul, il ne faut pas essayer de "
"l’attraper.\\nSes parents sont sûrement dans le coin et\\nrisquent d’entrer "
"dans une colère noire."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15909
msgid ""
"When the mother sees the back of her\\nMega-Evolved child, it makes her "
"think\\nof the day when her child will inevitably\\nleave her."
msgstr ""
"Quand la mère voit le dos de son petit\\nméga-évolué, elle pense au jour où "
"il la\\nquittera inévitablement."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : on Glace
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15984
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16061
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16148
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21003
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21073
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21149
msgid "Dragon"
msgstr "DRAGON"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:15987
msgid ""
"By cleverly flicking the fins on its back\\nside to side, it moves in any "
"direction\\nwhile facing forward. It spits ink to\\nescape if it senses "
"danger."
msgstr ""
"Il arrive à se déplacer en bougeant les\\nnageoires qui se trouvent sur son "
"dos.\\nIl crache de l’encre au moindre signe de\\ndanger."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16058
msgid "SEADRA"
msgstr "HYPOCEAN"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16064
msgid ""
"The poisonous barbs all over its body are\\nhighly valued as ingredients for"
" making\\ntraditional herbal medicine. It shows no\\nmercy to anything "
"approaching its nest."
msgstr ""
"Les pointes empoisonnées qui couvrent son\\ncorps entrent dans la "
"composition de\\ncertains remèdes. Il est sans merci\\npour ceux qui "
"s’approchent de son nid."

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16151
msgid ""
"It sleeps quietly, deep on the seafloor.\\nWhen it comes up to the surface, "
"it\\ncreates a huge whirlpool that can swallow\\neven ships."
msgstr ""
"Il dort tranquillement au fond de\\nl’océan. Quand il remonte à la "
"surface,\\nil crée d’énormes tourbillons qui peuvent\\navaler de gros "
"bateaux."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16221
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16310
msgid "Goldfish"
msgstr "Poisson"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16224
msgid ""
"In the springtime, schools of Goldeen\\ncan be seen swimming up falls and "
"rivers.\\nIt metes out staggering damage with its\\nsingle horn."
msgstr ""
"Au printemps, on peut voir des groupes de\\nPoissirene remonter les cours "
"d’eau.\\nIl inflige de sérieux dommages à l’aide\\nde son unique corne."

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16313
msgid ""
"It punches holes in boulders on stream-\\nbeds. This is a clever innovation "
"that\\nprevents its eggs from being attacked or\\nwashed away by the "
"current."
msgstr ""
"Il fait des trous dans les rochers dans\\nle lit des rivières pour mettre "
"ses œufs\\nà l’abri des prédateurs et du courant."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7557
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16394
msgid "STARYU"
msgstr "STARI"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16400
msgid ""
"It gathers with others in the night and\\nmakes its red core glow on and off"
" with\\nthe twinkling stars. It can regenerate\\nlimbs if they are severed "
"from its body."
msgstr ""
"Ils se réunissent la nuit et font briller\\nleur cœur rouge au rythme des "
"étoiles\\nscintillantes. S’il se fait couper un de ses\\nmembres, il est "
"capable de le régénérer."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Mystérieux
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16469
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16547
msgid "Mysterious"
msgstr "Secret"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16472
msgid ""
"People in ancient times imagined that\\nStarmie were transformed from "
"the\\nreflections of stars that twinkled on\\ngentle waves at night."
msgstr ""
"Autrefois, les gens pensaient que les\\nStaross provenaient du reflet des "
"étoiles\\nsur les vagues lors d’une nuit paisible."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16550
msgid ""
"Its movements have become more\\nhumanlike. Whether it's simply\\ntrying to "
"communicate or wants to\\nsupplant humanity is unclear."
msgstr ""
"Ses gestes sont devenus plus\\nhumains. Nul ne sait s’il cherche juste\\nà "
"communiquer ou à supplanter\\nl’humanité."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16610
msgid "MIME JR."
msgstr "MIME JR."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16613
msgid "Mime"
msgstr "Mime"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16616
msgid ""
"In an attempt to confuse its enemy,\\nit mimics the enemy's "
"movements.\\nOnce mimicked, the foe cannot take\\nits eyes off this Pokémon."
msgstr ""
"Il mime tout ce qu’il voit, et s’entraîne\\nbeaucoup pour reproduire les pas"
" de\\ndanse élégants des M. Glaquette."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Bloqueur
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16694
msgid "Barrier"
msgstr "Bouclier"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16697
msgid ""
"A Mr. Mime is a master of pantomime. It can\\nconvince others that something"
" unseeable\\nactually exists. Once believed, the\\nimaginary object does "
"become real."
msgstr ""
"M. Mime est un pantomime hors pair. Il\\nfait croire aux gens que quelque "
"chose\\nd’invisible existe réellement. Cet objet\\nimaginaire devient alors "
"réel."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16765
msgid "MR. MIME-G"
msgstr "M. MIME-G"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Danse
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16775
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:1578
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:1646
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:1714
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:1782
msgid "Dancing"
msgstr "La danse"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16778
msgid ""
"Its talent is tap-dancing. It can radiate\\nchilliness from the bottoms of "
"its feet to\\nto create a floor of ice, which this\\nPokémon can kick up to "
"use as a barrier."
msgstr ""
"Ce virtuose des claquettes dégage du froid\\nsous ses pieds pour créer un "
"sol de glace,\\nqu’il soulève pour s’en faire une barrière."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16846
msgid "MR. RIME"
msgstr "M. GLAQUETTE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Comédien
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16849
msgid "Comedian"
msgstr "Théâtre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16852
msgid ""
"It's highly skilled at tap-dancing. It\\nwaves its cane of ice in time with "
"its\\ngraceful movements."
msgstr ""
"Virtuose des claquettes, il se donne en\\nspectacle en dansant d’un pas "
"léger et en\\njonglant avec sa canne de glace."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Mante
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16918
msgid "Mantis"
msgstr "Mantis"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:16921
msgid ""
"Its blindingly fast speed adds to the\\nsharpness of its twin forearm "
"scythes.\\nThe scythes can slice through thick logs\\nin one wicked stroke."
msgstr ""
"Il est incroyablement rapide. Sa vitesse\\naméliore l’efficacité des deux "
"lames sur\\nses avant-bras. Elles peuvent trancher\\nun énorme tronc d’arbre"
" en un coup."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17021
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17102
msgid "SCIZOR"
msgstr "CIZAYOX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17027
msgid ""
"A Scizor has a body with the hardness of\\nsteel. It is not easily fazed by "
"ordinary\\nsorts of attacks. It flaps its wings to\\nregulate its body "
"temperature."
msgstr ""
"Le corps de Cizayox est dur comme de\\nl’acier. Les attaques ordinaires ne "
"le\\ndéstabilisent pas. Ce Pokémon bat des\\nailes pour réguler sa "
"température interne."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17112
msgid ""
"The excess energy that bathes this\\nPokémon keeps it in constant danger "
"of\\noverflow. It can't sustain a battle over\\nlong periods of time."
msgstr ""
"Le surplus d’énergie qui le baigne\\nmenace sans cesse de déborder. Il "
"ne\\lpeut soutenir un long combat."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17178
msgid "KLEAVOR"
msgstr "HACHECATEUR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17181
msgid "Axe"
msgstr "Hache"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17184
msgid ""
"A violent creature that fells trees with\\nits crude axes and shields itself"
" with hard\\nstone. Should one encounter this Pokémon\\nin the wild, one's "
"only recourse is to flee."
msgstr ""
"Une créature violente qui abat les arbres\\navec ses haches grossières et se"
" protège\\navec sa pierre dure. Si on le croise dans\\nla nature, mieux vaut"
" prendre la fuite."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17252
msgid "Kiss"
msgstr "Bisou"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17255
msgid ""
"It actively runs about, but also falls\\noften. Whenever it falls, it will "
"check its\\nreflection on a lake's surface to make\\nsure its face hasn't "
"become dirty."
msgstr ""
"LIPPOUTI court dans tous les sens\\net tombe souvent. Il regarde son "
"reflet\\ndans l’eau pour vérifier si son visage n’a\\npas été sali par ses "
"chutes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17326
msgid "Human Shape"
msgstr "Humanoïde"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17329
msgid ""
"A Jynx sashays rhythmically as if it were\\ndancing. Its motions are so "
"bouncingly\\nalluring, people seeing it are compelled to\\nshake their hips "
"without noticing."
msgstr ""
"Il marche en rythme comme s’il dansait.\\nSes mouvements sont si "
"communicatifs\\nque les gens qui le voient sont pris d’une\\nterrible envie "
"de bouger les hanches."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Électrique
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17400
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17474
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20654
msgid "Electric"
msgstr "ELECTRIK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17403
msgid ""
"If it touches metal and discharges the\\nelectricity it has stored in its "
"body, an\\nElekid begins swinging its arms in circles\\nto recharge itself."
msgstr ""
"Elekid stocke de l’électricité dans son\\ncorps. S’il touche du métal et "
"décharge\\nson électricité, il fait des cercles avec\\nses bras pour se "
"recharger."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17477
msgid ""
"When a storm approaches, it competes with\\nothers to scale heights that are"
" likely to\\nbe stricken by lightning. Some towns use\\nElectabuzz in place "
"of lightning rods."
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu’une tempête approche, ces\\nPokémon se battent pour grimper où "
"la\\nfoudre a le plus de chance de tomber. Ils\\nsont parfois utilisés comme"
" paratonnerre."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4385
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17552
msgid "ELECTIVIRE"
msgstr "ELEKABLE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Foudrélec
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17555
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2269
msgid "Thunderbolt"
msgstr "Tonnerre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17558
msgid ""
"When it gets excited, it thumps its chest.\\nWith every thud, thunder roars,"
" electric\\nsparks shower all around and blue sparks\\nbegin to crackle "
"between its horns."
msgstr ""
"La quantité d’électricité qu’il génère est\\nproportionnelle à son pouls. "
"Quand il\\nlivre un combat, son voltage augmente\\naussitôt."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17628
msgid "Live Coal"
msgstr "Charbon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17631
msgid ""
"If a Magby is spouting yellow flames from\\nits mouth, it is in good health."
" When it is\\nfatigued, black smoke will be mixed in with\\nthe flames."
msgstr ""
"Si Magby crache des flammes jaunes, c’est\\nqu’il est en bonne santé. "
"Lorsqu’il est\\nfatigué, de la fumée noire s’ajoute aux\\nflammes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17700
msgid "Spitfire"
msgstr "Crache-Feu"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17703
msgid ""
"In battle, it blows out intense flames from\\nall over its body to "
"intimidate its foe.\\nThese fiery bursts create heat waves that\\nignite "
"grass and trees in the area."
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu’il se bat, il fait jaillir des flammes\\nde son corps pour intimider "
"son adversaire\\net déclenche des vagues de chaleur qui\\nembrasent la "
"végétation environnante."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2820
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17776
msgid "MAGMORTAR"
msgstr "MAGANON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17779
msgid "Blast"
msgstr "Explosion"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17782
msgid ""
"According to what is known, a single pair\\nof male and female Magmortar "
"lives in\\none volcano. From its arm, it launches\\nfireballs hotter than "
"3,600ºF."
msgstr ""
"Selon ce que l’on sait, un seul couple\\nde Maganon vit dans chaque "
"volcan.\\nDe son bras, il lance des boules de feu\\nà plus de 2 000 degrés."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17852
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17929
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:1247
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:1308
msgid "Stag Beetle"
msgstr "Scarabée"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17855
msgid ""
"Their pincers are strong enough to\\nshatter thick logs. Because they "
"dislike\\ncold, Pinsir burrow and sleep under\\nthe ground on chilly nights."
msgstr ""
"Ses pinces sont assez fortes pour\\ndétruire de grosses bûches. Comme "
"il\\nn’aime pas le froid, il s’enfouit sous\\nterre lors des nuits fraîches."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:17932
msgid ""
"The influence of Mega Evolution leaves it\\nin a state of constant "
"excitement.\\nIt pierces enemies with its two large\\nhorns before shredding"
" them."
msgstr ""
"La Méga-Évolution le laisse dans un état\\nd’excitation permanent. Il "
"transperce\\nses ennemis de ses deux grandes cornes\\navant de les "
"déchiqueter."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18008
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18087
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18167
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18247
msgid "Wild Bull"
msgstr "Buffle"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18011
msgid ""
"It is not satisfied unless it is rampaging\\nat all times. If there is no "
"opponent for\\nTauros to battle, it will charge at thick\\ntrees and knock "
"them down to calm itself."
msgstr ""
"Il n’est pas satisfait s’il ne détruit pas\\ntout sur son passage. Lorsqu’il"
" ne trouve\\npas d’adversaire, il déracine de gros\\narbres pour passer ses "
"nerfs."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18077
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18157
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18237
msgid "TAUROS-P"
msgstr "TAUROS-P"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18090
msgid ""
"This Pokémon has a muscular body\\nand excels at close-quarters combat.\\nIt"
" uses its short horns to strike\\nthe opponent’s weak spots."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon au corps musclé excelle\\nau corps-à-corps. Il frappe "
"les\\npoints faibles de l’adversaire avec\\nses cornes courtes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18170
msgid ""
"When heated by fire energy, its horns can\\nget hotter than 1,800 degrees "
"Fahrenheit.\\nThose gored by them will suffer\\nboth wounds and burns."
msgstr ""
"Chauffées par son énergie de feu,\\nses cornes dépassent 1000 degrés.\\nSes "
"victimes subissent à la fois\\nblessures et brûlures."

#. source : patch FR actuel (correspondance douteuse, à vérifier)
#. source : patch FR actuel (récupéré par pointeur)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18250
msgid ""
"This Pokémon blasts water from holes on\\nthe tips of its horns--the high-"
"pressure\\njets pierce right through\\nTauros’s enemies."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon projette de l’eau par\\nle bout de ses cornes. Ces jets\\nà haute"
" pression transpercent\\nles ennemis de Tauros."

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main (le patch FR actuel donnait un morceau
#. d’un autre texte)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18322
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9098
msgid "Fish"
msgstr "Poisson"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18325
msgid ""
"Its swimming muscles are weak, so it is\\neasily washed away by currents. In"
" places\\nwhere water pools, you can see many\\nMagikarp deposited there by "
"the flow."
msgstr ""
"Ses muscles ne sont pas assez puissants\\npour qu’il puisse lutter contre le"
" courant.\\nOn peut souvent voir des Magicarpe\\nlà où l’eau a tendance à "
"stagner."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18410
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18497
msgid "Atrocious"
msgstr "Terrifiant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18413
msgid ""
"It is an extremely vicious and violent\\nPokémon. When humans begin to "
"fight,\\nit will appear and burn everything to the\\nground with intensely "
"hot flames."
msgstr ""
"C’est un Pokémon extrêmement violent.\\nQuand les humains commencent à se "
"battre,\\nil apparaît et brûle tout de ses flammes\\nintenses."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18500
msgid ""
"Although it obeys its instinctive drive to\\ndestroy everything within its "
"reach, it\\nwill respond to orders from a Trainer it\\ntruly trusts."
msgstr ""
"Bien qu’il obéisse à son instinct qui le\\npousse à détruire tout ce qui est"
" à sa\\nportée, il répond aux ordres d’un Dresseur\\nen qui il a toute "
"confiance."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18572
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18646
msgid "Transport"
msgstr "Transport"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18575
msgid ""
"People have driven Lapras almost to the\\npoint of extinction. In the "
"evenings,\\nit is said to sing plaintively as it seeks\\nwhat few others of "
"its kind still remain."
msgstr ""
"Les Lokhlass sont en voie d’extinction.\\nLe soir, on entend ce Pokémon "
"chantonner\\nune complainte mélancolique, espérant\\nretrouver ses rares "
"congénères."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18649
msgid ""
"Over 5,000 people can ride on its\\nshell at once. And it's a "
"very\\ncomfortable ride, without the slightest\\nshaking or swaying."
msgstr ""
"Plus de 5 000 personnes peuvent monter\\nsur sa carapace à la fois. Et la "
"balade\\nest très confortable, sans la moindre\\nsecousse ni le moindre "
"roulis."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18710
msgid "Transform"
msgstr "Morphing"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18713
msgid ""
"A Ditto rearranges its cell structure to\\ntransform itself. However, if it "
"tries to\\nchange based on its memory, it will get\\ndetails wrong."
msgstr ""
"Il peut modifier sa structure moléculaire\\npour prendre d’autres formes. "
"Mais quand il\\nessaye de se transformer de mémoire, il lui\\narrive de se "
"tromper sur certains détails."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Évolutif
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18789
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18897
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18957
msgid "Evolution"
msgstr "Evolution"

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:18900
msgid ""
"Having gotten even friendlier and\\nmore innocent, Eevee tries to "
"play\\nwith anyone around, only to end up\\ncrushing them with its immense "
"body."
msgstr ""
"Encore plus affectueux et innocent,\\nEVOLI veut jouer avec tout le "
"monde,\\nmais finit par écraser les gens sous\\nson corps immense."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19034
msgid "Bubble Jet"
msgstr "Bulleur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19037
msgid ""
"Vaporeon underwent a spontaneous\\nmutation and grew fins and gills "
"that\\nallow them to live underwater. They have\\nthe ability to freely "
"control water."
msgstr ""
"Aquali a subi une mutation spontanée. Des\\nnageoires et des branchies sont "
"apparues\\npour lui permettre de vivre dans les fonds\\nmarins. Il contrôle "
"l’eau à volonté."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19102
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5493
msgid "Lightning"
msgstr "Orage"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19105
msgid ""
"Its cells generate weak power that is\\namplified by its fur's static "
"electricity\\nto drop thunderbolts. The bristling fur is\\nmade of "
"electrically charged needles."
msgstr ""
"Ses cellules génèrent un courant de faible\\nintensité, amplifié par "
"l’électricité\\nstatique de sa fourrure faite d’aiguilles\\nélectrisées. Il "
"peut envoyer des éclairs."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19173
msgid ""
"Flareon's fluffy fur releases heat into\\nthe air so that its body does not "
"get\\nexcessively hot. Its body temperature can\\nrise to a maximum of 1,650"
" degrees F."
msgstr ""
"Sa fourrure soyeuse a pour fonction de\\nrejeter la chaleur dans l’air pour "
"que son\\ncorps ne surchauffe pas. La température\\nde son corps peut "
"atteindre 900 degrés."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19239
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3219
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12677
msgid "Sun"
msgstr "Soleil"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19242
msgid ""
"An Espeon is extremely loyal to any\\nTrainer it considers to be worthy. It "
"is\\nsaid to have developed precognitive\\npowers to protect its Trainer "
"from harm."
msgstr ""
"Mentali est extrêmement loyal envers les\\nDresseurs qu’il respecte. On "
"raconte que\\nce Pokémon a développé des talents\\ndivinatoires pour "
"protéger son Dresseur."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Lune
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19306
msgid "Moonlight"
msgstr "Rayon Lune"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19309
msgid ""
"Umbreon evolved from exposure to the\\nmoon's energy pulses. It lurks in "
"darkness\\nand waits for its foes to move. The rings\\non its body glow when"
" it leaps to attack."
msgstr ""
"Il a évolué suite à une exposition aux\\nrayons lunaires. Il se cache dans "
"le noir\\net attend le passage de ses ennemis.\\nSes anneaux s’illuminent "
"quand il bondit."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19371
msgid "LEAFEON"
msgstr "PHYLLALI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19374
msgid "Verdant"
msgstr "Verdoyant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19377
msgid ""
"Its cellular composition is closer to\\nthat of a plant than an animal. It "
"uses\\nphotosynthesis to produce its energy\\nsupply without eating food."
msgstr ""
"Les habitants de Galar adorent l’odeur\\nunique qui se dégage de ses "
"feuilles,\\naussi entrent-elles dans la\\ncomposition d’un parfum très "
"populaire."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19438
msgid "GLACEON"
msgstr "GIVRALI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19441
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7866
msgid "Fresh Snow"
msgstr "Poudreuse"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19444
msgid ""
"It can control its body temperature\\nat will. This enables it to freeze "
"the\\nmoisture in the atmosphere, creating\\nflurries of diamond dust."
msgstr ""
"Totalement subjuguées par la beauté\\ndes cristaux de glace qu’il fait "
"tomber,\\nses proies ne réalisent que trop tard\\nqu’elles sont en train de "
"geler."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4704
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19508
msgid "SYLVEON"
msgstr "NYMPHALI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19511
msgid "Intertwine"
msgstr "Attachant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19514
msgid ""
"Its ribbonlike feelers give off an aura\\nthat weakens hostility in its "
"prey, causing\\nthem to let down their guard. A moment\\nlater, it pounces."
msgstr ""
"Grâce à ses antennes semblables à des\\nrubans, il peut émettre des "
"ondes\\nneutralisant l’hostilité et ainsi mettre\\nfin aux querelles."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19585
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19662
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19743
msgid "Virtual"
msgstr "Virtuel"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19588
msgid ""
"It is capable of reverting itself entirely\\nback to program data in order "
"to enter\\ncyberspace. A Porygon is copy-\\nprotected so it cannot be "
"duplicated."
msgstr ""
"Il peut se décompiler et retourner à l’état\\nde programme informatique pour"
" entrer\\ndans le cyber-espace. Protégé contre le\\npiratage, il est "
"impossible à copier."

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19665
msgid ""
"It was created by humans using the power\\nof science. It has been given "
"artificial\\nintelligence that enables it to learn new\\ngestures and "
"emotions on its own."
msgstr ""
"PORYGON2 fut créé par des humains. Ce\\nPOKéMON a été doté d’une "
"intelligence\\nartificielle qui lui permet d’apprendre des\\nmouvements et "
"des émotions par lui-même."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19740
msgid "PORYGON-Z"
msgstr "PORYGON-Z"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19746
msgid ""
"In order to create a more advanced\\nPokémon, an additional program "
"was\\ninstalled, but apparently it contained a\\ndefect that made it move "
"oddly."
msgstr ""
"Depuis qu’on lui a ajouté un programme\\npermettant de voyager entre "
"les\\ndimensions, son comportement est\\ndevenu instable."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19819
msgid "OMANYTE"
msgstr "AMONITA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19822
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19896
msgid "Spiral"
msgstr "Spirale"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19825
msgid ""
"One of the ancient and long-since-extinct\\nPokémon that have been "
"regenerated\\nfrom fossils by humans. If attacked,\\nit withdraws into its "
"hard shell."
msgstr ""
"C’est un ancien Pokémon disparu depuis\\nlongtemps qui a été ressuscité à "
"partir\\nde fossiles. Lorsqu’il est attaqué par un\\nennemi, il se rétracte "
"dans sa coquille."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19899
msgid ""
"An Omastar uses its tentacles to capture\\nits prey. It is believed to have "
"become\\nextinct because its shell grew too large,\\nmaking its movements "
"slow and ponderous."
msgstr ""
"Il capture ses proies avec ses tentacules.\\nOn pense que l’espèce s’est "
"éteinte parce\\nque sa coquille était devenue trop grande,\\nrendant ses "
"mouvements lents et pesants."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19969
msgid "KABUTO"
msgstr "KABUTO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:19975
msgid ""
"It is a Pokémon that has been regenerated\\nfrom a fossil. However, in rare "
"cases, living\\nexamples have been discovered. Kabuto\\nhave not changed for"
" 300 million years."
msgstr ""
"C’est un Pokémon ressuscité à partir d’un\\nfossile. Cependant, on a "
"découvert des\\nspécimens vivants. Ce Pokémon n’a pas\\nchangé depuis 300 "
"millions d’années."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20055
msgid ""
"Kabutops once swam underwater to hunt \\nfor prey. It was apparently "
"evolving from\\nbeing a water dweller to living on land as\\nevident from "
"changes in its gills and legs."
msgstr ""
"Jadis, il trouvait ses proies sous l’eau.\\nLes changements dans ses "
"branchies\\nsemblent indiquer que ce Pokémon\\nterrestre descend d’une "
"créature marine."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Fossile
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20122
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20199
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:6216
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:6281
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:6345
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:6410
msgid "Fossil"
msgstr "Fossil"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20125
msgid ""
"Aerodactyl is a Pokémon from the age\\nof dinosaurs. It was regenerated from"
" DNA\\nextracted from amber. It is imagined to\\nhave been the king of the "
"skies."
msgstr ""
"C’est un Pokémon de l’ère des dinosaures.\\nIl fut ressuscité à partir de "
"cellules dans\\nun morceau d’ambre. On pense qu’il était\\nle roi des cieux "
"à l’époque préhistorique."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20202
msgid ""
"The power of Mega Evolution has\\ncompletely restored its genes. The "
"rocks\\non its body are harder than diamond."
msgstr ""
"Le pouvoir de la Méga-Évolution a\\nentièrement restauré ses gènes. "
"Les\\nrochers de son corps sont plus durs que\\nle diamant."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20272
msgid "MUNCHLAX"
msgstr "GOINFREX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20275
msgid "Big Eater"
msgstr "Goinfre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20278
msgid ""
"When it finds something that looks like\\nit might be edible, it goes right "
"ahead\\nand swallows it whole. That's why it gets\\nfatter day by day."
msgstr ""
"Il ne pense qu’à manger énormément. Il\\nn’a que faire du goût et "
"n’hésite\\nd’ailleurs pas à engloutir de la\\nnourriture avariée."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Pionceur
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20347
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20420
msgid "Sleeping"
msgstr "Je dormais"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20350
msgid ""
"Snorlax's typical day consists of nothing\\nmore than eating and sleeping. "
"It is such\\na docile Pokémon that there are children\\nwho use its big "
"belly as a place to play."
msgstr ""
"Les journées de Ronflex se résument\\naux repas et aux siestes. Il est "
"tellement\\ngentil que les enfants n’hésitent pas à\\njouer sur son énorme "
"ventre."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20423
msgid ""
"Gigantamax energy has affected\\nstray seeds and even pebbles that\\ngot "
"stuck to Snorlax, making them grow\\nto a huge size."
msgstr ""
"L’énergie Gigamax a affecté des\\ngraines égarées et même des "
"cailloux\\ncollés à RONFLEX, qui sont devenus\\nénormes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: data/maps/Route25_BillsHouse_hns/scripts.inc:346
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8202
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20485
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20561
msgid "ARTICUNO"
msgstr "ARTIKODIN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: data/scripts/debug.inc:713 src/battle_debug.c:350
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20488
msgid "Freeze"
msgstr "Glaciaire"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20491
msgid ""
"Articuno is a legendary bird Pokémon that\\ncan control ice. The flapping of"
" its wings\\nchills the air. As a result, it is said that\\nwhen this "
"Pokémon flies, snow will fall."
msgstr ""
"C’est un Pokémon oiseau légendaire qui\\npeut contrôler la glace. Son "
"battement\\nd’ailes gèle l’air tout autour de lui. On dit\\nque lorsqu’il "
"vole, la neige va tomber."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20559
msgid "ARTICUNO-G"
msgstr "ARTIKODIN-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20569
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1331
msgid "Cruel"
msgstr "Implacable"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20572
msgid ""
"It fires beams that immobilize opponents\\nas if they had been frozen "
"solid.\\nIts feather-like blades of psychic energy\\nrip through thick iron "
"sheets like paper."
msgstr ""
"Ses rayons immobilisent l’ennemi comme s’il\\nétait gelé. Ses lames "
"psychiques en forme\\nde plumes déchirent l’acier comme du\\npapier."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: data/maps/Route25_BillsHouse_hns/scripts.inc:349
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8076
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20651
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20729
msgid "ZAPDOS"
msgstr "ELECTHOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20657
msgid ""
"Zapdos is a legendary bird Pokémon that\\nhas the ability to control "
"electricity.\\nIt usually lives in thunderclouds. It gains\\npower if it is "
"stricken by lightning bolts."
msgstr ""
"C’est un Pokémon oiseau légendaire\\ncapable de contrôler l’électricité. Il "
"vit\\ngénéralement dans les nuages orageux. La\\nfoudre le rend plus fort."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20727
msgid "ZAPDOS-G"
msgstr "ELECTHOR-G"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20737
msgid "Strong Legs"
msgstr "Grand-Pied"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20740
msgid ""
"When its feathers rub together, they\\nproduce a crackling sound like "
"the\\nzapping of electricity. Apparently, it runs\\nthrough the mountains at"
" over 180 mph."
msgstr ""
"Ses plumes crépitent comme de l’électricité\\nquand elles se frottent. Il "
"parcourrait les\\nmontagnes à plus de 300 km/h."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: data/maps/Route25_BillsHouse_hns/scripts.inc:352
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7378
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20815
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20919
msgid "MOLTRES"
msgstr "SULFURA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20821
msgid ""
"Moltres is a legendary bird Pokémon\\nthat can control fire. If injured, it "
"is said\\nto dip its body in the molten magma of\\na volcano to burn and "
"heal itself."
msgstr ""
"C’est un Pokémon oiseau légendaire\\npouvant contrôler le feu. On raconte "
"que\\nlorsqu’il est blessé, il se baigne dans un\\nvolcan en ébullition pour"
" se soigner."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20917
msgid "MOLTRES-G"
msgstr "SULFURA-G"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20927
msgid "Malevolent"
msgstr "Malveillant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:20930
msgid ""
"This Pokémon's sinister, flame-like aura\\nwill consume the spirit of any "
"creature\\nit hits. Victims become burned-out\\nshadows of themselves."
msgstr ""
"Son aura sinistre semblable à des flammes\\nconsume l’esprit de ceux qu’elle"
" touche.\\nSes victimes ne sont plus que l’ombre\\nd’elles-mêmes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21006
msgid ""
"A Dratini continually molts and sloughs\\noff its old skin. It does so "
"because the\\nlife energy within its body steadily builds\\nto reach "
"uncontrollable levels."
msgstr ""
"Minidraco mue constamment. En effet,\\nl’énergie vitale de son corps "
"augmente\\nrégulièrement et sa mue lui permet d’éviter\\nd’atteindre des "
"niveaux incontrôlables."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21076
msgid ""
"A Dragonair stores an enormous amount of\\nenergy inside its body. It is "
"said to alter\\nthe weather around it by loosing energy\\nfrom the crystals "
"on its neck and tail."
msgstr ""
"Il stocke de l’énergie dans son corps. On\\nraconte qu’il peut modifier les "
"conditions\\nclimatiques en déchargeant l’énergie des\\ncristaux de son cou "
"et de sa queue."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21152
msgid ""
"It can circle the globe in just 16 hours.\\nIt is a kindhearted Pokémon that"
" leads\\nlost and foundering ships in a storm\\nto the safety of land."
msgstr ""
"Dracolosse est capable de faire le tour de\\nla planète en seize heures à "
"peine. Ce\\nPokémon au grand cœur ramène à bon\\nport les navires perdus "
"dans les tempêtes."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21230
msgid ""
"Mega Evolution has excessively\\npowered up this Pokémon's feelings\\nof "
"kindness. It finishes off its\\nopponents with mercy in its heart."
msgstr ""
"La Méga-Évolution a démesurément\\nrenforcé la bienveillance de "
"ce\\nPokémon. Il achève ses adversaires\\navec compassion."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21288
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21360
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21436
msgid "MEWTWO"
msgstr "MEWTWO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21291
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21367
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21443
msgid "Genetic"
msgstr "Génétique"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21294
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that was created by genetic\\nmanipulation. However, even though "
"the\\nscientific power of humans made its body,\\nthey failed to give it a "
"warm heart."
msgstr ""
"Mewtwo a été créé par manipulation\\ngénétique. Bien que les humains "
"aient\\nréussi à créer son corps, il n’a pas été\\ndoté d’un cœur sensible."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21370
msgid ""
"Psychic power has augmented its muscles.\\nIt has a grip strength of one ton"
" and can\\nsprint a hundred meters in two seconds\\nflat!"
msgstr ""
"Le pouvoir psychique a renforcé ses\\nmuscles. Il a une poigne d’une tonne "
"et\\ncourt cent mètres en deux secondes\\nchrono!"

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21446
msgid ""
"Despite its diminished size, its mental\\npower has grown phenomenally. With"
" a mere\\nthought, it can smash a skyscraper to\\nsmithereens."
msgstr ""
"Malgré sa taille réduite, son pouvoir\\nmental a augmenté de façon "
"phénoménale.\\nD’une simple pensée, il peut réduire un\\ngratte-ciel en "
"miettes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21524
msgid "MEW"
msgstr "MEW"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21527
msgid "New Species"
msgstr "Nouveau"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_1_families.h:21530
msgid ""
"A Mew is said to possess the genes of all\\nPokémon. It is capable of making"
" itself\\ninvisible at will, so it entirely avoids\\nnotice even if it "
"approaches people."
msgstr ""
"On dit que Mew possède le code génétique\\nde tous les autres Pokémon. Il "
"peut se\\nrendre invisible et ne se fait pas\\nremarquer quand il s’approche"
" des gens."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:26
msgid "CHIKORITA"
msgstr "GERMIGNON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:29
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:99 src/debug.c:462
msgid "Leaf"
msgstr "Feuille"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:32
msgid ""
"It waves its leaf around to keep foes\\nat bay. However, a sweet fragrance "
"also\\nwafts from the leaf, creating a friendly\\natmosphere that becalms "
"the battlers."
msgstr ""
"En combat, il secoue sa feuille pour tenir\\nl’ennemi à distance. Un doux "
"parfum s’en\\ndégage, apaisant ainsi les Pokémon qui se\\nbattent et créant "
"une atmosphère amicale."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7762
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:96
msgid "BAYLEEF"
msgstr "MACRONIUM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:102
msgid ""
"A Bayleef's neck is ringed by curled-up\\nleaves. Inside each leaf is a "
"small tree\\nshoot. The fragrance of this shoot\\nmakes people peppy."
msgstr ""
"Son cou est entouré de nombreuses\\nfeuilles. Dans chacune d’elles se "
"trouve\\nune pousse d’arbre dont le parfum donne\\nla pêche aux personnes "
"qui le sentent."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:173
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:260
msgid "Herb"
msgstr "Herbe"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:176
msgid ""
"The fragrance of a Meganium's flower\\nsoothes and calms emotions. In "
"battle,\\nit gives off more of its becalming scent\\nto blunt the foe's "
"fighting spirit."
msgstr ""
"Le parfum de la fleur de Meganium apaise\\net calme les esprits. Pendant les"
" combats,\\nce Pokémon émet son parfum relaxant\\npour atténuer "
"l’agressivité de l’ennemi."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:263
msgid ""
"This Pokémon can fire a tremendously\\npowerful Solar Beam from its "
"four\\nflowers. Another name for this is\\nMega Sol Cannon."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon tire un Lance-Soleil\\nsurpuissant de ses quatre fleurs. "
"On\\lsurnomme ce tir “canon Méga-Soleil”."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:314
msgid "CYNDAQUIL"
msgstr "HERICENDRE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:317
msgid "Fire Mouse"
msgstr "Souris Feu"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:320
msgid ""
"It flares flames from its back to protect\\nitself. The fire burns "
"vigorously if the\\nPokémon is angry. When it is tired,\\nit sputters with "
"incomplete combustion."
msgstr ""
"Il se protège en faisant jaillir des\\nflammes de son dos. S’il est en "
"colère, elles\\nsont violentes. S’il est fatigué, quelques\\nflammèches "
"vacillent laborieusement."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7802
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:385
msgid "QUILAVA"
msgstr "FEURISSON"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:391
msgid ""
"It intimidates foes with intense gusts of\\nflames and superheated air. Its "
"quick\\nnimbleness lets it dodge attacks even\\nwhile scorching an enemy."
msgstr ""
"Il garde ses ennemis à distance grâce à\\nses flammes et à des rafales d’air"
" brûlant.\\nSon agilité lui permet d’éviter les\\nattaques, tout en "
"enflammant ses ennemis."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1191
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:462
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:534
msgid "TYPHLOSION"
msgstr "TYPHLOSION"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:468
msgid ""
"It can hide behind a shimmering heat haze\\nthat it creates using its "
"intense flames.\\nTyphlosion create blazing explosive\\nblasts that burn "
"everything to cinders."
msgstr ""
"Il se cache derrière un chatoyant nuage de\\nchaleur qu’il crée en attisant "
"ses flammes\\nintenses. Il peut générer des rafales\\nexplosives qui "
"réduisent tout en cendres."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:532
msgid "TYPHLOSION-H"
msgstr "TYPHLOSION-H"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:542
msgid "Ghost Flame"
msgstr "Feu Spectre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:545
msgid ""
"Said to purify lost, forsaken souls with\\nits flames and guide them to the "
"afterlife.\\nIt's believed its form was influenced by\\nthe energy of Mt. "
"Coronet in ancient times."
msgstr ""
"On dit que ses flammes purifient les âmes\\négarées et les guident vers "
"l’au-delà.\\nL’énergie du Mont Couronné aurait jadis\\nfaçonné sa forme."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:615
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:689
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:763
msgid "Big Jaw"
msgstr "Mâchoire"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:618
msgid ""
"Despite its small body, Totodile's jaws\\nare very powerful. While it may "
"think it is\\njust playfully nipping, its bite has enough\\nstrength to "
"cause serious injury."
msgstr ""
"Malgré son tout petit corps, la mâchoire de\\nKaiminus est très puissante. "
"Il mordille\\npour jouer, sans se rendre compte que sa\\nmorsure peut "
"gravement blesser quelqu’un."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7782
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:686
msgid "CROCONAW"
msgstr "CROCRODIL"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:692
msgid ""
"Once its jaws clamp down on its foe, it will\\nabsolutely not let go. "
"Because the tips of\\nits fangs are forked back like fishhooks,\\nthey "
"become irremovably embedded."
msgstr ""
"Quand il a refermé sa mâchoire sur son\\nennemi, il ne lâche pas prise. Ses "
"crocs\\nrecourbés comme des hameçons ne peuvent\\npas être retirés une fois "
"enfoncés."

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:766
msgid ""
"It opens its huge mouth to intimidate\\nenemies. In battle, it runs using "
"its thick\\nand powerful hind legs to charge the\\nfoe with incredible "
"speed."
msgstr ""
"Il impressionne ses ennemis en ouvrant son\\nénorme gueule. Au combat, il "
"piétine le sol\\nde ses puissantes pattes arrière avant de\\ncharger ses "
"adversaires à pleine vitesse."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:840
msgid "Double Jaw"
msgstr "Mâchoire"

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:843
msgid ""
"With its arms and hoodlike fin, this\\nPokémon forms a gigantic set of "
"jaws\\nwith a bite 10 times as powerful\\nas Mega Feraligatr's actual jaws."
msgstr ""
"Avec ses bras et son aileron en\\ncapuche, ce Pokémon forme une\\nmâchoire "
"géante qui mord 10 fois plus\\nfort que sa vraie mâchoire."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:894
msgid "SENTRET"
msgstr "FOUINETTE"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:900
msgid ""
"They take turns standing guard when it\\nis time to sleep. The sentry "
"awakens the\\nothers if it senses danger. If one becomes\\nseparated, it "
"turns sleepless with fear."
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu’un FOUINETTE dort, un autre monte\\nla garde pour le réveiller au "
"moindre\\nsigne de danger. Un FOUINETTE séparé de\\nsa meute arrête de "
"dormir car il a peur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:967
msgid "Long Body"
msgstr "Allongé"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:970
msgid ""
"A Furret has a very slim build. When under\\nattack, it can squirm through "
"narrow\\nspaces and get away. In spite of its short\\nlimbs, it is very "
"nimble and fleet."
msgstr ""
"Etant très mince, Fouinar peut s’enfuir en\\nse faufilant habilement dans "
"les recoins\\nétroits lorsqu’il est attaqué. Malgré ses\\npattes courtes, il"
" est très agile et rapide."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1032
msgid "HOOTHOOT"
msgstr "HOOTHOOT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1035
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1120
msgid "Owl"
msgstr "Hibou"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1038
msgid ""
"It has an internal organ that senses\\nthe earth's rotation. Using this "
"special\\norgan, a Hoothoot begins hooting at\\nprecisely the same time "
"every day."
msgstr ""
"Hoothoot est doté d’un organe interne qui\\nressent et suit la rotation de "
"la terre.\\nGrâce à cet organe, il commence à hululer\\ntous les jours "
"exactement à la même heure."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1123
msgid ""
"It unfailingly catches prey in darkness.\\nNoctowl owe their success to "
"superior\\nvision that allows them to see in minimal\\nlight, and to their "
"supple and silent wings."
msgstr ""
"Dans l’obscurité, Noarfang ne rate\\njamais une proie. Il le doit à sa "
"vision\\nsurdéveloppée qui lui permet de tout voir\\net à ses ailes souples "
"et silencieuses."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1185
msgid "LEDYBA"
msgstr "COXY"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1188
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1271
msgid "Five Star"
msgstr "5 Étoiles"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1191
msgid ""
"Ledyba communicate using a fluid that\\nthey secrete from where the legs "
"join the\\nbody. They are said to convey feelings to\\nothers by altering "
"the fluid's scent."
msgstr ""
"Les articulations des pattes de Coxy\\nsécrètent un fluide lui permettant "
"de\\ncommuniquer. Il exprime ses sentiments\\nen modifiant l’odeur de ce "
"fluide."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1274
msgid ""
"It is said that in lands with clean air,\\nwhere the stars fill the sky, "
"there live\\nmany Ledian. For good reason, they use\\nthe light of the stars"
" as energy."
msgstr ""
"On dit que là où le ciel est dégagé et où\\nles étoiles illuminent les "
"cieux, vivent\\nbeaucoup de Coxyclaque. En effet, leur\\nénergie provient de"
" la lumière des étoiles."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1352
msgid "SPINARAK"
msgstr "MIMIGAL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1355
msgid "String Spit"
msgstr "Crache Fil"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1358
msgid ""
"The web it spins can be considered its\\nsecond nervous system. It is said "
"that a\\nSpinarak determines its prey by the tiny\\nvibrations it feels "
"through the web."
msgstr ""
"La toile tissée par Mimigal est comme un\\nsecond système nerveux. On dit "
"qu’il peut\\ndéterminer quelle proie touche sa toile\\ngrâce aux infimes "
"vibrations des fils."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1435
msgid "Long Leg"
msgstr "Long-Patte"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1438
msgid ""
"Its feet are tipped with tiny hooked claws\\nthat enable it to scuttle on "
"ceilings and\\nvertical walls. It constricts its foe with\\nthin and strong "
"silk webbing."
msgstr ""
"A l’extrémité de ses pattes, on trouve des\\ncrochets qui lui permettent de "
"cavaler\\nsur les surfaces verticales et au plafond.\\nIl piège ses ennemis "
"dans sa toile de soie."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Poisson
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1506
msgid "Angler"
msgstr "Angler"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1509
msgid ""
"When it senses danger, it discharges\\npositive and negative electricity "
"from its\\ntwo antennae. It lives in depths beyond\\nsunlight's reach."
msgstr ""
"S’il pressent un danger, il décharge de\\nl’électricité à partir de ses "
"deux\\nantennes. Il vit dans les profondeurs, là\\noù la lumière ne parvient"
" jamais."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1580
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2192
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2267
msgid "Light"
msgstr "Lumière"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1583
msgid ""
"The light-emitting orbs on its back are\\nvery bright. They are formed from "
"a part of\\nits dorsal fin. This Pokémon illuminates\\nthe inky darkness of "
"deep seas."
msgstr ""
"Les globes de son dos sont très lumineux.\\nIls sont composés d’une partie "
"de sa\\nnageoire dorsale et éclairent la pénombre\\ndes fonds marins."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1656
msgid "Spike Ball"
msgstr "Balle Pic"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1659
msgid ""
"As its energy, it uses the feelings of\\ncompassion and pleasure exuded "
"by\\npeople and Pokémon. It stores up happy\\nfeelings in its shell, then "
"shares them out."
msgstr ""
"L’énergie de Togepi provient du plaisir\\net des émotions exprimés par les "
"gens et\\nles Pokémon. Il les accumule dans sa\\ncoquille, puis les partage "
"avec les autres."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1729
msgid ""
"It is said to be a Pokémon that brings good\\nfortune. When it spots someone"
" who is pure\\nof heart, a Togetic appears and shares its\\nhappiness with "
"that person."
msgstr ""
"On raconte que Togetic porte chance. Si\\nce Pokémon remarque quelqu’un doté"
" d’un\\ncœur pur, il apparaît et partage son\\nbonheur avec la personne en "
"question."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1627
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4834
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1802
msgid "TOGEKISS"
msgstr "TOGEKISS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1805
msgid "Jubilee"
msgstr "Célébration"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1808
msgid ""
"As everyone knows, it visits peaceful\\nregions, bringing them gifts of "
"kindness\\nand sweet blessings. It will never appear\\nwhere there is "
"strife."
msgstr ""
"Il ne se montre jamais en temps de\\nguerre ou de conflit. Ces derniers "
"temps,\\nil est rare de le croiser."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1877
msgid "NATU"
msgstr "NATU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1883
msgid ""
"It runs up short trees that grow on the\\nsavanna to peck at new shoots.\\nA"
" Natu's eyes look as if they are\\nalways observing something."
msgstr ""
"Il descend des petits arbustes de la\\nsavane pour picorer de jeunes "
"pousses.\\nSes yeux donnent toujours l’impression\\nqu’il observe quelque "
"chose."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1954
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7546
msgid "Mystic"
msgstr "Mystique"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:1957
msgid ""
"It has the enigmatic power of foreseeing\\nthe future. Some people in "
"different lands\\nhave long believed that Xatu are\\nemissaries from another"
" world."
msgstr ""
"Il a le pouvoir incroyable de deviner\\nle futur. Les hommes ont longtemps "
"cru\\nque Xatu était l’émissaire d’un autre\\nmonde."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2041
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2114
msgid "Wool"
msgstr "Laine"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2044
msgid ""
"Its fluffy wool rubs together and builds\\na static charge. The more energy "
"is\\ncharged, the more brightly the lightbulb\\nat the tip of its tail "
"glows."
msgstr ""
"La fourrure cotonneuse de Wattouat se\\ncharge d’électricité statique. Plus "
"elle\\nest chargée, plus l’ampoule au bout de sa\\nqueue est lumineuse."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2117
msgid ""
"Its fleece quality changes to generate\\nstrong static electricity with a "
"small\\namount of wool. The bare, slick parts of its\\nhide are shielded "
"against electricity."
msgstr ""
"La qualité de sa laine change pour générer\\nun maximum d’électricité "
"statique avec un\\nminimum de laine. Les sections glabres de\\nsa peau "
"résistent à l’électricité."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2195
msgid ""
"It gives off so much light that it can be\\nseen even from space. People in "
"the old\\ndays used its light to send signals back\\nand forth with others "
"far away."
msgstr ""
"Pharamp est si lumineux qu’on peut le voir\\nde l’espace. Jadis, les gens "
"utilisaient sa\\nlumière pour communiquer et s’envoyer des\\nsignaux à "
"grande distance."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2270
msgid ""
"Massive amounts of energy intensely\\nstimulated Ampharos's cells, "
"apparently\\nawakening its long-sleeping dragon's\\nblood."
msgstr ""
"Un fort afflux d’énergie a stimulé les\\ncellules de PHARAMP, "
"éveillant,\\lsemble-t-il, son sang de dragon\\llongtemps endormi."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2344
msgid "Polka Dot"
msgstr "Point Polka"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2347
msgid ""
"Its tail, which is packed with nutrition,\\nis very bouncy like a rubber "
"ball. On sunny\\ndays they gather at the edge of water and\\nsplash about "
"for fun."
msgstr ""
"Sa queue, remplie de nourriture, est aussi\\nélastique qu’un ballon "
"gonflable. Les jours\\nensoleillés, ils se réunissent au bord de\\nl’eau et "
"passent leur temps à s’arroser."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6087
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2419
msgid "MARILL"
msgstr "MARILL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2422
msgid "Aqua Mouse"
msgstr "Aquasouris"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2425
msgid ""
"Its body is covered with water-repellent\\nfur. Because of the fur, it can "
"swim\\nthrough water at high speed without being\\nslowed by the water's "
"resistance."
msgstr ""
"Son corps est couvert d’une fourrure\\nimperméable. Grâce à elle, il peut "
"nager\\nà grande vitesse sans être ralenti par la\\nrésistance de l’eau."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2504
msgid "Aqua Rabbit"
msgstr "Aqualapin"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2507
msgid ""
"It lives in water virtually all day long.\\nIts body color and pattern act "
"as\\ncamouflage that makes it tough for\\nenemies to spot in water."
msgstr ""
"Il passe tout son temps sous l’eau.\\nLa forme et la couleur de son "
"corps\\nservent de camouflage pour que ses\\nennemis ne puissent pas "
"l’apercevoir."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2573
msgid "BONSLY"
msgstr "MANZAI"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2576
msgid "Bonsai"
msgstr "Bonsai"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2579
msgid ""
"Bonsly prefers an arid atmosphere.\\nIn order to adjust the level of "
"fluids\\nin its body, it exudes water from its eyes.\\nThis makes it appear "
"to be crying."
msgstr ""
"Il évacue sa sueur et ses larmes par les\\nyeux. Sa sueur a un goût "
"légèrement salé,\\ntandis que ses larmes ont un soupçon\\nd’amertume."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7981
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2645
msgid "SUDOWOODO"
msgstr "SIMULARBRE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2648
msgid "Imitation"
msgstr "Imitation"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2651
msgid ""
"It mimics a tree to avoid being attacked\\nby enemies. But since its "
"forelegs\\nremain green throughout the year, it is\\neasily identified as a "
"fake in the winter."
msgstr ""
"Il se camoufle en arbre pour éviter d’être\\nattaqué par ses ennemis. Mais "
"étant donné\\nque ses pattes sont vertes toute l’année,\\nil est facile à "
"repérer pendant l’hiver."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2735
msgid "HOPPIP"
msgstr "GRANIVOL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2738
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2813
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2899
msgid "Cottonweed"
msgstr "Pissenlit"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2741
msgid ""
"This Pokémon drifts and floats with the\\nwind. If it senses the approach of"
" strong\\nwinds, a Hoppip links leaves with others\\nto prepare against "
"being blown away."
msgstr ""
"Granivol flotte à la dérive, porté par le\\nvent. S’il sent qu’un vent très "
"fort\\napproche, il attache ses feuilles aux\\nautres Granivol pour ne pas "
"être emporté."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2810
msgid "SKIPLOOM"
msgstr "FLORAVOL"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2816
msgid ""
"It blossoms when the temperature rises\\nabove 64 degrees F. Because its "
"flower's\\nblooming changes with the temperature,\\nit is sometimes used as "
"a thermometer."
msgstr ""
"Sa fleur éclot lorsque la température\\natteint 18 degrés. Son ouverture "
"change\\nen fonction de la température. Certains\\nse servent de lui comme "
"d’un thermomètre."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2902
msgid ""
"Jumpluff ride warm southern winds to\\ncross the sea and fly to foreign "
"lands.\\nThis Pokémon lands when it encounters\\ncold air while it is "
"floating."
msgstr ""
"Cotovol traverse la mer, porté par\\nles vents, pour découvrir de "
"nouveaux\\nterritoires. Ce Pokémon se rapproche\\ndu sol quand le vent est "
"trop froid."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2969
msgid "AIPOM"
msgstr "CAPUMAIN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2972
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3056
msgid "Long Tail"
msgstr "Longqueue"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:2975
msgid ""
"Its tail ends with a dexterous, handlike\\nappendage. However, because it "
"uses the\\ntail so much, Aipom's real hands have\\nbecome rather clumsy."
msgstr ""
"L’extrémité de la queue de Capumain\\nressemble à une main et peut être "
"utilisée\\nde façon ingénieuse. Il l’utilise tant, que\\nses mains sont "
"devenues très maladroites."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3053
msgid "AMBIPOM"
msgstr "CAPIDEXTRE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3059
msgid ""
"They live on large trees. Split into two,\\nthe tails are so adept at "
"handling and\\ndoing things, Ambipom rarely uses\\nits hands now."
msgstr ""
"Il utilise toujours ses deux queues\\npour faire la moindre tâche. Il s’en "
"sert\\naussi pour enlacer les gens qu’il\\naffectionne tout "
"particulièrement."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3140
msgid "SUNKERN"
msgstr "TOURNEGRIN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3146
msgid ""
"Sunkern try to minimize movement to\\nconserve the nutrients they have "
"stored\\nin their bodies for evolution. They will\\nnot eat, subsisting only"
" on morning dew."
msgstr ""
"Il essaye de bouger le moins possible pour\\nconserver tous les nutriments "
"qu’il stocke\\ndans son corps pour son évolution. Il ne\\nmange pas et vit "
"grâce à la rosée matinale."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1469
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7153
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3216
msgid "SUNFLORA"
msgstr "HELIATRONC"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3222
msgid ""
"Sunflora convert solar energy into\\nnutrition. They are highly active in "
"the\\nwarm daytime but suddenly stop moving as\\nsoon as the sun sets."
msgstr ""
"Heliatronc convertit l’énergie solaire en\\nnutriments. Il remue activement "
"pendant la\\njournée, quand il fait chaud. Il redevient\\nimmobile dès que "
"le soleil se couche."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3289
msgid "Clear Wing"
msgstr "Translaile"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3292
msgid ""
"It can see 360 degrees without moving\\nits eyes. It is a great flier "
"capable of\\nmaking sudden stops and turning midair to\\nquickly chase down "
"targeted prey."
msgstr ""
"Il a un champ de vision de 360 degrés sans\\navoir besoin de bouger les "
"yeux. Il vole\\nincroyablement bien et peut descendre en\\npiqué sur ses "
"proies."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3379
msgid "YANMEGA"
msgstr "YANMEGA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3382
msgid "Ogre Darner"
msgstr "Libellogre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3385
msgid ""
"This six-legged Pokémon is easily capable\\nof transporting an adult in "
"flight. It is\\nadept at biting apart foes while flying\\nby at high speed."
msgstr ""
"Il peut voler avec aise tout en portant\\nun adulte dans ses six pattes. Les"
" ailes\\nde sa queue lui servent de balancier."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3476
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3559
msgid "Water Fish"
msgstr "Poisson"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3479
msgid ""
"Wooper usually live in water but come\\nout onto land seeking food "
"occasionally.\\nOn land, they coat their bodies with a\\ngooey, toxic film."
msgstr ""
"Axoloto vit généralement dans l’eau. Mais\\nde temps en temps, il vient sur "
"terre pour\\nchercher à manger. A terre, il recouvre son\\ncorps d’un voile "
"visqueux et toxique."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3562
msgid ""
"A Quagsire hunts by leaving its mouth wide\\nopen in water and waiting for "
"its prey to\\nblunder in. Because it doesn't move, it\\ndoes not get very "
"hungry."
msgstr ""
"Maraiste trouve sa nourriture en laissant\\nsa bouche ouverte dans l’eau, il"
" attend que\\nses proies y pénètrent. Comme ce Pokémon\\nest inactif, il n’a"
" jamais très faim."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3637
msgid "WOOPER-P"
msgstr "AXOLOTO-P"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3647
msgid "Poison Fish"
msgstr "Poisson Tox."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3650
msgid ""
"After losing a territorial struggle,\\nWooper began living on land.\\nThe "
"Pokémon changed over time, developing\\na poisonous film to protect its "
"body."
msgstr ""
"Après avoir perdu une lutte de\\nterritoire, Axoloto s’est installé\\nsur la"
" terre ferme et s’est couvert\\nd’un film toxique protecteur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3717
msgid "CLODSIRE"
msgstr "TERRAISTE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3720
msgid "Spiny Fish"
msgstr "Poissépine"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3723
msgid ""
"When attacked, this Pokémon will\\nretaliate by sticking thick spines "
"out\\nfrom its body. It's a risky move\\nthat puts everything on the line."
msgstr ""
"Attaqué, il riposte en dressant\\nd’épaisses épines sur son corps.\\nC’est "
"une manœuvre risquée où il\\njoue son va-tout."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3790
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4641
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4719
msgid "Darkness"
msgstr "Obscurité"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3793
msgid ""
"Murkrow were feared as the alleged\\nbearers of ill fortune. It shows "
"strong\\ninterest in anything that sparkles. It will\\neven try to steal "
"rings from women."
msgstr ""
"Jadis, Cornebre était craint et détesté\\ncar on disait qu’il portait "
"malheur. Il est\\nattiré par tout ce qui brille. Parfois, il\\nessaye de "
"voler les bagues des filles."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4298
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3873
msgid "HONCHKROW"
msgstr "CORBOSS"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3876
msgid "Big Boss"
msgstr "Grand Patron"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3879
msgid ""
"Becoming active at night, it is known\\nto swarm with numerous Murkrow in "
"tow.\\nIt is said that it never forgives the\\nmistakes of its cronies."
msgstr ""
"Ses sous-fifres font le sale boulot\\npour lui. Il n’intervient en combat "
"que\\npour donner le coup de grâce à son\\nennemi."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Strident
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3948
msgid "Screech"
msgstr "Grincement"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:3951
msgid ""
"A Misdreavus frightens people with a\\ncreepy, sobbing cry. It apparently "
"uses\\nits red spheres to absorb the fear of foes\\nas its nutrition."
msgstr ""
"Il effraie les gens avec son cri à faire\\nfroid dans le dos, sorte de "
"lamentation.\\nIl utilise ses sphères rouges pour se\\nnourrir de la terreur"
" de ses ennemis."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4854
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4026
msgid "MISMAGIUS"
msgstr "MAGIREVE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4029
msgid "Magical"
msgstr "Magique"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4032
msgid ""
"Its cries sound like incantations.\\nThose hearing it are tormented "
"by\\nheadaches and hallucinations.\\nIt appears where you least expect it."
msgstr ""
"Il susurre des malédictions pour\\ntourmenter ses ennemis et leur "
"infliger\\nde terribles migraines ou des\\nhallucinations terrifiantes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2383
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2402
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2421
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2572
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2591
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2610
msgid "UNOWN"
msgstr "ZARBI"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Symbolique
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4109
msgid "Symbol"
msgstr "Symbol"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7914
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4201
msgid "WYNAUT"
msgstr "OKEOKE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4204
msgid "Bright"
msgstr "Ravi"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4207
msgid ""
"A Wynaut loves to eat sweet fruits.\\nIt cleverly picks fruits using its "
"earlike\\narms. They gather in fruit gardens, drawn\\nby the fragrance."
msgstr ""
"Okeoke raffole des fruits sucrés qu’il\\nattrape à l’aide de ses bras en "
"forme\\nd’oreilles. Ces Pokémon se réunissent dans\\nles jardins fruitiers, "
"attirés par l’odeur."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1547
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8818
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4274
msgid "WOBBUFFET"
msgstr "QULBUTOKE"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4277
msgid "Patient"
msgstr "Patient"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4280
msgid ""
"Usually docile, a Wobbuffet strikes back\\nferociously if its black tail is "
"attacked.\\nIt makes its lair in caves where it waits\\nfor nightfall."
msgstr ""
"Normalement très docile, il attaquera\\nférocement si sa queue noire "
"est\\nattaquée. Il vit dans les grottes où il\\nattend la tombée de la nuit."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4366
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4451
msgid "Long Neck"
msgstr "Long-Cou"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4369
msgid ""
"A Girafarig is an herbivore--it eats\\ngrass and tree shoots. While it is "
"eating,\\nits tail makes chewing and swallowing\\nmotions as if it were also"
" eating."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon herbivore se nourrit d’herbes\\net de pousses d’arbres. Quand il "
"mange, sa\\nqueue se met à bouger comme si elle\\nétait aussi en train de "
"mâcher."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1131
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1277
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4448
msgid "FARIGIRAF"
msgstr "FARIGIRAF"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4454
msgid ""
"Now that the brain waves from the\\nhead and tail are synced up, "
"the\\npsychic power of this Pokémon is 10\\ntimes stronger than Girafarig's."
msgstr ""
"Les ondes cérébrales de sa tête et de\\nsa queue étant synchronisées, "
"ses\\npouvoirs psychiques sont 10 fois plus\\nforts que ceux de Girafarig."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6806
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4514
msgid "PINECO"
msgstr "POMDEPIK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4517
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4591
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1926
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1996
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2067
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2139
msgid "Bagworm"
msgstr "Ver Caché"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4520
msgid ""
"A Pineco hangs from a tree branch and\\nwaits for prey. While eating, if it "
"is\\ndisturbed by someone shaking its tree, it\\nfalls on the ground and "
"suddenly explodes."
msgstr ""
"Pomdepik s’accroche à une branche d’arbre\\net attend patiemment que sa "
"proie passe.\\nSi quelqu’un secoue son arbre pendant qu’il\\nmange, il tombe"
" au sol et explose."

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4594
msgid ""
"It keeps itself inside its steel shell.\\nThe shell is opened when it is "
"catching\\nprey, but it is so quick that the shell's\\ninside cannot be "
"seen."
msgstr ""
"FORETRESS se cache dans sa carapace en\\nacier trempé. La carapace s’ouvre "
"quand il\\nattrape sa proie, mais cela va si vite\\nqu’il est impossible de "
"voir à l’intérieur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4667
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4742
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4807
msgid "Land Snake"
msgstr "Serpent"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4670
msgid ""
"Its drill-tipped tail is used to burrow into\\nthe ground backwards. This "
"Pokémon is\\nknown to make its nest in complex shapes\\ndeep under the "
"ground."
msgstr ""
"Il a une perceuse au bout de la queue. Il\\nl’utilise pour creuser des "
"souterrains à\\nreculons. On dit que ce Pokémon enfouit\\nson nid aux formes"
" complexes sous terre."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4739
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4804
msgid "DUDUNSPARCE"
msgstr "DEUSOLOURDO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4745
msgid ""
"This Pokémon uses its hard tail to\\nmake its nest by boring holes "
"into\\nbedrock deep underground. The nest\\ncan reach lengths of over six "
"miles."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon creuse la roche profonde\\navec sa queue dure pour faire son "
"nid.\\nCelui-ci peut atteindre plus de\\n10 km de long."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4810
msgid ""
"A recent study uncovered that the\\nnumber of segments a "
"Dudunsparce's\\nbody has is determined by the\\nPokémon's genes."
msgstr ""
"Une étude récente a révélé que le\\nnombre de segments du corps "
"de\\nDeusolourdo dépend de ses gènes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4875
msgid "Fly Scorpion"
msgstr "Scorpivol"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4878
msgid ""
"It glides without making a single sound.\\nIt grasps the face of its foe "
"using its\\nhind and large front claws, then stabs\\nwith its poison barb."
msgstr ""
"Il plane dans les airs sans un bruit. Il\\ns’accroche au visage de son "
"ennemi grâce à\\nses serres et aux pinces de ses pattes\\navant, et pique "
"avec son dard empoisonné."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4724
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4958
msgid "GLISCOR"
msgstr "SCORVOL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4961
msgid "Fang Scorp"
msgstr "Scorpicroc"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:4964
msgid ""
"Gliscor observes prey while hanging\\nupside down from branches. Its flight "
"is\\nsoundless. When the chance presents\\nitself, it swoops!"
msgstr ""
"Il vole sans un bruit, et capture ses\\nproies avec sa queue pour leur "
"infliger\\nune morsure critique."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5040
msgid ""
"By baring its fangs and making a scary\\nface, it sends smaller Pokémon "
"scurrying\\nin terror. The Snubbull does seem a\\nlittle sad at making its "
"foes flee."
msgstr ""
"Il terrorise les Pokémon plus petits que\\nlui en montrant les dents et en "
"faisant\\nune grimace. Cependant, il est toujours un\\npeu triste de voir "
"ses ennemis s’enfuir."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5116
msgid ""
"It has a particularly well-developed lower\\njaw. The huge fangs are heavy, "
"causing\\nit to tilt its head. Unless it is startled,\\nit will not try to "
"bite."
msgstr ""
"Il a une mâchoire inférieure très\\ndéveloppée. Ses crocs sont si "
"lourds\\nqu’ils l’obligent à pencher la tête. Il ne\\nmord jamais sans "
"raison, sauf s’il a peur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5191
msgid ""
"A Qwilfish uses the pressure of water\\nit swallows to shoot toxic quills "
"all at\\nonce from all over its body. It finds\\nswimming to be somewhat "
"challenging."
msgstr ""
"Il se gonfle en aspirant de l’eau. Il utilise\\nla pression de l’eau avalée "
"pour envoyer\\nd’un coup les pointes toxiques de son\\ncorps. Nager lui "
"demande un gros effort."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5263
msgid "QWILFISH-H"
msgstr "QWILFISH-H"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5276
msgid ""
"A form of Qwilfish from the distant past.\\nFishers detest this troublesome "
"Pokémon\\nbecause it sprays poison from its spines,\\ngetting it everywhere."
msgstr ""
"Une forme ancienne de Qwilfish. Les\\npêcheurs détestent ce Pokémon gênant, "
"qui\\nprojette partout le poison de ses épines."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5345
msgid "OVERQWIL"
msgstr "QWILPIK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5348
msgid "Pin Cluster"
msgstr "Épineux"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5351
msgid ""
"Its lancelike spikes and savage\\ntemperament have earned it the\\nnickname "
"“Sea Fiend”.\\nIt slurps up poison to nourish itself."
msgstr ""
"Ses piques acérées et son tempérament\\nféroce lui ont valu le surnom de "
"“Démon des\\nmers”. Il se nourrit du poison qu’il aspire."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5421
msgid "Mold"
msgstr "Pourri"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5424
msgid ""
"A Shuckle hides under rocks, keeping its\\nbody concealed inside its shell "
"while\\neating stored berries. The berries mix with\\nits body fluids to "
"become a juice."
msgstr ""
"Il se cache sous les rochers, abritant son\\ncorps dans sa carapace et mange"
" les baies\\nqu’il a mises de côté. Elles se mélangent à\\nses fluides "
"corporels pour produire du jus."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5491
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5583
msgid "Single Horn"
msgstr "Unicorne"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5494
msgid ""
"They gather in forests seeking the sweet\\nsap of trees. It is completely "
"clad in a\\nsteel-hard shell. It is proud of its horn,\\nwhich it uses to "
"fling foes."
msgstr ""
"Ils se réunissent dans les forêts à la\\nrecherche de sève d’arbre. Il "
"est\\nextrêmement fier de sa corne qu’il utilise\\npour faire voler ses "
"adversaires."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5586
msgid ""
"A tremendous influx of energy builds it up,\\nbut when Mega Evolution ends, "
"Heracross\\nis bothered by terrible soreness in its\\nmuscles."
msgstr ""
"Un afflux d’énergie formidable le\\nrenforce, mais une fois la Méga-"
"Évolution\\nterminée, SCARHINO souffre de terribles\\ncourbatures."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5658
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5750
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5841
msgid "Sharp Claw"
msgstr "Grifacérée"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5661
msgid ""
"A Sneasel scales trees by punching its\\nhooked claws into the bark. It "
"seeks out\\nunguarded nests and steals eggs for food\\nwhile the parents are"
" away."
msgstr ""
"Il grimpe aux arbres en enfonçant ses\\ngriffes crochetées dans l’écorce. "
"Il\\ncherche les nids non surveillés par les\\nparents et vole les œufs pour"
" les manger."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5747
msgid "WEAVILE"
msgstr "DIMORET"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5753
msgid ""
"They travel in groups of four or five,\\nleaving signs for one another on "
"trees\\nand rocks. They bring down their prey\\nwith coordinated attacks."
msgstr ""
"Ils chassent en hordes. Grâce à leur\\nbonne coordination, ils "
"peuvent\\naisément venir à bout de grands\\nPokémon comme Mammochon."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5831
msgid "SNEASEL-H"
msgstr "FARFURET-H"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5844
msgid ""
"Its sturdy, curved claws are ideal for\\ntraversing precipitous cliffs. From"
" the\\ntips of these claws drips a venom that\\ninfiltrates the nerves of "
"any prey caught."
msgstr ""
"Ses griffes robustes et recourbées sont\\nidéales pour escalader les "
"falaises. Leur\\npointe distille un venin qui s’attaque aux\\nnerfs de ses "
"proies."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5926
msgid "SNEASLER"
msgstr "FARFUREX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5929
msgid "Free Climb"
msgstr "Grimpeur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5932
msgid ""
"Because of its wicked poison and daunting\\nphysical prowess, no other "
"species could\\nhope to best it on frozen highlands. It\\nprefers solitude "
"and doesn't form packs."
msgstr ""
"Grâce à son poison redoutable et à sa\\nforce physique, nul ne peut le "
"vaincre sur\\nles hauts plateaux gelés. Il préfère la\\nsolitude à la meute."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:5998
msgid "TEDDIURSA"
msgstr "TEDDIURSA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6001
msgid "Little Bear"
msgstr "Mini Ours"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6004
msgid ""
"It licks its palms that are sweetened by\\nbeing soaked in honey. A "
"Teddiursa makes\\nits own honey by blending fruits and pollen\\ncollected by"
" Beedrill."
msgstr ""
"Il aime se lécher les paumes quand elles\\nsont encore pleines de miel. Il "
"concocte\\nson propre miel en mélangeant les fruits\\net le pollen ramassés "
"par Dardargnan."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6073
msgid "Hibernator"
msgstr "Hibernant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6076
msgid ""
"In forests, it is said that there are many\\nstreams and towering trees "
"where an\\nUrsaring gathers food. It walks through\\nits forest collecting "
"food every day."
msgstr ""
"On dit que les Ursaring trouvent leur\\nnourriture dans les cours d’eau et "
"les\\ngrands arbres des forêts. Ils errent dans\\nla forêt pour chercher de "
"la nourriture."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3887
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4106
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6156
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6220
msgid "URSALUNA"
msgstr "URSAKING"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6159
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6223
msgid "Peat"
msgstr "Tourbe"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6162
msgid ""
"Swampy terrain gives Ursaluna its burly\\nphysique and newfound capacity "
"to\\nmanipulate peat at will."
msgstr ""
"Les terrains marécageux ont donné à\\nUrsaking son physique robuste et "
"la\\ncapacité nouvelle de manipuler la\\ntourbe à sa guise."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6226
msgid ""
"It crossed the sea and drifted\\nashore in a new land. Surviving in "
"this\\nplace led it to take on a unique\\nappearance and gain special "
"powers."
msgstr ""
"Il a traversé la mer et s’est échoué\\nsur une terre inconnue. Survivre en "
"ce\\nlieu lui a donné une apparence unique\\net des pouvoirs spéciaux."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6287
msgid "SLUGMA"
msgstr "LIMAGMA"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Lave
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6290
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6368
msgid "Lava"
msgstr "Lava"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6293
msgid ""
"It is a species of Pokémon that lives in\\nvolcanic areas. If its body "
"cools, its skin\\nhardens and immobilizes it. To avoid that,\\nit sleeps "
"near magma."
msgstr ""
"Cette espèce de Pokémon vit dans les\\nzones volcaniques. Si son corps "
"refroidit,\\nsa peau durcit et l’immobilise. C’est pour\\ncette raison qu’il"
" dort près de la lave."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6371
msgid ""
"The shell on its back is made of hardened\\nmagma. Tens of thousands of "
"years spent\\nliving in volcanic craters have turned\\nMagcargo's bodies "
"into magma."
msgstr ""
"La carapace sur son dos est faite de magma\\ndurci. Des dizaines de milliers"
" d’années\\npassées dans les cratères volcaniques ont\\ntransformé son corps"
" en magma."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6440
msgid "SWINUB"
msgstr "MARCACRIN"

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6443
msgid "Pig"
msgstr "Cochon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6446
msgid ""
"It roots for food by rubbing its snout\\nagainst the ground. Its favorite "
"food is a\\nmushroom that grows under dried grass.\\nIt occasionally roots "
"out hot springs."
msgstr ""
"Il cherche à manger en reniflant le sol.\\nSon mets préféré est un "
"champignon\\nqui pousse sous l’herbe fanée. Il découvre\\nparfois des "
"sources d’eau chaude."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6518
msgid "Swine"
msgstr "Porc"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6521
msgid ""
"A Piloswine is covered by a thick coat\\nof long hair for enduring freezing "
"cold.\\nIt uses its tusks to dig up food that has\\nbeen buried under ice."
msgstr ""
"Il est recouvert de longs poils épais lui\\npermettant de supporter le froid"
" hivernal.\\nIl utilise ses défenses pour déterrer la\\nnourriture cachée "
"sous la glace."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6606
msgid "MAMOSWINE"
msgstr "MAMMOCHON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6609
msgid "Twin Tusk"
msgstr "Deudéfenses"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6612
msgid ""
"A frozen Mamoswine was dug from ice\\ndating back 10,000 years. It woke up "
"to\\nmuch amazement. This Pokémon has been\\naround for a long, long, long "
"time."
msgstr ""
"On le retrouve dessiné sur des fresques\\nmurales vieilles de 10 000 ans. On"
" a cru\\npendant un temps que son espèce\\ns’était éteinte."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6698
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6778
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6852
msgid "Coral"
msgstr "Corail"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6701
msgid ""
"Corsola live in warm southern seas.\\nIf the sea becomes polluted, the "
"beautiful\\ncoral stalks become discolored and crumble\\naway in tatters."
msgstr ""
"Corayon vit dans les mers du sud.\\nSi son environnement est pollué, ses "
"belles\\nbranches perdent leur couleur avant de\\ntomber en morceaux."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6768
msgid "CORSOLA-G"
msgstr "CORAYON-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6781
msgid ""
"Sudden climate change wiped out this\\nancient kind of Corsola. With its "
"branches,\\nit absorbs others' life-force. It curses\\nthose unaware that "
"kick it by accident."
msgstr ""
"Ce Corayon ancien a disparu à cause d’un\\nbrusque changement de climat. "
"Ses\\nbranches aspirent la vitalité d’autrui. Il\\nmaudit ceux qui le "
"heurtent."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6849
msgid "CURSOLA"
msgstr "CORAYOME"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6855
msgid ""
"Its shell is overflowing with its\\nheightened otherworldly energy. "
"The\\nectoplasm serves as protection for this\\nPokémon's core spirit."
msgstr ""
"Son énergie spectrale accrue s’est\\nrépandue hors de sa coquille. Il "
"protège\\nl’âme de son noyau avec son corps\\nspirituel."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6922
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6996
msgid "Jet"
msgstr "Jet"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6925
msgid ""
"A Remoraid uses its abdominal muscles\\nto forcefully expel swallowed water,"
" then\\nshoot down flying prey. When evolution\\napproaches, it travels down"
" rivers."
msgstr ""
"Il aspire de l’eau qu’il recrache à forte\\npression sur les proies "
"volantes, grâce à\\nses muscles abdominaux. Avant d’évoluer,\\nil descend le"
" courant des rivières."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:6999
msgid ""
"It ensnares its foe with its suction-\\ncupped tentacles before delivering "
"the\\nfinishing blow. If the foe turns out to be\\ntoo strong, it spews ink "
"to escape."
msgstr ""
"Octillery attrape son ennemi avec ses\\ntentacules avant de lui asséner le "
"coup\\nfinal. Si l’ennemi s’avère trop fort, il lui\\ncrache de l’encre à la"
" figure et s’échappe."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6030
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7078
msgid "DELIBIRD"
msgstr "CADOIZO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7081
msgid "Delivery"
msgstr "Livraison"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7084
msgid ""
"It carries food bundled up in its tail.\\nThere was a famous explorer "
"who\\nmanaged to scale Mt. Everest thanks\\nto a Delibird sharing its food."
msgstr ""
"Il transporte sa nourriture dans sa queue.\\nUn célèbre explorateur réussit "
"à atteindre\\nle sommet de l’Everest grâce à l’un d’eux,\\nqui partagea sa "
"nourriture avec lui."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7149
msgid "MANTYKE"
msgstr "BABIMANTA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7152
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7230
msgid "Kite"
msgstr "Cervolant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7155
msgid ""
"When it swims close to the surface\\nof the ocean, people aboard ships "
"are\\nable to observe the pattern on its back.\\nIt often swims in a school "
"of Remoraid."
msgstr ""
"Les Babimanta vivant à Galar semblent\\nun peu engourdis. Cela pourrait être"
" dû\\nà la basse température de la mer."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7233
msgid ""
"On sunny days, schools of Mantine can be\\nseen elegantly leaping over the "
"waves.\\nIt is not bothered by the Remoraid that\\nhitches rides."
msgstr ""
"Les jours de beau temps, on peut voir des\\nbancs de Demanta sauter au-"
"dessus des\\nvagues. Le Remoraid qui l’accompagne ne\\ndérange pas ce "
"Pokémon."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7303
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7378
msgid "Armor Bird"
msgstr "Armoiseau"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7306
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that has a body and wings of\\nsteel. People in the past used "
"feathers\\nfallen from Skarmory to make swords and\\nknives."
msgstr ""
"Son corps et ses ailes sont faits d’acier.\\nAutrefois, les hommes "
"utilisaient ses\\nplumes pour fabriquer des épées et\\ndes couteaux."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7381
msgid ""
"Due to the effects of Mega Evolution,\\nits pincers have taken a "
"more\\ndiabolical form, ripping anything\\nthey pierce to shreds."
msgstr ""
"Sous l’effet de la Méga-Évolution,\\nses pinces ont pris une forme "
"plus\\ndiabolique et déchiquettent tout ce\\nqu’elles transpercent."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7433
msgid "HOUNDOUR"
msgstr "MALOSSE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7439
msgid ""
"Houndour communicate with each other\\nusing a variety of cries to corner "
"their\\nprey. This Pokémon's remarkable teamwork\\nis simply unparalleled."
msgstr ""
"Les Malosse chassent en meute organisée.\\nIls communiquent grâce à une "
"série de\\npetits cris et encerclent ainsi leur proie.\\nLeur travail "
"d’équipe est remarquable."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7507
msgid ""
"In a Houndoom pack, the one with its horns\\nraked sharply back serves a "
"leadership\\nrole. They choose their leader by fighting\\namong themselves."
msgstr ""
"Dans une meute de Demolosse, le\\nleader est doté de cornes inclinées "
"vers\\nl’arrière. Ces Pokémon choisissent leur\\nchef en organisant des "
"combats entre eux."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7593
msgid ""
"Its red claws and the tips of its tail are\\nmelting from high internal "
"temperatures\\nthat are painful to Houndoom itself.\\n"
msgstr ""
"Ses griffes rouges et le bout de sa\\nqueue fondent à cause de "
"sa\\ntempérature interne élevée, qui fait\\nsouffrir DEMOLOSSE lui-même.\\n"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7658
msgid "PHANPY"
msgstr "PHANPY"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7661
msgid "Long Nose"
msgstr "Long-Nez"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7664
msgid ""
"Phanpy's big ears serve as broad fans.\\nWhen it becomes hot, it flaps the "
"ears\\nbusily to cool down. Even the young are\\nvery strong."
msgstr ""
"Phanpy utilise ses oreilles comme de\\ngros éventails. Quand il fait chaud, "
"il les\\nsecoue tranquillement pour se rafraîchir.\\nMême les jeunes sont "
"très forts."

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7737
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8499
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8574
msgid "Armor"
msgstr "Armure"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7740
msgid ""
"A Donphan is so strong it can easily haul\\na dump truck. Its hide has "
"toughened to a\\nrock-hard state. An ordinary sort of\\nattack won't even "
"leave a scratch."
msgstr ""
"Il est si fort qu’il peut facilement\\nsoulever un gros camion. Sa peau "
"est\\naussi dure que la pierre et une attaque\\nordinaire n’arriverait pas à"
" l’égratigner."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5642
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8183
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7820
msgid "STANTLER"
msgstr "CERFROUSSE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7823
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7895
msgid "Big Horn"
msgstr "Maxi Corne"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7826
msgid ""
"Stantler's magnificent antlers were\\nonce traded at high prices as works of"
" art.\\nAs a result, this Pokémon was hunted\\nclose to extinction."
msgstr ""
"Les superbes bois de Cerfrousse\\nétaient vendus très cher comme "
"œuvres\\nd’art. Ce Pokémon fut chassé et l’espèce\\nproche de l’extinction à"
" cause de ses bois."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3979
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7892
msgid "WYRDEER"
msgstr "CERBYLLIN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7898
msgid ""
"The black orbs shine with an uncanny light\\nwhen it is erecting invisible "
"barriers.\\nThe fur shed from its beard retains heat\\nand is useful for "
"winter clothing."
msgstr ""
"Ses orbes noirs brillent d’une lueur\\nétrange quand il érige des "
"barrières\\ninvisibles. Les poils de sa barbe gardent\\nla chaleur et "
"servent aux habits d’hiver."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1567
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2947
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2967
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2987
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3007
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3027
msgid "SMEARGLE"
msgstr "QUEULORIOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7966
msgid "Painter"
msgstr "Peintre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:7969
msgid ""
"A Smeargle marks its territory using a\\nfluid that leaks out from the tip "
"of its\\ntail. About 5,000 different marks left by\\nthis Pokémon have been "
"found."
msgstr ""
"Il délimite son territoire en libérant un\\nfluide corporel qui sort de sa "
"queue. On a\\ndécouvert plus de 5 000 traces de fluide\\ndifférentes "
"laissées par ce Pokémon."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8043
msgid "Milk Cow"
msgstr "Vachalait"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8046
msgid ""
"It gives over five gallons of milk daily.\\nIts sweet milk is enjoyed by "
"children and\\ngrown-ups alike. People who can't drink\\nmilk turn it into "
"yogurt and eat it instead."
msgstr ""
"ECREMEUH produit plus de 20 litres de\\nlait par jour. Son lait sucré fait "
"la joie\\ndes petits et des grands. Les gens qui\\nne boivent pas de lait en"
" font du yaourt."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7251
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8120
msgid "RAIKOU"
msgstr "RAIKOU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8126
msgid ""
"Raikou embodies the speed of lightning.\\nIts roars send shock waves "
"shuddering\\nthrough the air and ground as if\\nlightning bolts were "
"crashing down."
msgstr ""
"Raikou incarne la vitesse de l’éclair. Les\\nrugissements de ce Pokémon "
"libèrent des\\nondes de choc provenant du ciel, frappant\\nle sol avec la "
"puissance de la foudre."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2900
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8019
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8202
msgid "ENTEI"
msgstr "ENTEI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8208
msgid ""
"Entei embodies the passion of magma.\\nIt is thought to have been born in "
"the\\neruption of a volcano. It blasts fire that\\nconsumes all that it "
"touches."
msgstr ""
"Entei incarne la colère du magma. Il\\nserait né suite à l’éruption d’un "
"volcan. Il\\npeut envoyer d’énormes jets de flammes\\nqui calcinent tout ce "
"qu’ils touchent."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2768
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8145
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8283
msgid "SUICUNE"
msgstr "SUICUNE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8289
msgid ""
"Suicune embodies the compassion of\\na pure spring of water. It runs "
"across\\nthe land with gliding elegance. It has the\\npower to purify dirty "
"water."
msgstr ""
"Suicune incarne la tranquillité d’une\\nsource d’eau pure. Il parcourt les "
"plaines\\navec grâce. Ce Pokémon a le pouvoir de\\npurifier l’eau."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8353
msgid "LARVITAR"
msgstr "EMBRYLEX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8356
msgid "Rock Skin"
msgstr "Peaupierre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8359
msgid ""
"A Larvitar is born deep under the ground.\\nIt must eat its way through the "
"soil above\\nand reach the surface for it to see its\\nparents' faces."
msgstr ""
"Il naît sous terre. Pour remonter à la\\nsurface, il doit manger la terre "
"au-dessus\\nde lui. Jusqu’à ce qu’il y parvienne, il ne\\npeut pas voir le "
"visage de ses parents."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8423
msgid "PUPITAR"
msgstr "YMPHECT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8426
msgid "Hard Shell"
msgstr "Carapadure"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8429
msgid ""
"A Pupitar creates a gas inside its body\\nthat it ejects under compression "
"to propel\\nitself like a jet. Its body can withstand\\na collision with "
"solid steel."
msgstr ""
"Ymphect crée un gaz qu’il comprime\\npuissamment pour se propulser. Son "
"corps\\nest très solide. Il ne l’endommage pas même\\nlorsqu’il frappe de "
"l’acier trempé."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8502
msgid ""
"A Tyranitar is so overwhelmingly powerful,\\nit can bring down a whole "
"mountain to make\\nits nest. It roams in mountains seeking\\nnew opponents "
"to fight."
msgstr ""
"Tyranocif est si puissant qu’il peut\\nabattre une montagne pour y faire son"
" nid.\\nIl se promène dans les montagnes pour y\\ntrouver de nouveaux "
"adversaires."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8577
msgid ""
"Due to the colossal power poured into it,\\nthis Pokémon's back split right "
"open. Its\\ndestructive instincts are the only thing\\nkeeping it moving."
msgstr ""
"La puissance colossale qui l’a envahi a\\nfendu son dos. Seul son "
"instinct\\ndestructeur le fait encore avancer."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8649
msgid "LUGIA"
msgstr "LUGIA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8652
msgid "Diving"
msgstr "Plongeon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8655
msgid ""
"Lugia is so powerful even a light\\nfluttering of its wings can blow "
"apart\\nhouses. As a result, it chooses to live out\\nof sight deep under "
"the sea."
msgstr ""
"Ses ailes ont une puissance dévastatrice.\\nUn simple battement de celles-ci"
" peut\\ndétruire des petites maisons. Il vit loin de\\ntout, dans les "
"profondeurs océaniques."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8740
msgid "HO-OH"
msgstr "HO-OH"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Arcenciel
#: src/battle_debug.c:418 src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8743
msgid "Rainbow"
msgstr "Rainbow"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8746
msgid ""
"Its feathers--which glow in seven colors\\ndepending on the angle at which "
"they are\\nstruck by light--are thought to bring joy.\\nIt is said to live "
"at the foot of a rainbow."
msgstr ""
"Ses plumes brillent de sept couleurs selon\\nl’orientation par rapport à la "
"lumière. On\\ndit qu’elles portent bonheur et que ce\\nPOKéMON vit au pied "
"d’un arc-en-ciel."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8820
msgid "CELEBI"
msgstr "CELEBI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8823
msgid "Time Travel"
msgstr "Temporel"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_2_families.h:8826
msgid ""
"This Pokémon came from the future by\\ncrossing over time. It is thought "
"that so\\nlong as Celebi appears, a bright and\\nshining future awaits us."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon est venu du futur en voyageant\\ndans le temps. On raconte que "
"tant que\\nCelebi apparaît, cela signifie que le\\nfutur sera bon et "
"agréable."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:26
msgid "TREECKO"
msgstr "ARCKO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:29
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:100
msgid "Wood Gecko"
msgstr "Bois Gecko"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:32
msgid ""
"It makes its nest in a giant tree in the\\nforest. It ferociously guards "
"against\\nanything nearing its territory. It is said\\nto be the protector "
"of the forest's trees."
msgstr ""
"Il fait son nid dans les arbres géants et\\nprotège férocement son "
"territoire de tout\\nce qui s’en approche. On dit qu’il est le\\nprotecteur "
"des arbres de la forêt."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3286
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:97
msgid "GROVYLE"
msgstr "MASSKO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:103
msgid ""
"Leaves grow out of this Pokémon's body.\\nThey help obscure a Grovyle from "
"the eyes\\nof its enemies while it is in a thickly\\novergrown forest."
msgstr ""
"De grandes feuilles poussent sur le dos\\nde ce Pokémon. Il les utilise pour"
" se\\ncacher de ses ennemis quand il se trouve\\ndans une végétation "
"luxuriante."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:634
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:173
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:243
msgid "SCEPTILE"
msgstr "JUNGKO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:176
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:250
msgid "Forest"
msgstr "Forêt"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:179
msgid ""
"In the jungle, its power is without equal.\\nThis Pokémon carefully grows "
"trees and\\nplants. It regulates its body temperature\\nby basking in "
"sunlight."
msgstr ""
"Dans la jungle, sa force est sans égale.\\nCe Pokémon prend grand soin des "
"arbres\\net des plantes. Il régule sa température\\ncorporelle en se "
"prélassant au soleil."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:253
msgid ""
"Thanks to the power in its quick legs,\\nMega Sceptile can be on its "
"opponent in a\\nflash. It can cut off a portion of its tail\\nto fire it "
"like a missile at an opponent."
msgstr ""
"Grâce à ses pattes rapides, MEGA-JUNGKO\\nfond sur l’ennemi en un éclair. Il"
" peut\\ndétacher un bout de sa queue pour le\\nlancer comme un missile."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:319
msgid "TORCHIC"
msgstr "POUSSIFEU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:322
msgid "Chick"
msgstr "Poussin"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:325
msgid ""
"If attacked, it strikes back by spitting\\nballs of fire it forms in its "
"stomach.\\nA Torchic dislikes darkness because it\\ncan't see its "
"surroundings."
msgstr ""
"S’il est attaqué, il crache des boules de\\nfeu qu’il forme dans son "
"estomac.\\nIl déteste l’obscurité car il aime voir ce\\nqui se trouve autour"
" de lui."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3326
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:404
msgid "COMBUSKEN"
msgstr "GALIFEU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:407
msgid "Young Fowl"
msgstr "Poulet"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:410
msgid ""
"It lashes out with 10 kicks per second.\\nIts strong fighting instinct "
"compels it\\nto keep up its offensive until the\\nopponent gives up."
msgstr ""
"Il peut envoyer jusqu’à 10 coups de pied\\nà la seconde. Son esprit de "
"guerrier le\\npousse à rester sur l’offensive jusqu’à\\nl’abandon de son "
"adversaire."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7597
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:491
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:578
msgid "BLAZIKEN"
msgstr "BRASEGALI"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Ardent
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:494
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:585
msgid "Blaze"
msgstr "Brasier"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:497
msgid ""
"It learns martial arts that use punches\\nand kicks. Every several years, "
"its old\\nfeathers burn off, and new, supple\\nfeathers grow back in their "
"place."
msgstr ""
"Il maîtrise les arts martiaux à base de\\ncoups de pied et de coups de "
"poing. Tous\\nles sept ans, ses vieilles plumes brûlent\\net sont remplacées"
" par des neuves."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:588
msgid ""
"As it unleashes a flurry of savage kicks,\\nits legs can begin to burn from "
"the\\nfriction of the surrounding atmosphere.\\nThey're always a source of "
"pride to it."
msgstr ""
"Quand il déchaîne une rafale de coups de\\npied sauvages, ses jambes "
"peuvent\\ns’enflammer sous la friction de l’air.\\nElles font toute sa "
"fierté."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:654
msgid "MUDKIP"
msgstr "GOBOU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:657
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:728
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:808
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:884
msgid "Mud Fish"
msgstr "Poissonboue"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:660
msgid ""
"On land, it can powerfully lift large\\nboulders by planting its four feet "
"and\\nheaving. It sleeps by burying itself in soil\\nat the water's edge."
msgstr ""
"Sur le sol, il peut facilement tirer de gros\\nrochers grâce à ses "
"puissantes pattes.\\nPour dormir, il creuse des trous au bord\\nde l’eau et "
"s’y installe tranquillement."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3306
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:725
msgid "MARSHTOMP"
msgstr "FLOBIO"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:731
msgid ""
"Its toughened hind legs enable it to stand\\nupright. Because it weakens if "
"its skin\\ndries out, it replenishes fluids by playing\\nin mud."
msgstr ""
"Ses pattes arrière lui permettent de se\\ntenir debout. Comme il ne "
"supporterait\\npas que sa peau s’assèche, il passe son\\ntemps à jouer dans "
"la boue."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:805
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:877
msgid "SWAMPERT"
msgstr "LAGGRON"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:811
msgid ""
"If it senses the approach of a storm and\\na tidal wave, it protects its "
"seaside nest\\nby piling up boulders. It swims as fast as\\na jet ski."
msgstr ""
"S’il sent venir une tempête, il protège\\nson nid au bord de l’eau en "
"empilant de\\ngros rochers. Quand il nage, il est aussi\\nrapide qu’un jet-"
"ski."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:887
msgid ""
"When it Mega Evolves, the strength that it\\nneeds to act in the water is "
"increased.\\nIt can use its tenacious power\\nboth on land and in the water."
msgstr ""
"Quand il méga-évolue, la force qui lui sert\\nà agir dans l’eau augmente. Il"
" peut user de\\nsa puissance tenace sur terre comme dans\\nl’eau."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:966
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1039
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:1919
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:1988
msgid "Bite"
msgstr "Morsure"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:969
msgid ""
"It savagely threatens foes with bared\\nfangs. It chases after fleeing "
"targets\\ntenaciously. It turns tail and runs,\\nhowever, if the foe strikes"
" back."
msgstr ""
"Il menace férocement ses adversaires à\\nl’aide de ses crocs acérés. Il est "
"très\\ntenace mais a tendance à rentrer la queue\\net à fuir si son "
"adversaire riposte."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1036
msgid "MIGHTYENA"
msgstr "GRAHYENA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1042
msgid ""
"In the wild, Mightyena live in a pack.\\nThey never defy their leader's "
"orders.\\nThey defeat foes with perfectly\\ncoordinated teamwork."
msgstr ""
"Dans la nature, les Grahyena vivent en\\nmeute. Ils obéissent toujours aux "
"ordres\\ndu dominant et battent leurs adversaires\\ngrâce à leur travail "
"d’équipe coordonné."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1122
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1279
msgid "Tiny Raccoon"
msgstr "Petit Raton"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1125
msgid ""
"Rubbing its nose against the ground, it\\nalways wanders about back and "
"forth in\\nsearch of something. It is distinguished\\nby the zigzag "
"footprints it leaves."
msgstr ""
"Il erre toujours de droite à gauche le nez\\nplanté dans le sol à la "
"recherche de\\nquelque chose. Il laisse des empreintes\\nen zigzag très "
"caractéristiques."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: data/maps/Route25_BillsHouse_hns/scripts.inc:361
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5571
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1197
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1351
msgid "LINOONE"
msgstr "LINEON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1200
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1359
msgid "Rushing"
msgstr "Fonceur"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1203
msgid ""
"It is exceedingly fast if it only has to run\\nin a straight line. When it "
"spots pond-\\ndwelling prey underwater, it quickly leaps\\nin and catches it"
" with its sharp claws."
msgstr ""
"Il est très rapide quand il s’agit de courir\\nen ligne droite. Quand il "
"aperçoit une proie\\nau fond de l’eau, il bondit dessus et la\\nsaisit de "
"ses griffes acérées."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1269
msgid "ZIGZAGOON-G"
msgstr "ZIGZATON-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1282
msgid ""
"Its restlessness has it constantly moving\\nin zigzags. It will purposely "
"run into other\\nPokémon to start fights. It's thought to\\nbe the oldest "
"form of Zigzagoon."
msgstr ""
"Trop agité, il se déplace sans cesse en\\nzigzag et bouscule exprès les "
"autres\\nPokémon pour se battre. Ce serait la forme\\nla plus ancienne de "
"Zigzaton."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1349
msgid "LINOONE-G"
msgstr "LINEON-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1362
msgid ""
"This very aggressive Pokémon will\\nrecklessly challenge opponents "
"stronger\\nthan itself. It uses its long tongue to\\ntaunt them to then "
"tackle forcefully."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon très agressif défie sans\\nréfléchir des adversaires plus forts "
"que\\nlui. Il les nargue avec sa longue langue\\navant de les charger."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1428
msgid "OBSTAGOON"
msgstr "IXON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1431
msgid "Blocking"
msgstr "Barrage"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1434
msgid ""
"Its voice is staggering in volume.\\nObstagoon has a tendency to take on "
"a\\nthreatening posture and shout--this move\\nis known as Obstruct."
msgstr ""
"Il possède une puissance vocale\\nremarquable. On appelle Blocage "
"sa\\ntechnique qui consiste à intimider l’ennemi\\navec son cri guttural."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1502
msgid "WURMPLE"
msgstr "CHENIPOTTE"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1508
msgid ""
"It sticks to tree branches and eats\\nleaves. The thread it spits from its "
"mouth,\\nwhich becomes gooey when it touches\\nair, slows the movement of "
"its foes."
msgstr ""
"Il s’accroche aux branches des arbres\\net mange leurs feuilles. Le fil "
"qu’il\\nsécrète devient gluant au contact de l’air\\net sert à ralentir ses "
"ennemis."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1573
msgid "SILCOON"
msgstr "ARMULYS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1579
msgid ""
"It prepares for evolution using the\\nenergy it stored while it was a "
"Wurmple.\\nIt keeps watch over the surroundings with\\nits two eyes."
msgstr ""
"Il prépare son évolution en utilisant\\nl’énergie accumulée quand il était "
"un\\nChenipotte. Il est très vigilant\\net surveille sans cesse les "
"alentours."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2277
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1651
msgid "BEAUTIFLY"
msgstr "CHARMILLON"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1657
msgid ""
"Its colorfully patterned wings are its\\nmost prominent feature. It flies "
"through\\nflower-covered fields collecting pollen.\\nIt attacks ferociously "
"when angered."
msgstr ""
"Ses ailes colorées sont son signe\\ndistinctif. Il vole gentiment au-"
"dessus\\ndes champs fleuris mais sait aussi se\\nmontrer féroce s’il est "
"énervé."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1745
msgid "CASCOON"
msgstr "BLINDALYS"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1751
msgid ""
"To avoid detection by its enemies, it hides\\nmotionlessly beneath large "
"leaves and in\\nthe gaps of branches. It also attaches\\ndead leaves to its "
"body for camouflage."
msgstr ""
"Pour éviter d’être repéré, il se cache sans\\nbouger entre les branches des "
"arbres et\\nattache également des feuilles mortes sur\\nlui pour se "
"camoufler."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1833
msgid ""
"It is a nocturnal Pokémon that flies from\\nfields and mountains to the "
"attraction of\\nstreetlights at night. It looses highly\\ntoxic powder from "
"its wings."
msgstr ""
"La nuit venue, ce Pokémon nocturne quitte\\nles champs et les montagnes, "
"attiré par les\\nlumières de la ville. En chemin, il laisse\\ntomber de la "
"poudre toxique de ses ailes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1926
msgid "Water Weed"
msgstr "Aquaplante"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1929
msgid ""
"This Pokémon lives in ponds with clean\\nwater. It is known to ferry small "
"Pokémon\\nacross ponds by carrying them on the\\nbroad leaf on its head."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon vit dans les étangs où l’eau\\nest claire. Il transporte les "
"Pokémon\\nplus petits que lui sur la grande feuille\\nse trouvant sur sa "
"tête."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1994
msgid "LOMBRE"
msgstr "LOMBRE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: data/scripts/debug.inc:748
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:1997
msgid "Jolly"
msgstr "Jovial"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2000
msgid ""
"In the evening, it takes great delight in\\npopping out of rivers and "
"startling people.\\nIt feeds on aquatic moss that grows on\\nrocks in the "
"riverbed."
msgstr ""
"Le soir, il adore surgir des rivières pour\\neffrayer les passants. Il se "
"nourrit de la\\nmousse qui pousse sur les rochers dans\\nle lit des "
"rivières."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1587
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2071
msgid "LUDICOLO"
msgstr "LUDICOLO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2074
msgid "Carefree"
msgstr "Insouciant"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2077
msgid ""
"When it hears festive music, all the cells\\nin its body become stimulated, "
"and it\\nbegins moving in rhythm. It does not\\nquail even when it faces a "
"tough opponent."
msgstr ""
"Quand il entend de la musique festive, tout\\nson corps réagit et il se met "
"à danser en\\nrythme. Il ne tremble jamais, même pas\\ndevant un adversaire "
"redoutable."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2158
msgid "SEEDOT"
msgstr "GRAINIPIOT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2161
msgid "Acorn"
msgstr "Gland"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2164
msgid ""
"It hangs off branches and absorbs\\nnutrients. When it finishes eating, "
"its\\nbody becomes so heavy that it drops to\\nthe ground with a thump."
msgstr ""
"Il s’accroche aux branches et absorbe\\nleurs nutriments. Une fois rassasié,"
" il a\\npris tant de poids qu’il se laisse tomber\\nlourdement sur le sol."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2234
msgid "NUZLEAF"
msgstr "PIFEUIL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2237
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:4554
msgid "Wily"
msgstr "Malin"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2240
msgid ""
"A forest-dwelling Pokémon that is skilled\\nat climbing trees. Its long and "
"pointed\\nnose is its weak point. It loses power if\\nthe nose is gripped."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon habite dans les forêts et est\\ntrès doué pour grimper aux "
"arbres. Son nez\\nlong et pointu est son point faible et il\\nperd ses "
"forces si on l’agrippe."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3119
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2332
msgid "SHIFTRY"
msgstr "TENGALICE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2335
msgid "Wicked"
msgstr "Malveillant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2338
msgid ""
"It is said to arrive on chilly, wintry winds.\\nFeared from long ago as the "
"guardian of\\nforests, this Pokémon lives in a deep\\nforest where people do"
" not venture."
msgstr ""
"On dit qu’il arrive en même temps que\\nles vents glacés de l’hiver. Ce "
"Pokémon\\nest le gardien des forêts où les\\nhumains n’osent pas "
"s’aventurer."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2417
msgid "Tiny Swallow"
msgstr "Minirondel"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2420
msgid ""
"Although it is small, it is very courageous.\\nIt will take on a larger "
"Skarmory on an\\nequal footing. However, its will weakens if\\nit becomes "
"hungry."
msgstr ""
"Petit mais téméraire, il n’hésite pas à\\nse mesurer à un grand Airmure. "
"Mais\\nsa détermination diminue quand il\\ncommence à avoir faim."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8539
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2496
msgid "SWELLOW"
msgstr "HELEDELLE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2499
msgid "Swallow"
msgstr "Avale"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2502
msgid ""
"A Swellow dives upon prey from far above.\\nIt never misses its targets. It "
"takes to\\nthe skies in search of lands with a warm\\nclimate."
msgstr ""
"Heledelle vole très haut dans le ciel\\npour piquer sur ses proies qu’il ne "
"manque\\njamais. Il recherche sans cesse des terres\\nau climat chaud."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2573
msgid "Seagull"
msgstr "Mouette"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2576
msgid ""
"It makes its nest on a sheer cliff at the\\nedge of the sea. It has trouble "
"keeping\\nits wings flapping in flight. Instead, it\\nsoars on updrafts."
msgstr ""
"GOELISE fait son nid sur la paroi des\\nfalaises au bord de la mer. Ayant "
"des\\ndifficultés pour battre des ailes, il aime\\nprofiter des courants "
"ascendants."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2748
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3524
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2651
msgid "PELIPPER"
msgstr "BEKIPAN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2654
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7719
msgid "Water Bird"
msgstr "Oiseaudo"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2657
msgid ""
"It skims the tops of waves as it flies.\\nWhen it spots prey, it uses its "
"large beak\\nto scoop up the victim with water.\\nIt protects its eggs in "
"its beak."
msgstr ""
"Il frôle la surface des vagues quand il\\nvole. Son large bec lui sert à "
"attraper les\\nproies qu’il repère dans l’eau, mais aussi\\nà protéger ses "
"œufs."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2738
msgid "Feeling"
msgstr "Sentiment"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2741
msgid ""
"A Ralts has the power to sense the\\nemotions of people and Pokémon with "
"the\\nhorns on its head. It takes cover if it\\nsenses any hostility."
msgstr ""
"Grâce aux cornes sur sa tête, Tarsal a\\nla faculté de ressentir les "
"émotions des\\ngens et des Pokémon. Il se met à l’abri au\\nmoindre signe "
"d’hostilité."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2804
msgid "KIRLIA"
msgstr "KIRLIA"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2807
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6561
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:5763
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:5828
msgid "Emotion"
msgstr "Emotion"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2810
msgid ""
"A Kirlia has the psychic power to create \\na rip in the dimensions and see "
"into the\\nfuture. It is said to dance with pleasure\\non sunny mornings."
msgstr ""
"Kirlia a la faculté de créer une faille\\nentre les dimensions pour voir "
"dans le\\nfutur. On raconte qu’il danse joyeusement\\nles matins "
"ensoleillés."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:461
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1759
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3939
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5807
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8472
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2882
msgid "GARDEVOIR"
msgstr "GARDEVOIR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2885
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2959
msgid "Embrace"
msgstr "Étreinte"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2888
msgid ""
"It apparently does not feel the pull of\\ngravity because it supports itself"
" with\\npsychic power. It will give its life to\\nprotect its Trainer."
msgstr ""
"Apparemment, il ne ressent pas la force\\nde la gravité car il lévite grâce "
"à ses\\npouvoirs psychiques. Ce Pokémon donnerait\\nsa vie pour sauver son "
"Dresseur."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:2962
msgid ""
"By opening its heart, Mega Gardevoir\\nbecomes able to use tremendous "
"psychic\\npower. The red plate in its chest is said to\\nbe a physical "
"manifestation of its heart."
msgstr ""
"En ouvrant son cœur, MEGA-GARDEVOIR peut\\nutiliser un pouvoir psychique "
"formidable.\\nLa plaque rouge de sa poitrine serait la\\nmanifestation "
"physique de son cœur."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3037
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3106
msgid "GALLADE"
msgstr "GALLAME"

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3040
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3113
msgid "Blade"
msgstr "Lame"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3043
msgid ""
"A master of courtesy and swordsmanship,\\nit fights using extending swords "
"on its\\nelbows when trying to protect someone.\\nIt can sense what its foe "
"is thinking."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon, que l’on surnomme\\n“l’escrimeur”, ne se sert de ses coudes\\nen"
" forme de lames que s’il doit défendre\\nquelque chose."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3116
msgid ""
"Mega Gallade has a knightly appearance.\\nIt can use its psychic power to "
"reshape\\nboth arms into blades simultaneously and\\nfight using a dual-"
"wielding style."
msgstr ""
"MEGA-GALLAME a l’allure d’un chevalier.\\nSon pouvoir psychique change ses "
"deux\\nbras en lames à la fois pour combattre à\\ndeux armes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3184
msgid "SURSKIT"
msgstr "ARAKDO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3187
msgid "Pond Skater"
msgstr "Maresurfeur"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3190
msgid ""
"They gather on puddles after evening\\ndownpours, gliding across the "
"surface\\nof water as if sliding. It secretes honey\\nwith a sweet aroma "
"from its head."
msgstr ""
"Ils se réunissent sur les mares les\\nlendemains d’averses pour y glisser "
"comme\\ns’ils patinaient. La tête d’ARAKDO sécrète\\nun miel à l’arôme "
"agréable."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2297
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3263
msgid "MASQUERAIN"
msgstr "MASKADRA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3266
msgid "Eyeball"
msgstr "Boule Œil"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3269
msgid ""
"It intimidates foes with the large eyelike\\npatterns on its antennae. "
"Because it can't\\nfly if its wings get wet, it shelters itself\\nfrom rain "
"under large trees and eaves."
msgstr ""
"Il intimide ses ennemis à l’aide de ses\\nantennes en forme de gros yeux. Il"
" évite\\nla pluie car ses ailes mouillées seraient\\ntrop lourdes pour qu’il"
" puisse voler."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3352
msgid ""
"It loves to eat damp, composted soil in\\nforests. If you enter a forest "
"after a\\nlong rain, you can see many Shroomish\\nfeasting on composted "
"soil."
msgstr ""
"Il adore se nourrir de compost humide.\\nSi vous allez en forêt après une "
"longue\\naverse, vous trouverez certainement des\\nBalignon en train de se "
"régaler."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:781
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1429
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2728
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3429
msgid "BRELOOM"
msgstr "CHAPIGNON"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3435
msgid ""
"It scatters spores from holes in the cap\\non its head. It loves warm and "
"humid\\nclimates. It feeds on trees and plants in\\nfields and forests."
msgstr ""
"Les trous se trouvant sur sa tête\\ndégagent des spores. Il aime "
"les\\nclimats chauds et humides et se\\nnourrit d’arbres et de plantes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3503
msgid "Slacker"
msgstr "Flâneur"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3506
msgid ""
"It sleeps virtually all day and night long.\\nIt doesn't change its nest its"
" entire life,\\nbut it sometimes travels great distances\\nby swimming in "
"rivers."
msgstr ""
"Il passe tout son temps à dormir, de jour\\ncomme de nuit. Il garde le même "
"nid toute\\nsa vie mais voyage de temps en temps sur\\nde grandes distances "
"en nageant."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6548
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3572
msgid "VIGOROTH"
msgstr "VIGOROTH"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3575
msgid "Wild Monkey"
msgstr "Turbusinge"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3578
msgid ""
"It can't keep still because its blood boils\\nwith energy. It runs through "
"the fields\\nand mountains all day to calm itself. If it\\ndoesn't, it can't"
" sleep at night."
msgstr ""
"Son sang, qui circule énergiquement en lui,\\nl’empêche de rester en place. "
"Il court à\\ntravers les champs et les montagnes pour\\nse calmer et trouver"
" le sommeil."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8320
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3650
msgid "SLAKING"
msgstr "MONAFLEMIT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3653
msgid "Lazy"
msgstr "Fainéant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3656
msgid ""
"Hordes of Slaking gather around trees\\nwhen fruits come into season. They "
"wait\\naround patiently for ripened fruits to fall\\nout of the trees."
msgstr ""
"Des hordes de Monaflemit se réunissent\\naux pieds des arbres à la saison "
"des\\nfruits. Ils attendent alors patiemment\\nqu’ils tombent pour pouvoir "
"les manger."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3727
msgid "Trainee"
msgstr "Apprenti"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3730
msgid ""
"It makes its nest at the roots of a mighty\\ntree. Using its whiskerlike "
"antennae, it\\nprobes its surroundings in the\\npitch-black darkness of "
"soil."
msgstr ""
"Il fait son nid aux pieds des arbres\\nimposants. A l’aide de ses "
"antennes,\\nil sonde son environnement dans\\nl’obscurité des sous-sols."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:574
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3800
msgid "NINJASK"
msgstr "NINJASK"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3803
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:718
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:780
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:843
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:919
msgid "Ninja"
msgstr "Ninja"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3806
msgid ""
"Because it darts about vigorously at high\\nspeed, it is very difficult to "
"see. Hearing\\nits distinctive cries for too long induces\\na headache."
msgstr ""
"Comme il se déplace très rapidement,\\nil est très difficile à apercevoir. "
"On peut\\nattraper des maux de tête si on écoute\\nson cri distinctif trop "
"longtemps."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3883
msgid "SHEDINJA"
msgstr "MUNJA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3886
msgid "Shed"
msgstr "Exuvie"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3889
msgid ""
"A peculiar Pokémon that floats in air even\\nthough its wings remain "
"completely still.\\nThe inside of its body is hollow and\\nutterly dark."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon étrange flotte dans les airs\\nmême si ses ailes restent "
"immobiles.\\nL’intérieur de son corps est creux et\\ntotalement sombre."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6468
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3955
msgid "WHISMUR"
msgstr "CHUCHMUR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3958
msgid "Whisper"
msgstr "Chuchoteur"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:3961
msgid ""
"Its cries equal a jet plane in volume.\\nIt inhales through its ear canals. "
"Because\\nof this system, it can cry continually\\nwithout having to catch "
"its breath."
msgstr ""
"Ses cris sont aussi bruyants qu’un avion\\nà réaction. Comme il inhale par "
"ses oreilles,\\nil est capable de crier continuellement\\nsans reprendre sa "
"respiration."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1957
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4031
msgid "LOUDRED"
msgstr "RAMBOUM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4034
msgid "Big Voice"
msgstr "Grosse Voix"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4037
msgid ""
"It positions the round speakers on its\\nhead to assail foes with ultrasonic"
" waves\\nat massive volume. It builds power by\\nstomping the ground."
msgstr ""
"Il utilise les haut-parleurs sur sa tête\\npour attaquer ses adversaires à "
"coup\\nd’ondes ultrasoniques. Il concentre sa\\nforce en piétinant le sol."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4365
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6347
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8838
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4109
msgid "EXPLOUD"
msgstr "BROUHABAM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4112
msgid "Loud Noise"
msgstr "Bruit Sourd"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4115
msgid ""
"It has sound-generating organs all over\\nits body. It communicates with "
"others by\\nadjusting the tone and volume of the cries\\nit emits."
msgstr ""
"Sur tout le corps, il possède des organes\\npouvant générer du son. Il "
"communique\\nen ajustant la tonalité et le volume des\\ncris qu’il émet."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4179
msgid "MAKUHITA"
msgstr "MAKUHITA"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Tenace
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4182
msgid "Guts"
msgstr "Cran"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4185
msgid ""
"It loves to toughen up its body above all\\nelse. If you hear quaking "
"rumbles in a cave,\\nit is the sound of Makuhita undertaking\\nstrenuous "
"training."
msgstr ""
"Il adore muscler son corps plus que tout\\nau monde. Si vous entendez "
"des\\ngrognements dans une grotte, c’est qu’un\\nMakuhita est en train de "
"s’y entraîner."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:701
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4255
msgid "HARIYAMA"
msgstr "HARIYAMA"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Cogneur
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4258
msgid "Arm Thrust"
msgstr "Cogne"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4261
msgid ""
"It has the habit of challenging others\\nwithout hesitation to tests of "
"strength.\\nIt's been known to stand on train tracks\\nand stop trains using"
" forearm thrusts."
msgstr ""
"Sans hésitation, il défie ceux qu’il croise\\npour tester leur force. Il est"
" connu pour\\npouvoir arrêter un train en marche à la\\nseule force de ses "
"bras."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4326
msgid "NOSEPASS"
msgstr "TARINOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4329
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4409
msgid "Compass"
msgstr "Boussole"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4332
msgid ""
"Its body emits a powerful magnetism.\\nIt feeds on prey that is pulled in by"
" the\\nforce. Its magnetism is stronger in cold\\nseasons."
msgstr ""
"Son corps émet un puissant magnétisme.\\nIl se nourrit des proies qu’il "
"attire par\\ncette force. Ce magnétisme est encore\\nplus fort les saisons "
"froides."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4198
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4406
msgid "PROBOPASS"
msgstr "TARINORME"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#. SoulSilver (approché) : Il dirige par magnétisme 3 petites\nunités appelées
#. Mini-nez qui lui\lpermettent d’attaquer de 3 côtés.
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4412
msgid ""
"It freely controls three units called\\nMini-Noses using magnetic "
"force.\\nWith them, it can attack its foes from\\nthree directions."
msgstr ""
"Il utilise ses trois petites unités pour\\ncombattre ses ennemis et capturer"
" ses\\nproies. Le reste de son corps se\\ncontente de donner des ordres."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1091
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3438
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5602
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4483
msgid "SKITTY"
msgstr "SKITTY"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4486
msgid "Kitten"
msgstr "Chaton"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4489
msgid ""
"A Skitty's adorably cute behavior makes it\\nhighly popular. In battle, it "
"makes its tail\\npuff out. It threatens foes with a sharp\\ngrowl."
msgstr ""
"Le côté adorable de Skitty en fait un\\nPokémon très apprécié. En combat, "
"il\\nhérisse sa queue et menace ses\\nadversaires d’un miaulement aigu."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4563
msgid "DELCATTY"
msgstr "DELCATTY"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4566
msgid "Prim"
msgstr "Guindé"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4569
msgid ""
"Rather than keeping a permanent lair,\\nit habitually seeks comfortable "
"spots and\\nsleeps there. It is nocturnal and becomes\\nactive at dusk."
msgstr ""
"Plutôt que d’avoir un endroit bien à lui,\\nil préfère chercher des "
"endroits\\nconfortables et s’y reposer. Ce Pokémon\\ndevient actif à la "
"tombée de la nuit."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6175
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4638
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4712
msgid "SABLEYE"
msgstr "TENEFIX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4644
msgid ""
"It digs branching holes in caves using its\\nsharp claws in search of food--"
"raw gems.\\nA Sableye lurks in darkness and is seen\\nonly rarely."
msgstr ""
"Il creuse dans les grottes à la recherche\\nde pierres précieuses, dont il "
"se nourrit.\\nLes Tenefix restent dans l’obscurité\\nà l’abri des regards."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4722
msgid ""
"Bathed in the energy of Mega Evolution,\\nthe gemstone on its chest expands,"
" rips\\nthrough its skin, and falls out."
msgstr ""
"Baignée dans l’énergie de la\\nMéga-Évolution, la gemme de sa "
"poitrine\\ngrossit, déchire sa peau et tombe."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3099
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4795
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4871
msgid "MAWILE"
msgstr "MYSDIBULE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4798
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4878
msgid "Deceiver"
msgstr "Trompeur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4801
msgid ""
"Its giant jaws are actually steel horns\\nthat transformed. It fools foes "
"into\\ncomplacency with its adorable gestures,\\nthen chomps them with its "
"huge jaws."
msgstr ""
"Ses mâchoires géantes sont en fait ce qui\\nreste de deux cornes en acier "
"qui se sont\\ntransformées. Il attire ses proies avec\\nson air amical avant"
" de les avaler."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4881
msgid ""
"Its two sets of jaws thrash about\\nviolently as if they each had a will "
"of\\ntheir own. One gnash from them can turn a\\nboulder to dust."
msgstr ""
"Ses deux paires de mâchoires s’agitent\\nviolemment comme si elles "
"avaient\\nchacune leur volonté. Une seule morsure\\nréduit un rocher en "
"poussière."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4949
msgid "ARON"
msgstr "GALEKID"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4952
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5024
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5101
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5176
msgid "Iron Armor"
msgstr "Armurfer"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:4955
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that is clad in steel armor.\\nA new suit of armor is made when it"
" evolves.\\nThe old, discarded armor is salvaged as\\nmetal for making iron "
"products."
msgstr ""
"Il est recouvert d’une armure en acier.\\nQuand il évolue, il en revêt une "
"nouvelle\\net abandonne l’ancienne. Celle-ci est très\\nrecherchée par "
"l’industrie sidérurgique."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5021
msgid "LAIRON"
msgstr "GALEGON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5027
msgid ""
"When two Lairon meet in the wild, they\\nfight for territory by bashing into"
" each\\nother with their steel bodies. The sound\\nof their collision "
"carries for miles."
msgstr ""
"Quand deux Galegon se rencontrent,\\nils se battent pour leur territoire "
"en\\nse fonçant dessus. On peut entendre\\nces affrontements à des "
"kilomètres."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3787
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5098
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5169
msgid "AGGRON"
msgstr "GALEKING"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5104
msgid ""
"Its iron horns grow longer a little at\\na time. They are used to determine "
"the\\nAggron's age. The gouges in its armor are\\nworn with pride as "
"mementos from battles."
msgstr ""
"Sa corne de fer grandit doucement au fil\\ndu temps et peut servir à deviner"
" son âge.\\nIl conserve fièrement les marques sur son\\narmure comme "
"souvenir de ses combats."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5179
msgid ""
"When Aggron Mega Evolves into\\nMega Aggron, the destructive ability "
"of\\nits fearsome horns can turn a steel-clad\\ntank into so much scrap "
"metal."
msgstr ""
"Quand GALEKING méga-évolue en\\nMEGA-GALEKING, ses cornes "
"redoutables\\npeuvent réduire un char blindé à l’état\\nde ferraille."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5192
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5245
msgid "MEDITITE"
msgstr "MEDITIKKA"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Méditation
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5248
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5330
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5421
msgid "Meditate"
msgstr "Yoga"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5251
msgid ""
"It continually meditates for hours every\\nday. As a result of rigorous and "
"dedicated\\nyoga training, it has tempered its\\nspiritual power so much it "
"can fly."
msgstr ""
"Il médite sans s’arrêter plusieurs heures\\npar jour. Grâce à cette "
"discipline, il est\\nmaintenant capable de léviter par la force\\nde son "
"esprit."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:721
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5622
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5327
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5414
msgid "MEDICHAM"
msgstr "CHARMINA"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5333
msgid ""
"Through crushingly harsh yoga training, it\\ngained the power to foretell "
"its foe's\\nactions. It battles with elegant, dance-\\nlike movement."
msgstr ""
"Grâce à sa pratique du yoga, CHARMINA\\nest capable de prédire les actions "
"de ses\\nennemis. Quand il se bat, il donne\\nl’impression d’être en train "
"de danser."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5424
msgid ""
"It uses its amped-up willpower to create\\nadditional arms for itself. The "
"more it\\nhas trained its spirit, the more realistic\\nand dexterous these "
"arms become."
msgstr ""
"Sa volonté décuplée lui permet de se\\ncréer des bras supplémentaires. Plus "
"il\\nentraîne son esprit, plus ces bras sont\\nréalistes et habiles."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2125
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5490
msgid "ELECTRIKE"
msgstr "DYNAVOLT"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5496
msgid ""
"It generates electricity using friction\\nfrom the atmosphere. In seasons "
"with\\nespecially arid air, its entire body blazes\\nwith violent showers of"
" sparks."
msgstr ""
"Il génère de l’électricité en utilisant la\\nfriction de l’air. Les "
"saisons\\nparticulièrement sèches, son corps entier\\ncrée de violentes "
"gerbes d’étincelles."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:614
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3672
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7232
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5561
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5633
msgid "MANECTRIC"
msgstr "ELECSPRINT"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Décharge
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5564
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5640
msgid "Discharge"
msgstr "Coup d’Jus"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5567
msgid ""
"Because lightning falls in their vicinities,\\nManectric were thought to "
"have been born\\nfrom lightning. In battle, they create\\nthunderclouds."
msgstr ""
"Comme l’orage gronde souvent autour\\nd’eux, les gens ont longtemps pensé "
"que\\nles Elecsprint naissaient de la foudre."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5643
msgid ""
"Too much electricity has built up in its\\nbody, irritating Manectric. Its "
"explosive\\nspeed is equal to that of a lightning bolt."
msgstr ""
"Trop d’électricité s’est accumulée dans\\nson corps, ce qui irrite "
"ELECSPRINT. Sa\\nvitesse explosive égale celle de la\\nfoudre."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5404
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6949
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5713
msgid "PLUSLE"
msgstr "POSIPI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5716
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5793
msgid "Cheering"
msgstr "Acclameur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5719
msgid ""
"It has the trait of cheering on its fellow\\nPokémon. By shorting out the "
"electricity\\nit releases from its paws, it creates\\npom-poms for cheering."
msgstr ""
"Il est connu pour adorer encourager ses\\nsemblables. Pour les motiver, il "
"fait\\njaillir en rythme de l’électricité par ses\\npetites pattes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5344
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7019
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5790
msgid "MINUN"
msgstr "NEGAPI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5796
msgid ""
"At a meeting of Pokémon academics, it was\\nannounced that simultaneous "
"exposure to\\nelectricity from a Plusle and Minun will\\npromote circulation"
" and boost vitality."
msgstr ""
"Il a été récemment découvert qu’être\\nexposé simultanément au courant "
"d’un\\nPosipi et d’un Negapi favorise la\\ncirculation et augmente la "
"vitalité."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:893
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6968
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5869
msgid "VOLBEAT"
msgstr "MUCIOLE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5872
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5955
msgid "Firefly"
msgstr "Luciole"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5875
msgid ""
"With their taillights lit, Volbeat fly in\\na swarm, drawing geometric "
"designs in the\\nnight sky. They move their nests if their\\npond water "
"becomes dirty."
msgstr ""
"Les Muciole volent et dessinent des\\nfigures géométriques dans le ciel à "
"l’aide\\nde la lumière sur leur queue. Ils changent\\nd’étang si l’eau n’est"
" pas assez propre."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:873
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6508
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7038
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5952
msgid "ILLUMISE"
msgstr "LUMIVOLE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:5958
msgid ""
"A nocturnal Pokémon that becomes active\\nupon nightfall. It leads a Volbeat"
" swarm\\nto draw patterns in the night sky. Over 200\\ndifferent patterns "
"have been confirmed."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon devient actif à la tombée de\\nla nuit et dirige les Muciole pour"
" dessiner\\ndes figures dans le ciel. Plus de 200\\nfigures ont été "
"recensées."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6027
msgid "BUDEW"
msgstr "ROZBOUTON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6030
msgid "Bud"
msgstr "Bourgeon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6033
msgid ""
"Over the winter, it closes its bud and\\nendures the cold. Sensitive to "
"changing\\ntemperature, the bud is said to bloom\\nwhen it feels the sun's "
"warm touch."
msgstr ""
"Plus l’eau dont il se nourrit est pure,\\nplus le niveau de toxicité du "
"pollen\\nqu’il répand est élevé."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5364
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6099
msgid "ROSELIA"
msgstr "ROSELIA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6102
msgid "Thorn"
msgstr "Épine"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6105
msgid ""
"A Roselia that drinks nutritionally rich\\nspringwater blooms with lovely "
"flowers.\\nThe fragrance of its flowers has the\\neffect of making its foes "
"careless."
msgstr ""
"Un Roselia qui boit de l’eau riche en\\nnutriments donnera de jolies "
"fleurs.\\nL’odeur qu’elles dégagent a tendance à\\ndéconcentrer ses "
"adversaires."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1409
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4425
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6194
msgid "ROSERADE"
msgstr "ROSERADE"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6197
msgid "Bouquet"
msgstr "Bouquet"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6200
msgid ""
"Its sweet aroma attracts prey.\\nWith the movements of a dancer,\\nit "
"strikes with whips that are densely\\nlined with poison thorns."
msgstr ""
"Après avoir troublé les sens de ses\\nadversaires avec le parfum exquis "
"de\\nses fleurs, il les frappe violemment\\navec ses fouets ornés d’épines."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6278
msgid "GULPIN"
msgstr "GLOUPTI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6281
msgid "Stomach"
msgstr "Estomac"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6284
msgid ""
"This Pokémon's stomach fluid can even\\ndigest scrap iron. In one gulp, it "
"can\\nswallow something that is as large as\\nitself."
msgstr ""
"L’estomac de ce Pokémon peut même\\ndigérer des morceaux de métal.\\nD’une "
"bouchée, il peut avaler quelque\\nchose d’aussi gros que lui."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6364
msgid "SWALOT"
msgstr "AVALTOUT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6367
msgid "Poison Bag"
msgstr "Sac Poison"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6370
msgid ""
"Its powerful stomach acid is capable of\\ndigesting almost anything. The one"
" thing\\nin the whole world a Swalot can't digest is\\nits own stomach."
msgstr ""
"L’acide de son estomac peut dissoudre\\npresque tout. La seule chose qu’il "
"ne\\npuisse pas dissoudre est l’estomac de\\nce Pokémon."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6451
msgid "Savage"
msgstr "Féroce"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6454
msgid ""
"Carvanha attack ships in swarms, making\\nthem sink. Although it is said to "
"be a very\\nvicious Pokémon, it timidly flees as soon\\nas it finds itself "
"alone."
msgstr ""
"Les Carvanha unissent leurs forces\\npour faire couler les bateaux. Ils "
"sont\\ntrès méchants en groupe mais fuient\\ntimidement dès qu’ils se "
"retrouvent seuls."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6524
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6601
msgid "SHARPEDO"
msgstr "SHARPEDO"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6527
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6608
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12523
msgid "Brutal"
msgstr "Brutal"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6530
msgid ""
"The vicious and sly gangster of the sea.\\nIts skin is specially textured to"
" minimize\\ndrag in water. Its speed tops out at over\\n75 miles per hour."
msgstr ""
"Le gangster rusé des océans. Sa peau est\\nconçue pour offrir peu de "
"résistance à\\nl’eau. Il est capable de nager à plus de\\n120 km/h."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6611
msgid ""
"The yellow patterns it bears are old scars.\\nThe energy from Mega Evolution"
" runs\\nthrough them, causing it sharp pain and\\nsuffering."
msgstr ""
"Les motifs jaunes qu’il porte sont de\\nvieilles cicatrices. L’énergie de "
"la\\nMéga-Évolution les parcourt et lui cause\\nune vive douleur."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3398
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6678
msgid "WAILMER"
msgstr "WAILMER"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6681
msgid "Ball Whale"
msgstr "Baleinboule"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6684
msgid ""
"While this Pokémon usually lives in the sea,\\nit can survive on land, "
"although not too\\nlong. It loses vitality if its body becomes\\ndried out."
msgstr ""
"Bien qu’il vive dans les océans, il peut\\nsurvivre quelque temps hors de "
"l’eau.\\nIl perd toute sa vitalité si son corps\\ns’assèche."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6751
msgid "WAILORD"
msgstr "WAILORD"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6754
msgid "Float Whale"
msgstr "Cachabouée"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6757
msgid ""
"It breathes through nostrils that it\\nraises above the sea. By inhaling to "
"its\\nmaximum capacity, a Wailord can dive close\\nto 10,000 feet beneath "
"the waves."
msgstr ""
"Il respire en faisant sortir ses évents\\nhors de l’eau. En inhalant au "
"maximum,\\nil peut descendre jusqu’à 3 000 mètres\\nde profondeur."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6825
msgid "NUMEL"
msgstr "CHAMALLOT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6828
msgid "Numb"
msgstr "Engourdi"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6831
msgid ""
"A Numel stores boiling magma in the hump\\non its back. It is a hardy "
"Pokémon that can\\ntransport a 220-pound load. It has served\\nhumans at "
"work since long ago."
msgstr ""
"Il peut stocker du magma en fusion dans\\nla bosse de son dos. Il peut "
"porter des\\ncharges de 100 kilos et s’avère souvent\\nutile aux humains "
"dans leurs travaux."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2800
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3847
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6914
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7002
msgid "CAMERUPT"
msgstr "CAMERUPT"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6917
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7009
msgid "Eruption"
msgstr "Eruption"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:6920
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that lives in the crater of\\na volcano. Every 10 years, the "
"volcanoes\\non its back erupt violently. Research is\\nunder way on the "
"cause of eruption."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon vit dans les cratères des\\nvolcans. Tous les 10 ans, les volcans"
" sur\\nson dos entrent violemment en éruption,\\nmais personne ne sait "
"pourquoi."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7012
msgid ""
"The humps on its back have transformed\\ninto one large and very active "
"volcano. It\\nhas a deep hatred of water or any moisture\\nand has an "
"explosive personality."
msgstr ""
"Les bosses de son dos sont devenues un\\nseul grand volcan très actif. Il "
"déteste\\nl’eau et l’humidité, et il a un caractère\\nexplosif."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2880
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3691
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7083
msgid "TORKOAL"
msgstr "CHARTOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7086
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:2179
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:2244
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:2307
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:2373
msgid "Coal"
msgstr "Charbon"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7089
msgid ""
"It battles using energy it gets from\\nburning coal. When loosing smoke from"
" its\\nnostrils, it lets off a sound that is\\nsimilar to a locomotive's "
"horn."
msgstr ""
"Il tire sa force de la combustion de son\\ncharbon. Le bruit qu’il fait en "
"laissant\\ns’échapper de la vapeur rappelle celui\\ndes vieilles "
"locomotives."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7155
msgid "SPOINK"
msgstr "SPOINK"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7158
msgid "Bounce"
msgstr "Rebond"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7161
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that manipulates psychic power\\nat will. It doesn't stop bouncing"
" even when\\nit is asleep. It loves eating mushrooms\\nthat grow "
"underground."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon utilise les pouvoirs\\npsychiques à sa guise. Il ne "
"s’arrête\\njamais de rebondir, même en dormant. Ses\\nmets préférés sont les"
" champignons."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:421
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5788
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6194
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7232
msgid "GRUMPIG"
msgstr "GRORET"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7235
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7361
msgid "Manipulate"
msgstr "Magouilleur"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7238
msgid ""
"It stores power in the black pearls on its\\nforehead. When it uses psychic "
"power, it\\nperforms an odd dance step. Its style of\\ndancing became hugely"
" popular overseas."
msgstr ""
"Il concentre son énergie à l’intérieur des\\nperles sur sa tête. Il exécute "
"d’étranges\\npas de danse quand il utilise ses pouvoirs\\npsychiques. Son "
"style est très apprécié."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6930
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7000
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7309
msgid "SPINDA"
msgstr "SPINDA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7312
msgid "Spot Panda"
msgstr "Panda Tache"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7315
msgid ""
"It is distinguished by a pattern of\\nspots that is always different. "
"Its\\nunsteady, tottering walk has the\\neffect of fouling its foe's aim."
msgstr ""
"La forme de ses taches est unique. Sa\\ndémarche maladroite et chancelante "
"a\\npour effet de faire perdre leur\\nconcentration à ses ennemis."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7392
msgid "TRAPINCH"
msgstr "KRAKNOIX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7395
msgid "Ant Pit"
msgstr "Piégeur"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7398
msgid ""
"Its big jaws crunch through boulders.\\nBecause its head is so big, it has a"
" hard\\ntime getting back upright if it tips over\\nonto its back."
msgstr ""
"Ses mâchoires arrivent à briser de gros\\nrochers. Sa tête est si lourde "
"qu’il a du\\nmal à se remettre droit s’il tombe sur\\nle dos."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7464
msgid "VIBRAVA"
msgstr "VIBRANINF"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7467
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3370
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3446
msgid "Vibration"
msgstr "Vibration"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7470
msgid ""
"It looses ultrasonic waves by rubbing its\\nwings together. Since a "
"Vibrava's wings\\nare still in the process of growing, it can\\nonly fly "
"short distances."
msgstr ""
"Il crée des ultrasons en joignant ses ailes\\nentre elles. Comme elles ne "
"sont pas\\ncomplètement formées, il ne peut voler que\\nsur de courtes "
"distances."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5018
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7543
msgid "FLYGON"
msgstr "LIBEGON"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7549
msgid ""
"The flapping of its wings sounds like\\nsinging. To prevent detection by "
"enemies,\\nit hides itself by flapping up a cloud of\\ndesert sand."
msgstr ""
"Le son du battement de ses ailes\\nressemble à de la musique. Pour "
"éviter\\nd’être repéré, il se cache en soulevant un\\nnuage de sable autour "
"de lui."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7618
msgid "CACNEA"
msgstr "CACNEA"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7621
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5543
msgid "Cactus"
msgstr "Cactus"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7624
msgid ""
"Cacnea live in deserts with virtually no\\nrainfall. It battles by swinging "
"its thick,\\nspiked arms. Once a year, a yellow flower\\nblooms."
msgstr ""
"Cacnea vit dans les déserts où la pluie\\nne tombe jamais. Il se bat en "
"balançant ses\\nbras couverts de pointes. Une fois par an,\\nune fleur éclot"
" sur sa tête."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3159
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7697
msgid "CACTURNE"
msgstr "CACTURNE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7700
msgid "Scarecrow"
msgstr "Épouvantail"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7703
msgid ""
"After spending thousands of years in\\nharsh deserts, its blood transformed "
"into\\nthe same substances as sand. It is\\nnocturnal, so it hunts at night."
msgstr ""
"Après des milliers d’années passées dans\\nle désert, son sang a pris la "
"consistance\\ndu sable. C’est un Pokémon nocturne,\\nil ne chasse donc que "
"la nuit."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7779
msgid "SWABLU"
msgstr "TYLTON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7782
msgid "Cotton Bird"
msgstr "Oiseaucoton"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7785
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that has wings like cottony\\nclouds. After enduring winter, in "
"which\\nlittle food is available, Swablu flocks\\nmove closer to towns in "
"the spring."
msgstr ""
"Les ailes de ce Pokémon ressemblent à\\ndes nuages de coton. Après l’hiver, "
"passé\\navec peu de nourriture, il se rapproche des\\nvilles où il est sûr "
"de trouver à manger."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1739
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3543
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4517
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4664
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6416
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8990
msgid "ALTARIA"
msgstr "ALTARIA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7856
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7933
msgid "Humming"
msgstr "Virevolteur"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7859
msgid ""
"It hums in a beautiful soprano voice.\\nIt flies among white clouds in the "
"blue\\nsky. It launches intensely hot fireballs\\nfrom its mouth."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon possède une jolie voix de\\nsoprano. Il vole au milieu des nuages"
" dans\\nle ciel bleu et est capable de cracher des\\nboules de feu avec son "
"bec."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:7936
msgid ""
"It sings with a voice that is even more\\nbeautiful than before it Mega "
"Evolved.\\nIts feathers became larger for protection\\nand glimmer with an "
"iridescent sheen."
msgstr ""
"Il chante d’une voix encore plus belle\\nqu’avant sa Méga-Évolution. Ses "
"plumes\\nont grandi pour le protéger et chatoient\\nde reflets irisés."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1060
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8360
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8005
msgid "ZANGOOSE"
msgstr "MANGRIFF"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8008
msgid "Cat Ferret"
msgstr "Chat Furet"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8011
msgid ""
"When it battles, it stands on its hind legs\\nand attacks with its sharply "
"clawed\\nforelegs. Its fur bristles if it encounters\\nany Seviper."
msgstr ""
"Pour se battre, il se dresse sur ses pattes\\narrière et attaque avec les "
"griffes de ses\\npattes avant. Son poil se hérisse s’il\\ncroise un Seviper."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8082
msgid "SEVIPER"
msgstr "SEVIPER"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8085
msgid "Fang Snake"
msgstr "Serpacroc"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8088
msgid ""
"Seviper and Zangoose are eternal rivals.\\nIt counters a Zangoose's dazzling"
" agility\\nwith its swordlike tail, which also oozes\\na horrible poison."
msgstr ""
"C’est l’éternel rival de Mangriff.\\nIl compense la vitesse de ce dernier "
"à\\nl’aide de sa queue tranchante qui contient\\nun poison très puissant."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4998
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8164
msgid "LUNATONE"
msgstr "SELEROC"

#. source : patch FR actuel (récupéré par pointeur)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8167
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8247
msgid "Meteorite"
msgstr "Météorite"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8170
msgid ""
"It becomes very active on the night of\\na full moon. This Pokémon was "
"first\\ndiscovered 40 years ago at the site of\\na meteor strike."
msgstr ""
"Il devient très actif les soirs de pleine\\nlune. Il fut découvert il y a 40"
" ans dans\\nun cratère de météorite."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:502
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4937
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8244
msgid "SOLROCK"
msgstr "SOLAROC"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8250
msgid ""
"Solar energy is the source of this \\nPokémon's power. On sunny days, groups"
" of\\nSolrock line up facing the sun and absorb\\nits light."
msgstr ""
"L’énergie solaire est la source du pouvoir\\nde ce Pokémon. Les jours "
"clairs, des\\ngroupes de Solaroc s’alignent en plein\\nsoleil pour absorber "
"sa lumière."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8320
msgid "BARBOACH"
msgstr "BARLOCHE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8323
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8407
msgid "Whiskers"
msgstr "Barbillon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8326
msgid ""
"Its body is covered with a slimy film.\\nThe film acts as a barrier to "
"prevent germs\\nin muddy water from entering the\\nBarboach's body."
msgstr ""
"Son corps est couvert d’un film fin qui lui\\nsert de protection contre les "
"microbes\\nque l’on trouve dans les eaux boueuses."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8404
msgid "WHISCASH"
msgstr "BARBICHA"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8410
msgid ""
"Mysteriously, it can foretell earthquakes.\\nIn the daytime, it sleeps in "
"mud at the\\nbottom of a pond. When it awakens, it\\ncontinually feeds "
"throughout the night."
msgstr ""
"Mystérieusement, il est capable de\\nprédire les tremblements de terre.\\nIl"
" passe la journée à dormir dans la boue\\net chasse toute la nuit."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8483
msgid "CORPHISH"
msgstr "ECRAPINCE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8486
msgid "Ruffian"
msgstr "Brute"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8489
msgid ""
"Once it grips prey with its large pincers,\\nit will never let go, no matter"
" what.\\nIt is a hardy Pokémon that can thrive\\nin any environment."
msgstr ""
"Quoi qu’il arrive, il ne relâche jamais une\\nproie tombée entre ses pinces."
" Ce Pokémon\\ntrès robuste peut survivre dans n’importe\\nquel "
"environnement."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8556
msgid "CRAWDAUNT"
msgstr "COLHOMARD"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8559
msgid "Rogue"
msgstr "Crapule"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8562
msgid ""
"A brutish Pokémon that loves to battle.\\nA veteran Crawdaunt that has "
"prevailed in\\nhundreds of battles has giant pincers\\nmarked with countless"
" scars."
msgstr ""
"C’est une brute qui adore se battre. Tant\\nelles sont nombreuses, il est "
"impossible\\nde compter les traces de combats sur les\\npinces d’un vieux "
"Colhomard."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2165
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6786
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8628
msgid "BALTOY"
msgstr "BALBUTO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8631
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8705
msgid "Clay Doll"
msgstr "Poupargile"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8634
msgid ""
"A Baltoy moves by spinning on its single\\nfoot. It has been depicted in "
"murals \\nadorning the walls of a once-bustling city\\nin an ancient age."
msgstr ""
"Balbuto se déplace en tournant sur son\\nunique pied. On a découvert des "
"dessins\\nle représentant dans les vestiges d’une\\nville des temps anciens."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1719
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3653
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4957
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8702
msgid "CLAYDOL"
msgstr "KAORINE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8708
msgid ""
"A Claydol sleeps while hovering in midair.\\nIts arms are separate from its "
"body.\\nThey are kept floating by the Pokémon's\\nmanipulation of psychic "
"power."
msgstr ""
"Kaorine dort en flottant dans les airs.\\nSes bras sont séparés de son corps"
" et\\nrestent en lévitation grâce aux pouvoirs\\npsychiques de ce Pokémon."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8783
msgid "LILEEP"
msgstr "LILIA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8786
msgid "Sea Lily"
msgstr "Lis d’Eau"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8789
msgid ""
"It disguises itself as seaweed by making\\nits tentacles sway. Unsuspecting "
"prey\\nthat come too close are swallowed whole.\\nIt became extinct 100 "
"million years ago."
msgstr ""
"Il se fait passer pour de vulgaires algues\\nen faisant flotter ses "
"tentacules. Ses\\nvictimes sont avalées d’un coup. L’espèce\\ns’était "
"éteinte il y a 100 millions d’années."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2461
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8861
msgid "CRADILY"
msgstr "VACILYS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8864
msgid "Barnacle"
msgstr "Bernacle"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8867
msgid ""
"It drags its heavy body along the\\nseafloor. It makes its nest in the "
"shallows\\nof warm seas. Cradily can be seen on\\nbeaches when the tide goes"
" out."
msgstr ""
"Il traîne lourdement son corps au fond\\nde l’océan et fait son nid dans "
"les\\nhauts-fonds des mers chaudes. On peut\\nen apercevoir à marée basse."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8940
msgid "ANORITH"
msgstr "ANORITH"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8943
msgid "Old Shrimp"
msgstr "Crustage"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:8946
msgid ""
"It was resurrected from a fossil using the\\npower of science. It swims by "
"undulating\\nthe eight wings at its sides. They were\\nfeet that adapted to "
"life in the sea."
msgstr ""
"La science l’a ressuscité à partir d’un\\nfossile. Il nage en ondulant les "
"huit ailes\\nsur ses côtés. Celles-ci ont réussi à\\ns’adapter à la vie "
"sous-marine."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2481
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9019
msgid "ARMALDO"
msgstr "ARMALDO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/battle_debug.c:2253 src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9022
msgid "Plate"
msgstr "Blindage"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9025
msgid ""
"Armaldo usually lives on land. However,\\nwhen it hunts for prey, it dives "
"beneath\\nthe ocean. It swims around using its two\\nlarge wings."
msgstr ""
"Armaldo vit généralement sur terre mais\\nil chasse ses proies au fond de "
"l’océan.\\nIl arrive à nager en utilisant ses deux\\ngrandes ailes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9095
msgid "FEEBAS"
msgstr "BARPAU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9101
msgid ""
"Feebas live in ponds that are heavily\\ninfested with weeds. Because of "
"its\\nhopelessly shabby appearance, it\\nseems as if few Trainers raise it."
msgstr ""
"Barpau vit dans les mares infestées\\nd’algues. À cause de son "
"apparence,\\ntrès peu de Dresseurs choisissent de\\ns’occuper de lui."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9174
msgid "MILOTIC"
msgstr "MILOBELLUS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9177
msgid "Tender"
msgstr "Tendre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9180
msgid ""
"It is said to live at the bottom of\\nlarge lakes. Considered to be the "
"most\\nbeautiful of all Pokémon, it has been\\ndepicted in paintings and "
"statues."
msgstr ""
"On dit qu’il vit au fond des grands lacs.\\nConsidéré comme le plus beau de "
"tous\\nles Pokémon, Milobellus a été\\nreproduit sur de nombreux tableaux."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:833
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2205
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9263
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9342
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9424
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9505
msgid "CASTFORM"
msgstr "MORPHEO"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Climat
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9266
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9345
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9427
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9508
msgid "Weather"
msgstr "Weather"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9269
msgid ""
"It alters its form depending on the\\nweather. Changes in the climate such "
"as\\nthe temperature and humidity appear to\\naffect its cellular structure."
msgstr ""
"Il change son apparence en fonction du\\ntemps. Les changements "
"climatiques,\\ncomme la température ou l’humidité,\\naffectent sa structure "
"cellulaire."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9348
msgid ""
"Castform takes this form on bright days.\\nIn an experiment where is was "
"placed in\\nfront of a heater, it didn't change to this\\nform. Its body is "
"warm and toasty."
msgstr ""
"Il change son apparence en fonction du\\ntemps. Les changements "
"climatiques,\\ncomme la température ou l’humidité,\\naffectent sa structure "
"cellulaire."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9430
msgid ""
"This is Castform's form while it's raining.\\nIn an experiment where it was "
"placed in a\\nshower, it didn't change to this form. Its\\nbody is soft, "
"slightly swollen with water."
msgstr ""
"Il change son apparence en fonction du\\ntemps. Les changements "
"climatiques,\\ncomme la température ou l’humidité,\\naffectent sa structure "
"cellulaire."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9511
msgid ""
"This is Castform's form in a hailstorm.\\nIn an experiment where it was "
"placed\\nin a freezer, it didn't change to this form.\\nIts cold skin is as "
"smooth as ice."
msgstr ""
"Il change son apparence en fonction du\\ntemps. Les changements "
"climatiques,\\ncomme la température ou l’humidité,\\naffectent sa structure "
"cellulaire."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9589
msgid "KECLEON"
msgstr "KECLEON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9592
msgid "Color Swap"
msgstr "Multicolor"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9595
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that has the ability to alter its\\nbody colors to match its "
"surroundings.\\nA Kecleon reverts to its original colors if\\nit is "
"startled."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon a la faculté de changer la\\ncouleur de son corps pour se fondre "
"dans\\nson environnement. S’il est effrayé,\\nil retrouve sa véritable "
"couleur."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9667
msgid "SHUPPET"
msgstr "POLICHOMBR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9670
msgid "Puppet"
msgstr "Poupée"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9673
msgid ""
"This Pokémon roams about deep in the\\nnight seeking such negative emotions "
"as\\ngrudges and envy. It retreats to its nest\\nwhen the sun begins to "
"rise."
msgstr ""
"Polichombr erre la nuit à la recherche\\nd’émotions négatives telles que la "
"rancune\\nou la jalousie. Il regagne son repaire aux\\npremiers rayons de "
"soleil."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:481
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8771
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:9193
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9747
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9824
msgid "BANETTE"
msgstr "BRANETTE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Marionnette
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9750
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9831
msgid "Marionette"
msgstr "Marionette"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9753
msgid ""
"An abandoned plush doll became this\\nPokémon. They are said to live in "
"garbage\\ndumps and wander about in search of the\\nchildren that threw them"
" away."
msgstr ""
"C’est une peluche abandonnée devenue\\nPokémon. Les Branette errent "
"dans\\nles décharges à la recherche des enfants\\nqui les ont abandonnés."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9834
msgid ""
"Extraordinary energy amplifies its\\ncursing power to such an extent that "
"it\\ncan't help but curse its own Trainer."
msgstr ""
"Une énergie extraordinaire décuple son\\npouvoir de malédiction, au point "
"qu’il ne\\npeut s’empêcher de maudire son propre\\nDresseur."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9906
msgid "DUSKULL"
msgstr "SKELENOX"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9909
msgid "Requiem"
msgstr "Requiem"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9912
msgid ""
"A glare from its single scarlet eye makes\\neven burly grown-ups freeze in "
"utter fear.\\nIt is a nocturnal Pokémon that roams\\nabout under the cloak "
"of darkness."
msgstr ""
"Un seul regard de son œil écarlate\\nsuffit à effrayer les plus courageux "
"des\\nhommes. C’est un Pokémon nocturne qui\\nvagabonde, masqué par les "
"ténèbres."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:441
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8731
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:9155
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:9301
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9984
msgid "DUSCLOPS"
msgstr "TERACLOPE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9987
msgid "Beckon"
msgstr "Appel"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:9990
msgid ""
"It is thought that its body is hollow with\\nonly a spectral ball of fire "
"burning inside.\\nHowever, no one has been able to\\nconfirm this theory as "
"fact."
msgstr ""
"On raconte que son corps creux ne\\ncontiendrait qu’une boule de "
"feu\\nspectrale. Mais personne n’a jamais pu\\nconfirmer cette théorie."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4258
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10071
msgid "DUSKNOIR"
msgstr "NOCTUNOIR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10074
msgid "Gripper"
msgstr "Mainpince"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10077
msgid ""
"This feared Pokémon is said to travel to\\nworlds unknown. Some even believe"
" that\\nit takes lost spirits into its pliant body\\nand guides them home."
msgstr ""
"Nul ne sait s’il est doté d’une volonté\\npropre. Les ondes du monde des "
"esprits\\nle poussent à conduire humains et\\nPokémon vers l’au-delà."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1449
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5934
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10153
msgid "TROPIUS"
msgstr "TROPIUS"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10156
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:3671
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:3738
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:3804
msgid "Fruit"
msgstr "Fruit"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10159
msgid ""
"It flies by flapping its broad leaves.\\nThe bunch of fruit that grows "
"around its\\nneck is deliciously sweet. In the spring,\\nit scatters pollen "
"from its neck."
msgstr ""
"Il vole en secouant ses larges ailes.\\nLes fruits qui poussent autour de "
"son cou\\nsont doux et délicieux. Au printemps, il\\nsort du pollen de son "
"cou."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10227
msgid "CHINGLING"
msgstr "KORILLON"

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10230
msgid "Bell"
msgstr "Cloche"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10233
msgid ""
"There is an orb inside its mouth.\\nWhen it hops, the orb bounces all\\nover"
" and makes a ringing sound.\\nIt can cry for an awfully long time."
msgstr ""
"Quand il sautille, l’orbe qu’il a dans la\\nbouche s’agite et tinte comme "
"une\\ncloche."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1337
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1699
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6448
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10310
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10396
msgid "CHIMECHO"
msgstr "EOKO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10313
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10403
msgid "Wind Chime"
msgstr "Carillon"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10316
msgid ""
"They fly about very actively when the hot\\nseason arrives. They communicate"
" among\\nthemselves using seven different and\\ndistinguishing cries."
msgstr ""
"Les EOKO volent plus vivement quand la\\nsaison chaude arrive. Ils "
"communiquent\\nentre eux à l’aide de sept cris différents."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10406
msgid ""
"It vibrates its entire body to attack in\\nall directions using sound waves."
" Any who\\nhear the vibrations get so confused, they\\nforget who they are."
msgstr ""
"Il fait vibrer tout son corps pour\\nattaquer avec des ondes sonores "
"dans\\ntoutes les directions. Ceux qui les\\nentendent en oublient qui ils "
"sont."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4497
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4644
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6370
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:8970
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10463
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10538
msgid "ABSOL"
msgstr "ABSOL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10466
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10545
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10622
msgid "Disaster"
msgstr "Désastre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10469
msgid ""
"It sharply senses even subtle changes in\\nthe sky and the land to predict "
"natural\\ndisasters. It is a long-lived Pokémon that\\nhas a life-span of "
"100 years."
msgstr ""
"Il arrive à capter précisément le moindre\\nchangement dans l’air ou sur "
"terre et peut\\nainsi prédire les catastrophes naturelles.\\nIl a une "
"espérance de vie de 100 ans."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10548
msgid ""
"As the energy of Mega Evolution fills it,\\nits fur bristles. What you see "
"on its back\\nare not true wings, and this Pokémon isn't\\nable to fly."
msgstr ""
"L’énergie de la Méga-Évolution\\nhérisse sa fourrure. Sur son dos, ce\\lne "
"sont pas de vraies ailes: il ne peut\\lpas voler."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10625
msgid ""
"Using fur that it has made into sharp,\\nclawlike shapes, it cuts down foes "
"with\\na single blow. This is an act of kindness\\nto keep them from "
"suffering."
msgstr ""
"Avec sa fourrure façonnée en griffes\\nacérées, il terrasse ses ennemis "
"d’un\\nseul coup. C’est un acte de bonté qui\\nleur évite de souffrir."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10681
msgid "SNORUNT"
msgstr "STALGAMIN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10684
msgid "Snow Hat"
msgstr "Capuche"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10687
msgid ""
"They tend to move about in groups of\\naround five Snorunt. In snowy "
"regions,\\nit is said that when they are seen late at\\nnight, snowfall will"
" arrive by morning."
msgstr ""
"Les Stalgamin se déplacent souvent\\npar groupes de cinq. En montagne, on "
"dit\\nqu’apercevoir ce Pokémon tard le soir\\nannonce un matin enneigé."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10761
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10834
msgid "GLALIE"
msgstr "ONIGLALI"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10764
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10841
msgid "Face"
msgstr "Visage"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10767
msgid ""
"A Glalie has the power to instantaneously\\nfreeze moisture in the "
"atmosphere.\\nA dazzling cloud of diamondlike ice\\ncrystals forms around "
"its body."
msgstr ""
"Oniglali a le pouvoir de geler\\ninstantanément l’humidité de l’air.\\nUn "
"nuage de cristaux de glace se\\nforme tout autour de son corps."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10844
msgid ""
"The power of Mega Evolution was so strong\\nthat it smashed Glalie's jaw. "
"Its inability\\nto eat very well leaves Glalie irritated."
msgstr ""
"La puissance de la Méga-Évolution était\\nsi forte qu’elle a brisé la "
"mâchoire\\nd’ONIGLALI. Ne pouvant plus bien manger,\\nil est irritable."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10909
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10980
msgid "FROSLASS"
msgstr "MOMARTIK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10912
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10987
msgid "Snow Land"
msgstr "Enneigement"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10915
msgid ""
"When it finds people or Pokémon it likes,\\nit freezes them and takes them "
"to its\\nchilly den, where they become its\\ndecorations."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon est né des regrets d’une\\nfemme disparue dans les pics "
"enneigés.\\nIl raffole des âmes gelées."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:10990
msgid ""
"This Pokémon can use eerie cold\\nair imbued with ghost energy to\\nfreeze "
"even insubstantial things,\\nsuch as flames or the wind."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon utilise un air froid\\nsinistre chargé d’énergie spectrale\\npour"
" geler même ce qui n’a pas de\\ncorps, comme les flammes ou le vent."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6528
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11047
msgid "SPHEAL"
msgstr "OBALIE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11050
msgid "Clap"
msgstr "Clap Clap"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11053
msgid ""
"It is completely covered with plushy fur.\\nAs a result, it never feels the "
"cold even\\nwhen it is rolling about on ice floes or\\ndiving in the sea."
msgstr ""
"Il est complètement recouvert d’une\\nfourrure épaisse. Grâce à elle, il "
"ne\\nressent jamais le froid, même s’il nage\\ndans de l’eau glacée."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:5049
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11126
msgid "SEALEO"
msgstr "PHOGLEUR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11129
msgid "Ball Roll"
msgstr "Roule Boule"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11132
msgid ""
"Sealeo live in herds on ice floes. Using its\\npowerful flippers, it "
"shatters ice.\\nIt dives into the sea to hunt prey five\\ntimes a day."
msgstr ""
"Les Phogleur vivent en groupe sur\\nla banquise. Ils fracassent la glace "
"à\\nl’aide de leurs nageoires et plongent pour\\nchasser cinq fois par jour."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11206
msgid "WALREIN"
msgstr "KAIMORSE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11209
msgid "Ice Break"
msgstr "Brise Glace"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11212
msgid ""
"To protect its herd, the leader battles\\nanything that invades its "
"territory, even\\nat the cost of its life. Its tusks may snap\\noff in "
"battle."
msgstr ""
"Pour protéger son groupe, KAIMORSE\\nattaque au péril de sa vie tout ce "
"qui\\ns’aventure sur son territoire. Il peut\\nperdre ses défenses pendant "
"un combat."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:6232
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11279
msgid "CLAMPERL"
msgstr "COQUIPERL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11285
msgid ""
"A Clamperl slams its shell closed on prey\\nto prevent escape. The pearl it "
"creates\\nupon evolution is said to be infused with\\na mysterious energy."
msgstr ""
"Coquiperl ferme sa coquille sur ses proies\\npour qu’elles ne puissent pas "
"s’enfuir. On\\nraconte que sa perle contient une énergie\\nmystérieuse."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11355
msgid "HUNTAIL"
msgstr "SERPANG"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11358
msgid "Deep Sea"
msgstr "Abysse"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11361
msgid ""
"To withstand the crushing pressure of\\nwater deep under the sea, its spine "
"is very\\nthick and sturdy. Its tail, which is shaped\\nlike a small fish, "
"has eyes that light up."
msgstr ""
"Grâce à sa colonne vertébrale très\\nrobuste, il arrive à supporter la "
"pression\\nau fond de l’océan. Sa queue en forme de\\npetit poisson a des "
"yeux qui s’allument."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:960
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11425
msgid "GOREBYSS"
msgstr "ROSABYSS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11428
msgid "South Sea"
msgstr "Mer du Sud"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11431
msgid ""
"A Gorebyss siphons the body fluids of prey\\nthrough its thin, tubular "
"mouth. Its light\\npink body color turns vivid when it\\nfinishes feeding."
msgstr ""
"Rosabyss aspire les fluides corporels\\nde ses ennemis à l’aide de sa bouche"
" très\\nfine. Le rose clair de sa peau devient très\\nvif quand il a fini de"
" manger."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:7283
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11498
msgid "RELICANTH"
msgstr "RELICANTH"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11501
msgid "Longevity"
msgstr "Longévité"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11504
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that was once believed to have\\nbeen extinct. The species has not"
" changed\\nits form for 100 million years. It walks on\\nthe seafloor using "
"its pectoral fins."
msgstr ""
"On a cru cette espèce éteinte et elle n’a\\npas évolué depuis 100 millions "
"d’années. Il\\nse déplace au fond de la mer en utilisant\\nses nageoires "
"comme s’il marchait."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:2257
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11584
msgid "LUVDISC"
msgstr "LOVDISC"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11587
msgid "Rendezvous"
msgstr "Rendezvous"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11590
msgid ""
"Luvdisc make the branches of Corsola\\ntheir nests. There is a custom from "
"long\\nago of giving a Luvdisc as a gift to\\nexpress one's feelings of "
"love."
msgstr ""
"Lovdisc crée son nid dans les branches\\nd’un Corayon. Une vieille tradition"
" veut\\nqu’on offre ce Pokémon aux personnes\\nqui nous sont chères."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11657
msgid "BAGON"
msgstr "DRABY"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11660
msgid "Rock Head"
msgstr "Tête de Roc"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11663
msgid ""
"Although it is small, this Pokémon is very\\npowerful because its body is a "
"bundle of\\nmuscles. It launches head-butts with its\\nironlike skull."
msgstr ""
"Les muscles de ce petit Pokémon le\\nrendent très puissant. Ses coups de "
"tête\\nsont redoutables grâce à son crâne solide\\ncomme l’acier."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11729
msgid "SHELGON"
msgstr "DRACKHAUS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11732
msgid "Endurance"
msgstr "Endurant"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11735
msgid ""
"It hardly eats while it awaits evolution.\\nIt becomes hardier by enduring "
"hunger.\\nIts shell peels off the instant it begins\\nto evolve."
msgstr ""
"En attendant son évolution, ce Pokémon\\nmange très peu pour s’endurcir. Sa "
"coquille\\nse détache dès qu’il commence à évoluer."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:4756
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:9224
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11806
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11881
msgid "SALAMENCE"
msgstr "DRATTAK"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11812
msgid ""
"After many long years, its cellular\\nstructure underwent a sudden mutation "
"to\\ngrow wings. When angered, it loses all\\nthought and rampages out of "
"control."
msgstr ""
"Après de longues années, sa structure\\ncellulaire subit un grand changement"
" pour\\npermettre à ses ailes de pousser. Une fois\\nénervé, il perd tout "
"contrôle de lui-même."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11891
msgid ""
"Mega Evolution fuels its brutality, and it\\nmay even turn on the Trainer "
"who raised it.\\nIt's been dubbed the blood-soaked.\\ncrescent."
msgstr ""
"La Méga-Évolution attise sa brutalité: il\\npeut même s’en prendre au "
"Dresseur qui l’a\\nélevé. On le surnomme le croissant\\nsanglant."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11959
msgid "BELDUM"
msgstr "TERHAL"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Boulefer
#: src/battle_debug.c:2235
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11962
msgid "Iron Ball"
msgstr "Balle Fer"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:11965
msgid ""
"When Beldum gather in a swarm, they move\\nin perfect unison as if they were"
" but one\\nPokémon. They communicate with each other\\nusing brain waves."
msgstr ""
"Quand les Terhal se réunissent, ils\\nse déplacent à l’unisson comme "
"s’ils\\nn’étaient qu’un Pokémon. Ils communiquent\\ngrâce à leurs ondes "
"cérébrales."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:1317
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12032
msgid "METANG"
msgstr "METANG"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12035
msgid "Iron Claw"
msgstr "Pincefer"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12038
msgid ""
"The claws tipping its arms pack the\\ndestructive power to tear through "
"thick\\niron sheets as if they were silk. It flies\\nat over 60 miles per "
"hour."
msgstr ""
"Les griffes sur ses bras renferment toute\\nsa puissance destructrice. Elles"
" déchirent\\nle métal aussi facilement que de la soie.\\nIl vole à 100 km/h."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3867
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3959
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12109
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12182
msgid "METAGROSS"
msgstr "METALOSSE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12112
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12189
msgid "Iron Leg"
msgstr "Pattefer"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12115
msgid ""
"Metagross has four brains that are joined\\nby a complex neural network. As "
"a result of\\nintegration, this Pokémon is smarter than\\na supercomputer."
msgstr ""
"Les quatre cerveaux de Metalosse sont\\nreliés par un réseau neuronal "
"complexe.\\nCe Pokémon est plus intelligent qu’un\\nsuperordinateur."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12192
msgid ""
"When it knows it can't win, it digs the\\nclaws on its legs into its "
"opponent and\\nstarts the countdown to a big explosion."
msgstr ""
"Quand il sait qu’il ne peut pas gagner, il\\nplante les griffes de ses "
"pattes dans\\nson adversaire et lance le compte à\\nrebours d’une grande "
"explosion."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3710
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12266
msgid "REGIROCK"
msgstr "REGIROCK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12269
msgid "Rock Peak"
msgstr "Pic Rocheux"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12272
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that is made entirely of rocks\\nand boulders. If parts of its "
"body chip off\\nin battle, Regirock repairs itself by\\nadding new rocks."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon est uniquement constitué\\nde pierres et de rochers. Quand "
"il\\nendommage son corps au combat, il le\\nrégénère en ajoutant de nouveaux"
" rochers."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3601
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12346
msgid "REGICE"
msgstr "REGICE"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12349
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:6367
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:6445
msgid "Iceberg"
msgstr "Iceberg"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12352
msgid ""
"Its entire body is made of Antarctic ice.\\nAfter extensive studies, "
"researchers\\nbelieve the ice was formed during an\\nice age."
msgstr ""
"Tout son corps est constitué de\\nglace provenant de l’Antarctique. "
"Les\\nscientifiques pensent que ce Pokémon\\ns’est constitué pendant l’âge "
"de glace."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/battle_frontier/trainer_hill.h:3582
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12429
msgid "REGISTEEL"
msgstr "REGISTEEL"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12432
msgid "Iron"
msgstr "Fer"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12435
msgid ""
"Its body is harder than any other kind of\\nmetal. The body metal is "
"composed of a\\nmysterious substance. Not only is it hard,\\nit shrinks and "
"stretches flexibly."
msgstr ""
"Son corps est plus dur que n’importe quel\\nmétal et est composé d’une "
"substance\\nmystérieuse. En plus d’être dur, il peut\\négalement raccourcir "
"ou s’allonger."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12508
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12583
msgid "LATIAS"
msgstr "LATIAS"

#. source : patch FR actuel (récupéré par pointeur)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12511
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12590
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12671
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12750
msgid "Eon"
msgstr "Éon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12514
msgid ""
"They make a small herd of only several\\nmembers. They rarely make contact "
"with\\npeople or other Pokémon. They disappear\\nif they sense enemies."
msgstr ""
"Il n’existe qu’un faible nombre de Latias.\\nIls ne rentrent que rarement en"
" contact\\navec les humains ou d’autres Pokémon et\\nfuient dès qu’ils "
"détectent un ennemi."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12593
msgid ""
"Its body is smaller than Mega Latios's\\nbody. It is more agile and can make"
" very\\nsharp turns. When it Mega Evolves, its\\ndefensive strength grows "
"substantially."
msgstr ""
"Son corps est plus petit que celui de\\nMEGA-LATIOS. Plus agile, il peut "
"virer\\ntrès sec. Quand il méga-évolue, sa\\ndéfense augmente nettement."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12668
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12743
msgid "LATIOS"
msgstr "LATIOS"

#. source : Émeraude FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12674
msgid ""
"Even in hiding, it can detect the locations\\nof others and sense their "
"emotions since\\nit has telepathy. Its intelligence allows\\nit to "
"understand human languages."
msgstr ""
"Même en se cachant, il parvient à détecter\\nles autres Pokémon et à sentir "
"leurs\\némotions grâce à son don de télépathie.\\nIl comprend le langage des"
" humains."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12753
msgid ""
"It's larger than Mega Latias, and can\\nachieve higher speeds in "
"flight.\\nThis Pokémon can use its speed in battle\\nto unleash a flurry of "
"attacks."
msgstr ""
"Plus grand que MEGA-LATIAS, il atteint\\nde plus grandes vitesses en vol. Il"
" se\\nsert de sa vitesse au combat pour\\nlancer une avalanche d’attaques."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12831
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12906
msgid "Sea Basin"
msgstr "Bassinmarin"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12834
msgid ""
"Kyogre has appeared in mythology as the\\ncreator of the sea. After long "
"years of\\nfeuding with Groudon, it took to sleep at\\nthe bottom of the "
"sea."
msgstr ""
"Selon la mythologie, Kyogre serait le\\ncréateur de la mer. Après s’être "
"battu de\\nlongues années contre Groudon, il partit\\nse reposer tout au "
"fond de l’océan."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12909
msgid ""
"When Kyogre roared, water poured forth\\nand the seas spread outward.\\nDark"
" clouds enshrouded the world,\\nand the deluge fell upon all…"
msgstr ""
"Quand KYOGRE rugit, l’eau jaillit et les\\nmers s’étendent. De sombres "
"nuages\\nenveloppent le monde et le déluge\\ns’abat sur tout…"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12987
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13062
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:178
msgid "Continent"
msgstr "Continent"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:12990
msgid ""
"Groudon has appeared in mythology as the\\ncreator of the land. It sleeps in"
" magma\\nunderground and is said to make volcanoes\\nerupt on awakening."
msgstr ""
"Groudon apparaît dans la mythologie\\ncomme le créateur de la terre. Il dort"
" dans\\nle magma souterrain et créerait des\\néruptions volcaniques en se "
"réveillant."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13065
msgid ""
"When Groudon howled, the earth swelled and\\nthe land grew wide. The sun "
"blazed atop\\nand all the world around the creature\\nwas enveloped in "
"incandescent heat."
msgstr ""
"Quand GROUDON hurle, la terre se soulève\\net s’étend. Le soleil brûle au-"
"dessus de\\nlui et le monde entier baigne dans une\\nchaleur incandescente."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13141
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13219
msgid "RAYQUAZA"
msgstr "RAYQUAZA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13144
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13222
msgid "Sky High"
msgstr "Cieux"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13147
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that flies endlessly in the\\nozone layer. It is said it would "
"descend\\nto the ground if Kyogre and Groudon\\nwere to fight."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon vole sans cesse au milieu\\nde la couche d’ozone. On raconte "
"qu’il\\nviendrait sur terre en cas de combat\\nentre Groudon et Kyogre."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13225
msgid ""
"Particles stream from the filaments that\\nextend from its jaw. They can "
"control the\\ndensity and humidity of the air, allowing\\nRayquaza to "
"manipulate the weather."
msgstr ""
"Des particules jaillissent des filaments\\nde sa mâchoire. Elles contrôlent "
"la\\ndensité et l’humidité de l’air, ce qui\\npermet à RAYQUAZA de manipuler"
" la météo."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13303
msgid "JIRACHI"
msgstr "JIRACHI"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Souhait
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13306
msgid "Wish"
msgstr "Voeu"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13309
msgid ""
"Jirachi is said to make wishes come true.\\nWhile it sleeps, a tough "
"crystalline shell\\nenvelops the body to protect it from\\nenemies."
msgstr ""
"Selon la légende, Jirachi aurait le pouvoir\\nd’exaucer les vœux. Quand il "
"dort, il\\ns’entoure d’une épaisse enveloppe de\\ncristal pour se protéger "
"de ses ennemis."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13393
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13473
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13552
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13632
msgid "DEOXYS"
msgstr "DEOXYS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13396
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13476
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13555
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13635
msgid "DNA"
msgstr "ADN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13399
msgid ""
"Deoxys emerged from a virus that came\\nfrom space. It is highly intelligent"
" and\\ncan shoot lasers from the crystalline\\norgan on its chest."
msgstr ""
"Il est le résultat de la mutation d’un virus\\nextraterrestre exposé à un "
"rayon laser.\\nSa structure corporelle lui confère une\\nagilité et une "
"vitesse supérieures."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13479
msgid ""
"This Deoxys has transformed into its\\naggressive guise. It can fool "
"enemies\\nby altering its appearance."
msgstr ""
"Ce Deoxys a pris son apparence\\nagressive. Il peut tromper l’ennemi\\nen "
"modifiant son aspect."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13558
msgid ""
"When it changes form, an aurora\\nappears. It absorbs attacks by\\naltering "
"its cellular structure."
msgstr ""
"Une aurore apparaît quand il\\nchange de forme. Il absorbe les\\nattaques en"
" modifiant ses cellules."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_3_families.h:13638
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that mutated from an\\nextraterrestrial virus exposed to a "
"laser\\nbeam. Its body is configured for superior \\nagility and speed."
msgstr ""
"Un Pokémon né d’un virus extraterrestre\\nqui a muté après avoir été exposé "
"à un\\nlaser. Son corps est conçu pour une\\nagilité et une vitesse "
"supérieures."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:27
msgid "TURTWIG"
msgstr "TORTIPOUSS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:30
msgid "Tiny Leaf"
msgstr "Minifeuille"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:33
msgid ""
"The shell on its back is made of soil. \\nOn a very healthy Turtwig, the "
"shell \\nshould feel moist. The leaf on its head\\nwilts if it is thirsty."
msgstr ""
"Sa carapace est faite de terre. Chez un\\nTortipouss en bonne santé, elle "
"est humide\\nau toucher. La feuille sur sa tête fane\\nquand il a soif."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:98
msgid "GROTLE"
msgstr "BOSKARA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:101
msgid "Grove"
msgstr "Bosquet"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:104
msgid ""
"A Grotle that lives in the forest is said\\nto have its own secret "
"springwater well. \\nIt carries fellow Pokémon there on \\nits back."
msgstr ""
"Un Boskara de la forêt aurait sa propre\\nsource secrète. Il y transporte "
"d’autres\\nPokémon sur son dos."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:175
msgid "TORTERRA"
msgstr "TORTERRA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:181
msgid ""
"Some Pokémon are born on a Torterra's\\nback and spend their entire life "
"there.\\nAncient people imagined that beneath \\nthe ground, a gigantic "
"Torterra dwelled."
msgstr ""
"Certains Pokémon naissent sur le dos d’un\\nTorterra et y passent toute leur"
" vie. Les\\nanciens pensaient qu’un Torterra géant\\nvivait sous terre."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:245
msgid "CHIMCHAR"
msgstr "OUISTICRAM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:248
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:29
msgid "Chimp"
msgstr "Chimpanzé"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:251
msgid ""
"Its fiery rear end is fueled by gas made\\nin its belly. Before going to "
"sleep,\\nChimchar extinguish the flame on their\\ntails to prevent fires."
msgstr ""
"Le feu de son postérieur est alimenté par\\nun gaz produit dans son ventre. "
"Avant de\\ndormir, il éteint sa flamme pour éviter les\\nincendies."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:320
msgid "MONFERNO"
msgstr "CHIMPENFEU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:323
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:2567
msgid "Playful"
msgstr "Garnement"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:326
msgid ""
"It carefully controls the intensity of\\nthe flame on its tail, so as to "
"keep its\\nfoes at an adequate distance.\\nIts fiery tail is but one weapon."
msgstr ""
"Il règle avec soin l’intensité de la flamme\\nde sa queue pour tenir "
"l’ennemi à distance.\\nSa queue enflammée n’est qu’une de ses\\narmes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:399
msgid "INFERNAPE"
msgstr "SIMIABRAZ"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:405
msgid ""
"Its crown of fire is indicative of its\\nfiery nature. It uses a special "
"kind of\\nmartial arts involving all of its limbs to\\ntake on any opponent."
msgstr ""
"Sa couronne de feu reflète son\\ntempérament fougueux. Il pratique un "
"art\\nmartial qui fait appel à ses quatre membres\\npour vaincre tout "
"ennemi."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:473
msgid "PIPLUP"
msgstr "TIPLOUF"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:476
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:550
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:5637
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:5703
msgid "Penguin"
msgstr "Pingouin"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:479
msgid ""
"A poor walker, it often falls down. However,\\nits strong pride makes it "
"puff up its chest\\nwithout a care. It's difficult to bond with\\nsince it "
"won't listen to its Trainer."
msgstr ""
"Il marche mal et tombe souvent, mais il\\nbombe fièrement le torse. "
"Difficile de s’en\\nfaire un ami: il n’écoute pas son Dresseur."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:547
msgid "PRINPLUP"
msgstr "PRINPLOUF"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:553
msgid ""
"Because every Prinplup considers itself\\nto be the most important, they can"
" never\\nform a group. It searches for prey in\\nicy seas."
msgstr ""
"Chaque Prinplouf se croit le plus\\nimportant, si bien qu’ils ne forment "
"jamais\\nde groupe. Il chasse ses proies dans les\\nmers glacées."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:632
msgid "EMPOLEON"
msgstr "PINGOLEON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:635
msgid "Emperor"
msgstr "Empereur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:638
msgid ""
"The three horns that extend from its\\nbeak attest to its power. It "
"avoids\\nunnecessary disputes, but it will decimate\\nanything that "
"threatens its pride."
msgstr ""
"Les trois cornes de son bec attestent de\\nsa puissance. Il évite les "
"conflits\\ninutiles, mais anéantit quiconque menace\\nsa fierté."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:706
msgid "STARLY"
msgstr "ETOURMI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:709
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:795
msgid "Starling"
msgstr "Étourneau"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:712
msgid ""
"They flock around mountains and fields,\\nchasing after bug Pokémon. "
"However,\\nthey bicker if the group grows too big.\\nTheir singing is noisy "
"and annoying."
msgstr ""
"Ils volent en bande dans les montagnes et\\nles champs pour chasser les "
"Pokémon\\nInsecte. Trop nombreux, ils se chamaillent\\nbruyamment."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:792
msgid "STARAVIA"
msgstr "ETOURVOL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:798
msgid ""
"Recognizing their own weakness, they\\nmaintain huge flocks. Fierce "
"scuffles\\nbreak out between various flocks.\\nWhen alone, a Staravia cries "
"noisily."
msgstr ""
"Conscients de leur faiblesse, ils vivent en\\ngrandes volées qui se "
"querellent\\nviolemment. Seul, un Étourvol piaille\\nbruyamment."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:881
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:970
msgid "STARAPTOR"
msgstr "ETOURAPTOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:884
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:977
msgid "Predator"
msgstr "Rapace"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:887
msgid ""
"When Staravia evolve into Staraptor,\\nthey leave the flock to live alone. "
"It has\\na savage nature. It will courageously\\nchallenge foes that are "
"much larger."
msgstr ""
"En évoluant, les Étourvol quittent leur\\nvolée pour vivre seuls. D’un "
"naturel féroce,\\nil défie sans peur des ennemis bien plus\\ngrands."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:980
msgid ""
"Mega Staraptor is a top-class flier.\\nIt can easily soar through the sky "
"while\\ngripping a Steelix that weighs more than\\n880 lbs."
msgstr ""
"MEGA-ETOURAPTOR est un aviateur hors\\npair. Il fend aisément le ciel en "
"tenant\\ndans ses serres un STEELIX de plus de\\n400 kg."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1032
msgid "BIDOOF"
msgstr "KEUNOTOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1035
msgid "Plump Mouse"
msgstr "Souridodue"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1038
msgid ""
"A comparison revealed that Bidoof's front\\nteeth grow at the same rate as "
"Rattata's.\\nIt constantly gnaws on logs and rocks to\\nwhittle down its "
"front teeth."
msgstr ""
"Ses incisives poussent aussi vite que\\ncelles des Rattata. Il ronge sans "
"arrêt\\nbois et pierres pour les user."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1119
msgid "BIBAREL"
msgstr "CASTORNO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1122
msgid "Beaver"
msgstr "Castor"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1125
msgid ""
"It makes its nest by damming streams\\nwith bark and mud. A river dammed "
"by\\nBibarel will never overflow its banks,\\nwhich is appreciated by people"
" nearby."
msgstr ""
"Il construit des barrages de bois et de\\nboue. Une rivière endiguée par "
"Castorno ne\\ndéborde jamais, au grand bonheur des\\nriverains."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1203
msgid "KRICKETOT"
msgstr "CRIKZIK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1206
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1303
msgid "Cricket"
msgstr "Criquet"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1209
msgid ""
"It shakes its head back to front,\\ncausing its antennae to hit each "
"other\\nand sound like a xylophone.\\nThese sounds are fall hallmarks."
msgstr ""
"Il secoue la tête d’avant en arrière pour\\nentrechoquer ses antennes, qui "
"sonnent\\ncomme un xylophone. Ce son annonce\\nl’automne."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1300
msgid "KRICKETUNE"
msgstr "MELOKRIK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1306
msgid ""
"It signals its emotions with its melodies.\\nThere is a village that hosts a"
" contest\\nbased on the amazingly variable cries\\nof this Pokémon."
msgstr ""
"Il exprime ses émotions par ses mélodies.\\nUn village organise un concours "
"basé sur\\nles cris étonnamment variés de ce Pokémon."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1387
msgid "SHINX"
msgstr "LIXY"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1390
msgid "Flash"
msgstr "Flash"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1393
msgid ""
"It rapidly contracts and relaxes its\\nmuscles to generate electricity. "
"Its\\nbody shines if endangered. It flees\\nwhile the foe is momentarily "
"blinded."
msgstr ""
"Il contracte ses muscles pour produire de\\nl’électricité. En danger, son "
"corps brille. Il\\nfuit pendant que l’ennemi est aveuglé."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1470
msgid "LUXIO"
msgstr "LUXIO"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1473
msgid "Spark"
msgstr "Etincelle"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1476
msgid ""
"Strong electricity courses through the\\ntips of its sharp claws. A light "
"scratch\\nhas enough amperage to cause fainting\\nin foes."
msgstr ""
"Un fort courant électrique parcourt le\\nbout de ses griffes acérées. Une "
"simple\\négratignure suffit à assommer l’ennemi."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1557
msgid "LUXRAY"
msgstr "LUXRAY"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1560
msgid "Gleam Eyes"
msgstr "Brillœil"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1563
msgid ""
"It has eyes which can see through\\nanything. Luxray's ability to "
"see\\nthrough objects comes in handy when\\nit's scouting for danger."
msgstr ""
"Ses yeux peuvent voir à travers n’importe\\nquoi. Ce don permet à Luxray de "
"repérer le\\nmoindre danger."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1642
msgid "CRANIDOS"
msgstr "KRANIDOS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1645
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1714
msgid "Head Butt"
msgstr "Coud’Boule"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1648
msgid ""
"A lifelong jungle dweller from 100 million\\nyears ago, its skull is as hard"
" as iron. \\nIt would snap obstructing trees with\\nheadbutts."
msgstr ""
"Il vivait dans la jungle il y a 100 millions\\nd’années. Son crâne est dur "
"comme le fer. Il\\nabattait les arbres gênants à coups de\\ntête."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1711
msgid "RAMPARDOS"
msgstr "CHARKOS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1717
msgid ""
"The result of repeated headbutts\\nis a skull grown thick and "
"hard.\\nHowever, its brain has shrunk in size\\ncompared with Cranidos's."
msgstr ""
"À force d’enchaîner les coups de tête, sa\\ncalotte crânienne s’est "
"épaissie. Son\\ncerveau a donc dû rétrécir et il est plus\\npetit que celui "
"du Kranidos."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1783
msgid "SHIELDON"
msgstr "DINOCLIER"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1786
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1856
msgid "Shield"
msgstr "Bouclier"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1789
msgid ""
"This Pokémon lived in primeval jungles.\\nFew enemies would have been "
"willing to\\nsquare off against its heavily armored\\nface, so it's thought."
msgstr ""
"Grâce à sa tête très robuste, on suppose\\nqu’il n’avait que très peu "
"d’ennemis. Il\\nvivait dans les forêts primaires, il y a fort\\nlongtemps."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1853
msgid "BASTIODON"
msgstr "BASTIODON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1859
msgid ""
"Their rock-hard faces serve to protect\\nthem from any frontral "
"attacks.\\nWhen attacked, they form a wall.\\nThey shielded their young in "
"that way."
msgstr ""
"Leur face dure comme la roche les protège\\ndes attaques frontales. "
"Attaqués, ils\\nforment un mur. Ainsi protégeaient-ils\\nleurs petits."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1923
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1993
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2064
msgid "BURMY"
msgstr "CHENITI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1929
msgid ""
"If its cloak is even slightly damaged, it\\nwill immediately repair it with "
"whatever is\\nnear at hand. The Pokémon within the cloak\\nis scrawny and "
"vulnerable to the cold."
msgstr ""
"Si sa cape est abîmée, il la répare aussitôt\\navec ce qui lui tombe sous la"
" main. Le\\nPokémon qu’elle abrite est chétif et\\nfrileux."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:1999
msgid ""
"It weaves a cloak together with sand, mud,\\nand silk it spits out. This "
"earthen cloak\\nis ruined by wind and rain, so the Pokémon\\nhides away in "
"caves and other such places."
msgstr ""
"Il tisse sa cape avec du sable, de la\\nboue et la soie qu’il crache. "
"Vent\\net pluie l’abîment, donc il se cache\\ndans les grottes et autres "
"abris."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2070
msgid ""
"When confronted by a lack of other\\nmaterials, Burmy will create its "
"cloak\\nusing dust and refuse. The cloak seems to\\nbe more comfortable than"
" one would think."
msgstr ""
"À défaut d’autres matériaux, Cheniti\\nse fait une cape de poussière et "
"de\\ndéchets. Elle serait plus confortable\\nqu’on ne le pense."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2136
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2204
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2273
msgid "WORMADAM"
msgstr "CHENISELLE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2142
msgid ""
"Its appearance changes depending\\non where Burmy evolved. The "
"materials\\non hand become a part of its body.\\nThe cloak is never shed."
msgstr ""
"Son apparence dépend de l’endroit où\\nCheniti a évolué. Les matériaux "
"alentour\\nfont partie de son corps. Il ne quitte\\njamais sa cape."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2210
msgid ""
"Its earthen skin is reasonably hard, it has\\nno problem repelling a "
"Starly's pecking.\\nIt is said that a Wormadam that evolves\\non a cold day "
"will have a thicker cloak."
msgstr ""
"Sa peau de terre repousse sans mal\\nles coups de bec d’Étourmi. "
"Évolué\\npar temps froid, Cheniselle aurait\\nune cape plus épaisse."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2279
msgid ""
"Its body, composed of refuse, blends in to\\nthe scenery enough to be "
"inconspicuous.\\nThis seems to be the perfect way for it to\\nevade the "
"detection of predators."
msgstr ""
"Son corps fait de déchets se fond\\ndans le décor au point de "
"passer\\ninaperçu. Idéal pour échapper\\naux prédateurs."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2341
msgid "MOTHIM"
msgstr "PAPILORD"

#. source : patch FR actuel (correspondance douteuse, à vérifier)
#. source : patch FR actuel (récupéré par pointeur)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2344
msgid "Moth"
msgstr "Phalène"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2412
msgid "COMBEE"
msgstr "APITRINI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2415
msgid "Tiny Bee"
msgstr "Miniabeille"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2418
msgid ""
"A Pokémon formed by three others.\\nIt constantly gathers honey from "
"flowers\\nto please Vespiquen. At night, they\\ncluster to form a beehive "
"and sleep."
msgstr ""
"Un Pokémon formé de trois individus. Il\\nbutine sans cesse pour plaire à "
"Apireine.\\nLa nuit, ils s’agglutinent en ruche pour\\ndormir."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2500
msgid "VESPIQUEN"
msgstr "APIREINE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2503
msgid "Beehive"
msgstr "Ruche"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2506
msgid ""
"It houses its colony in cells in its body\\nand releases various pheromones "
"to\\nmake those grubs do its bidding.\\nThere is only one in a colony."
msgstr ""
"Son corps abrite les alvéoles de sa colonie.\\nIl émet des phéromones pour "
"commander\\nses larves. Il n’y en a qu’un par colonie."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2577
msgid "PACHIRISU"
msgstr "PACHIRISU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2580
msgid "EleSquirrel"
msgstr "Écurélec"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2583
msgid ""
"A pair may be seen rubbing their cheek\\npouches together in an effort to "
"share\\nstored electricity. It stores them with\\nberries in tree holes."
msgstr ""
"On voit parfois deux Pachirisu frotter\\nleurs joues pour partager leur "
"électricité.\\nIl en cache des boules avec ses Baies dans\\ndes troncs "
"creux."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2665
msgid "BUIZEL"
msgstr "MUSTEBOUEE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2668
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2749
msgid "Sea Weasel"
msgstr "Aquabelette"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2671
msgid ""
"It inflates its flotation sac, keeping its\\nface above water in order to "
"watch for\\nprey movement. It swims by rotating its\\ntwo tails like a "
"screw."
msgstr ""
"Il gonfle son flotteur pour garder la tête\\nhors de l’eau et guetter ses "
"proies. Il nage\\nen faisant tourner ses deux queues comme\\nune hélice."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2746
msgid "FLOATZEL"
msgstr "MUSTEFLOTT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2752
msgid ""
"Its flotation sac developed as a result\\nof pursuing aquatic prey. It can "
"double\\nas a rubber raft. It assists in the rescues\\nof drowning people."
msgstr ""
"Son flotteur s’est développé à force de\\nchasser des proies aquatiques. Il "
"sert de\\ncanot pneumatique pour secourir les gens\\nqui se noient."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2832
msgid "CHERUBI"
msgstr "CERIBOU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2835
msgid "Cherry"
msgstr "Cerise"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2838
msgid ""
"The small ball holds the nutrients needed\\nfor evolution. Apparently, it is"
" also very\\nsweet and tasty. Pokémon like Starly and\\nTaillow try to peck "
"it off."
msgstr ""
"La petite boule contient les nutriments\\nnécessaires à son évolution. Douce"
" et\\nsavoureuse, elle attire les becs des\\nÉtourmi et des Nirondelle."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2910
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2983
msgid "CHERRIM"
msgstr "CERIFLOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2913
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2986
msgid "Blossom"
msgstr "Floraison"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2916
msgid ""
"It's motionless, save for the occasional\\nquiver. A rich array of Pokémon "
"can be\\nfound gathered around it, drawn by the\\nscent exuded from "
"Cherrim's folded petals."
msgstr ""
"Il reste immobile, parfois frémissant. De\\nnombreux Pokémon se rassemblent "
"autour de\\nlui, attirés par le parfum de ses pétales\\nrepliés."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:2989
msgid ""
"Cherrim takes this form on sunny days.\\nIts faint scent entices bug Pokémon"
" to it.\\nIt immediately closes its petals and\\nbecomes immobile once the "
"sun hides."
msgstr ""
"Ceriflor prend cette forme au soleil.\\nSon doux parfum attire les "
"Pokémon\\nInsecte. Il se referme et se fige\\ndès que le soleil se cache."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3059
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3127
msgid "SHELLOS"
msgstr "SANCOKI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3062
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3130
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3198
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3264
msgid "Sea Slug"
msgstr "Aqualimace"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3065
msgid ""
"It oozes a purple fluid to deter enemies.\\nWhile harmless, the fluid is "
"awfully sticky.\\nApparently, there are more West Sea\\nShellos now than "
"there were in the past."
msgstr ""
"Il sécrète un liquide violet inoffensif\\nmais très collant pour repousser "
"l’ennemi.\\nLes Sancoki Mer Occident seraient plus\\nnombreux qu’avant."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3133
msgid ""
"It's capable of spending a limited amount\\nof time on land until their skin"
" dries out.\\nOne theory suggests that living in cold\\nseas causes Shellos "
"to take on this form."
msgstr ""
"Il peut rester un temps sur terre,\\njusqu’à ce que sa peau sèche. "
"Vivre\\ndans des mers froides donnerait\\ncette forme à Sancoki."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3195
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3261
msgid "GASTRODON"
msgstr "TRITOSOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3201
msgid ""
"It appears on shallow-water beaches to\\neat sand for nourishment. Should "
"one\\nGastrodon encounter another of a\\ndifferent color, a fierce battle "
"will ensue."
msgstr ""
"Il vit sur les plages et se nourrit de sable.\\nQuand deux Tritosor de "
"couleurs\\ndifférentes se croisent, le combat est\\nféroce."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3267
msgid ""
"Found more often on land than in the sea.\\nThey normally live in rocky "
"seashores, but\\nwhen cloudy or rainy, they can sometimes\\nbe found on "
"mountains, far from the sea."
msgstr ""
"On le trouve plus sur terre qu’en\\nmer. Il vit sur les côtes "
"rocheuses,\\nmais par temps pluvieux, on le voit\\nparfois en montagne."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3330
msgid "DRIFLOON"
msgstr "BAUDRIVE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3336
msgid ""
"Because of the way it floats aimlessly,\\nan old folktale calls it a "
"“Signpost for\\nWandering Spirits.” Children holding\\nthem sometimes "
"vanish."
msgstr ""
"Comme il flotte sans but, un vieux conte\\nl’appelle “le Guide des âmes "
"errantes”. Les\\nenfants qui en tiennent un disparaissent\\nparfois."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3403
msgid "DRIFBLIM"
msgstr "GRODRIVE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3406
msgid "Blimp"
msgstr "Ballon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3409
msgid ""
"Even while under careful observation,\\nlarge flocks of Drifblim flying at "
"dusk\\nwill inexplicably disappear from view.\\nNo one knows where they go."
msgstr ""
"Même observés de près, les vols de Grodrive\\nau crépuscule "
"disparaissent\\nmystérieusement. Nul ne sait où ils vont."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3477
msgid "BUNEARY"
msgstr "LAPOREILLE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3480
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3549
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3624
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:282
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:347
msgid "Rabbit"
msgstr "Lapin"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3483
msgid ""
"You can tell how it feels by the way\\nit rolls its ears. When it's "
"scared,\\nboth ears are rolled up. When it senses\\ndanger, it perks them "
"up."
msgstr ""
"La position de ses oreilles trahit son\\nhumeur. Effrayé, il les enroule. "
"S’il sent un\\ndanger, il les dresse."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3546
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3617
msgid "LOPUNNY"
msgstr "LOCKPIN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3552
msgid ""
"An extremely cautious Pokémon.\\nIt is very conscious of its looks "
"and\\nnever fails to groom its ears.\\nIt runs with sprightly jumps."
msgstr ""
"Un Pokémon extrêmement prudent. Soucieux\\nde son apparence, il ne manque "
"jamais de\\nlisser ses oreilles. Il court par bonds\\nlégers."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3627
msgid ""
"Mega Evolution awakens its combative\\ninstincts. It has shed any fur that "
"got in\\nthe way of its attacks.\\ncrescent."
msgstr ""
"La Méga-Évolution éveille son instinct\\ncombatif. Il s’est débarrassé de "
"toute\\nfourrure qui gênait ses attaques."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3694
msgid "GLAMEOW"
msgstr "CHAGLAM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3697
msgid "Catty"
msgstr "Chafouin"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3700
msgid ""
"It is a very fickle Pokémon, which is \\nvery popular among some. It claws "
"its\\nTrainer's nose if it isn't fed and\\npurrs when affectionate."
msgstr ""
"Un Pokémon capricieux, mais très apprécié\\nde certains. Il griffe le nez de"
" son\\nDresseur s’il a faim, et ronronne quand il\\nest content."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3764
msgid "PURUGLY"
msgstr "CHAFFREUX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3767
msgid "Tiger Cat"
msgstr "Chatigre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3770
msgid ""
"It is a brazen brute that barges its way\\ninto another Pokémon's nest and "
"claims\\nit as its own. It binds its body with its\\ntails to make itself "
"look bigger."
msgstr ""
"Une brute effrontée qui s’installe sans\\ngêne dans le nid d’autres Pokémon."
" Il se\\nceinture de ses queues pour paraître plus\\ngros."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3838
msgid "STUNKY"
msgstr "MOUFOUETTE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3841
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3913
msgid "Skunk"
msgstr "Moufette"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3844
msgid ""
"It protects itself by spraying a\\nnose-curling, stinky fluid from its "
"rear\\nto repel attackers. The stench lingers\\nfor 24 hours."
msgstr ""
"Pour se défendre, il projette par l’arrière\\nun liquide puant qui fait fuir"
" ses ennemis.\\nL’odeur persiste pendant 24 heures."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3910
msgid "SKUNTANK"
msgstr "MOUFFLAIR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3916
msgid ""
"It attacks by spraying a horribly smelly\\nfluid from the tip of its tail. "
"The fluid\\nsmells worse the longer it is allowed\\nto fester."
msgstr ""
"Il attaque en projetant un liquide\\nnauséabond par le bout de sa queue. "
"Plus ce\\nliquide macère, plus il empeste."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3981
msgid "BRONZOR"
msgstr "ARCHEOMIRE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3984
msgid "Bronze"
msgstr "Bronze"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:3987
msgid ""
"Implements shaped like it were discovered\\nin ancient tombs. There are "
"researchers\\nwho believe this Pokémon reflected like a\\nmirror in the "
"distant past."
msgstr ""
"Des objets à son effigie ont été trouvés\\ndans d’anciens tombeaux. "
"Certains\\nchercheurs pensent qu’il servait jadis de\\nmiroir."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4060
msgid "BRONZONG"
msgstr "ARCHEODONG"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4063
msgid "Bronze Bell"
msgstr "Clochebronze"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4066
msgid ""
"In ages past, this Pokémon was revered as\\na bringer of rain. One caused a "
"news stir\\nwhen it was dug up at a construction site\\nafter a 2000-year "
"sleep."
msgstr ""
"Jadis vénéré comme un porteur de pluie.\\nL’un d’eux fit sensation en étant "
"déterré\\nsur un chantier après 2000 ans de sommeil."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4134
msgid "CHATOT"
msgstr "PIJAKO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4137
msgid "Music Note"
msgstr "Note Musique"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4140
msgid ""
"It mimics the cries of other Pokémon to\\ntrick them into thinking it's one "
"of them.\\nThis way they won't attack it. It can\\nalso learn and speak "
"human words."
msgstr ""
"Il imite les cris d’autres Pokémon pour se\\nfaire passer pour l’un d’eux et"
" éviter leurs\\nattaques. Il peut aussi apprendre à parler."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4221
msgid "SPIRITOMB"
msgstr "SPIRITOMB"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4224
msgid "Forbidden"
msgstr "Interdit"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4227
msgid ""
"A Pokémon that was formed by 108 spirits.\\nIts constant mischief and "
"misdeeds\\nresulted in it being bound to an\\nOdd Keystone by a mysterious "
"spell."
msgstr ""
"Un Pokémon formé de 108 esprits. Ses\\nméfaits incessants lui ont valu "
"d’être lié à\\nune Clé de Voûte par un sort mystérieux."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4291
msgid "GIBLE"
msgstr "GRIKNOT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4294
msgid "Land Shark"
msgstr "Terrequin"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel (adapté)
#. lot : B_soulsilver
#. preuve : 803:443 — Il niche dans des cavités chauffées\npar géothermie,
#. dont il bondit pour\ndéchiqueter tout intrus.
#. ancien (patch FR actuel) : Il niche dans des terriers tiédis par
#. la\nchaleur du sous-sol. Gare aux imprudents:\nil leur saute dessus pour
#. les mordre.
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4297
msgid ""
"It nests in horizontal holes warmed by\\ngeothermal heat. Foes who stray "
"too\\nclose can expect to be pounced on\\nand bitten."
msgstr ""
"Il niche dans des cavités chauffées\\npar géothermie, dont il bondit "
"pour\\ndéchiqueter tout intrus."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4374
msgid "GABITE"
msgstr "CARMACHE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4380
msgid ""
"Shiny objects are its passion. It can be\\nfound in its cave, scarcely "
"moving,\\nits gaze fixed on the jewels it's amassed\\nor Carbink it has "
"caught."
msgstr ""
"Il adore tout ce qui brille. Au fond de sa\\ntanière, il contemple les "
"joyaux qu’il a\\ndérobés et les Strassie qu’il a kidnappés."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4461
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4546
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4628
msgid "GARCHOMP"
msgstr "CARCHACROK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4464
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4553
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4635
msgid "Mach"
msgstr "Supersonic"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4467
msgid ""
"When it folds up its body and extends its\\nwings, it looks like a jet "
"plane. It is\\ncovered in fine scales that reduce drag,\\nenabling it to fly"
" at high speeds."
msgstr ""
"Quand il replie son corps et déploie ses\\nailes, il ressemble à un avion à "
"réaction.\\nSes fines écailles lui permettent de voler\\ntrès vite."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4556
msgid ""
"Excess energy melted its arms and wings\\ninto giant scythes, sending it mad"
" with\\nrage. It swings its scythes wildly and\\nslices the ground to "
"pieces."
msgstr ""
"Un excès d’énergie a fait fondre ses\\nbras et ses ailes, devenus "
"d’immenses\\lfaux. Fou de rage, il les agite et\\ldécoupe le sol."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4638
msgid ""
"Garchomp has gained a new Mega-Evolved\\nform. It flies around foes at Mach "
"speed\\nand cuts them to shreds with its sinister\\nwing claws."
msgstr ""
"CARCHACROK a une nouvelle forme\\nméga-évoluée. Il décrit des "
"cercles\\lautour de ses ennemis à Mach 1. Ses\\lgriffes sinistres les "
"lacèrent."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4690
msgid "RIOLU"
msgstr "RIOLU"

#. source : patch FR actuel (récupéré par pointeur)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4693
msgid "Emanation"
msgstr "Émanation"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4696
msgid ""
"It can discern the physical and emotional\\nstates of people, Pokémon, and "
"other\\nnatural things from the shape of their\\naura waves."
msgstr ""
"Il perçoit sous forme d’ondes les émotions\\ndes humains et des Pokémon, "
"ainsi que tout\\nce qui l’entoure."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4762
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4833
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4910
msgid "LUCARIO"
msgstr "LUCARIO"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4765
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4840
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4917
msgid "Aura"
msgstr "Aura"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4768
msgid ""
"It understands human speech.\\nIt is said that no foe can remain "
"invisible\\nto Lucario, since it can detect Auras.\\nEven foes it could not "
"otherwise see."
msgstr ""
"Il comprend le langage humain. Lucario\\nperçoit les auras, si bien qu’aucun"
" ennemi\\nne peut se cacher de lui, même invisible."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4843
msgid ""
"It readies itself to face its enemies by\\nfocusing its mental energies. Its"
" fighting\\nstyle can be summed up in a single word:\\nheartless."
msgstr ""
"Il se prépare à affronter ses ennemis\\nen concentrant son énergie "
"mentale.\\lSon style de combat se résume en un\\lmot: impitoyable."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4920
msgid ""
"By completely cloaking itself in its aura,\\nMega Lucario Z can parry all "
"manner of\\nattacks, battling as if it were gracefully\\ndancing."
msgstr ""
"En s’enveloppant entièrement de son\\naura, MEGA-LUCARIO Z pare toutes "
"sortes\\nd’attaques et combat comme s’il dansait\\navec grâce."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4972
msgid "HIPPOPOTAS"
msgstr "HIPPOPOTAS"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4975
msgid "Hippo"
msgstr "Hippo"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:4978
msgid ""
"Hippopotas shuts its nostrils tight when\\ntravelling through sand. Instead "
"of\\nperspiration, it expels grains of sand\\nfrom its body."
msgstr ""
"Hippopotas ferme bien ses narines quand il\\nse déplace dans le sable. Au "
"lieu de\\ntranspirer, il rejette des grains de sable."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5057
msgid "HIPPOWDON"
msgstr "HIPPODOCUS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5060
msgid "Heavyweight"
msgstr "Poids Lourd"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5063
msgid ""
"It is surprisingly quick to anger.\\nIt brandishes its gaping mouth in "
"a\\ndisplay of fearsome strength and raises\\nvast quantities of sand while "
"attacking."
msgstr ""
"Il se met vite en colère. Il ouvre grand sa\\ngueule pour montrer sa force "
"et soulève\\nd’énormes quantités de sable pour\\nattaquer."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5139
msgid "SKORUPI"
msgstr "RAPION"

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main (le patch FR actuel donnait un morceau
#. d’un autre texte)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5142
msgid "Scorpion"
msgstr "Scorpion"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5145
msgid ""
"It grips prey with its tail claws and\\ninjects poison. It tenaciously "
"hangs\\non until the poison takes.\\nIt can survive a year without food."
msgstr ""
"Il agrippe sa proie avec les pinces de sa\\nqueue et lui injecte du poison "
"sans lâcher\\nprise. Il peut jeûner pendant un an."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5223
msgid "DRAPION"
msgstr "DRASCORE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5226
msgid "Ogre Scorp"
msgstr "Scorpogre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5229
msgid ""
"Possessing a sturdy build, it takes\\npride in its strength. It has the "
"power\\nin its clawed arms to make scrap\\nout of a car."
msgstr ""
"Doté d’un corps robuste, il est fier de sa\\nforce. Ses bras griffus peuvent"
" réduire\\nune voiture en tas de ferraille."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5300
msgid "CROAGUNK"
msgstr "CRADOPAUD"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5303
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5388
msgid "Toxic Mouth"
msgstr "Toxique"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5306
msgid ""
"Croagunk rarely fights fairly. Inflating\\nits poison sacs, it fills the "
"area with\\nan odd sound and hits flinching\\nopponents with a poison jab."
msgstr ""
"Cradopaud se bat rarement à la loyale. Il\\ngonfle ses poches à venin, émet "
"un son\\nétrange et frappe l’ennemi apeuré d’un\\nDirect Toxik."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5385
msgid "TOXICROAK"
msgstr "COATOX"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Il lance un coassement viril de victoire\nquand il
#. parvient à terrasser sa proie. Il\ns’apparente aux Crapustule.
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5391
msgid ""
"Swaying and dodging the attacks\\nof its foes, it weaves its flexible "
"body\\nin close, then lunges out with its\\npoisonous claws."
msgstr ""
"Il esquive les attaques avec\\nsouplesse et riposte d’un bond avec\\lses "
"griffes empoisonnées."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5471
msgid "CARNIVINE"
msgstr "VORTENTE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Chopinsecte
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5474
msgid "Bug Catcher"
msgstr "Scout"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5477
msgid ""
"Hanging from branches using its\\ntentacles, it looks like a plant.\\nIt "
"attracts prey with its sweet-smelling\\nsaliva, then chomps down."
msgstr ""
"Suspendu aux branches par ses tentacules,\\nil ressemble à une plante. Il "
"attire ses\\nproies avec sa salive parfumée, puis les\\ncroque."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5552
msgid "FINNEON"
msgstr "ECAYON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5555
msgid "Wing Fish"
msgstr "Poisson Ailé"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5558
msgid ""
"Its double tail fins propel its energetic\\njumps. When it breaks the "
"surface of the\\nsea, Wingull swoop down to grab it on\\nthe fly."
msgstr ""
"Avec sa double nageoire caudale, il peut\\nbondir hors de l’eau. C’est "
"souvent à ce\\nmoment que les Goélise de passage\\nl’attrapent et le gobent."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5640
msgid "LUMINEON"
msgstr "LUMINEON"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5643
msgid "Neon"
msgstr "Neon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5646
msgid ""
"Lumineon swimming in the darkness\\nof the deep sea look like stars "
"shining\\nin the night sky. It competes for food\\nwith Lanturn."
msgstr ""
"Dans les abysses, les Luminéon brillent\\ncomme des étoiles dans un ciel "
"nocturne. Il\\ndispute sa nourriture aux Lanturn."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5727
msgid "SNOVER"
msgstr "BLIZZI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5730
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5815
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5903
msgid "Frost Tree"
msgstr "Arbregelé"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5733
msgid ""
"During cold seasons, it migrates to the\\nmountain's lower reaches. "
"Seemingly\\ncurious about people, they gather around\\nfootsteps they find "
"on snowy mountains."
msgstr ""
"En hiver, il descend au pied des montagnes.\\nCurieux des humains, il se "
"rassemble autour\\ndes empreintes laissées dans la neige."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5812
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5896
msgid "ABOMASNOW"
msgstr "BLIZZAROI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5818
msgid ""
"It lives a quiet life on mountains that\\nare perpetually covered in snow. "
"It hides\\nitself by whipping up blizzards.\\nIt is also known as “The Ice "
"Monster.”"
msgstr ""
"Il vit paisiblement dans les montagnes aux\\nneiges éternelles et se cache "
"en soulevant\\ndes blizzards. On le surnomme “le Monstre\\ndes Glaces”."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5906
msgid ""
"The sprouts on Abomasnow's back grow into\\ngreat shafts of ice when it Mega"
" Evolves.\\nDislikes associating with others and\\nchooses to live quietly "
"deep in mountains."
msgstr ""
"Les pousses du dos de BLIZZAROI\\ndeviennent de grands piliers de "
"glace\\nquand il méga-évolue. Solitaire, il vit\\ntranquillement au fond des"
" montagnes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5976
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6062
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6140
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6217
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6293
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6394
msgid "ROTOM"
msgstr "MOTISMA"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5979
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6065
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6143
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6220
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6296
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6397
msgid "Plasma"
msgstr "Plasma"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:5982
msgid ""
"Its body is composed of plasma and loves\\nto surprise others. One boy's "
"invention led\\nto the development of many machines that\\ncan use of "
"Rotom's unique capabilities."
msgstr ""
"Son corps est fait de plasma et il adore\\nsurprendre. L’invention d’un "
"garçon a\\npermis de créer des machines tirant parti\\nde ses pouvoirs."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6068
msgid ""
"If the convection microwave oven is\\nnot working properly, then the "
"Rotom\\ninhabiting it will become lethargic. It\\nmakes mischief by turning "
"up the heat."
msgstr ""
"Si le four à micro-ondes marche\\nmal, le Motisma qui l’habite "
"devient\\nléthargique. Il fait des bêtises\\nen montant le chauffage."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6146
msgid ""
"It enjoys coming up with water-based\\npranks. The model of washing machine "
"that\\nRotom can inspirit has been discontinued,\\nso they are now traded at"
" high prices."
msgstr ""
"Il adore les farces aquatiques. Le\\nlave-linge qu’il peut posséder "
"n’est\\nplus fabriqué et se vend donc\\nà prix d’or."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6223
msgid ""
"In this form, Rotom likes to play freezing\\ncold pranks. You may find it's "
"turned the\\nbath you just filled to solid ice!\\nIt battles by spewing cold"
" air."
msgstr ""
"Sous cette forme, Motisma adore les\\nfarces glaciales, comme "
"changer\\nvotre bain en bloc de glace! Il se\\nbat en soufflant de l’air "
"froid."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6299
msgid ""
"The first appliance developed that Rotom\\ncoud inspirit was the electric "
"fan. It uses\\nits power over wind in its pranks, happily\\nblowing any "
"important documents it finds."
msgstr ""
"Le ventilateur fut le premier\\nappareil que Motisma put posséder.\\nIl "
"manie le vent pour ses farces et\\nfait voler les documents importants."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6400
msgid ""
"The lawn mower is an appliance that led to\\nthe development of the Rotom "
"Dex. It will\\nmow down grass and flowers, then swagger\\naround with pride "
"at its accomplishments."
msgstr ""
"La tondeuse est l’appareil qui a\\nmené au Motismadex. Il tond herbe\\net "
"fleurs, puis se pavane, fier de\\nson exploit."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6477
msgid "UXIE"
msgstr "CREHELF"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6483
msgid ""
"Known as ”The Being of Knowledge,”\\naccording to some sources, this "
"Pokémon\\nprovided people with the intelligence\\nnecessary to solve various"
" problems."
msgstr ""
"Surnommé “l’Être du Savoir”, il aurait donné\\naux humains l’intelligence "
"nécessaire pour\\nrésoudre leurs problèmes."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6558
msgid "MESPRIT"
msgstr "CREFOLLET"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6564
msgid ""
"Although it slumbers at the bottom of a\\nlake, its spirit is said to leave "
"its body\\nand flitter on the water surface. It\\ntaught humans of sorrow, "
"pain, and joy."
msgstr ""
"Il dort au fond d’un lac, mais son esprit\\nflotterait à la surface. Il a "
"enseigné aux\\nhumains la tristesse, la douleur et la joie."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6643
msgid "AZELF"
msgstr "CREFADET"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6646
msgid "Willpower"
msgstr "Volonté"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6649
msgid ""
"This Pokémon is said to have endowed\\nhumans with the determination needed "
"to\\ndo things. It is thought that Uxie, Mesprit\\nand Azelf all came from "
"the same egg."
msgstr ""
"Il aurait donné aux humains la volonté\\nd’agir. Créhelf, Créfollet et "
"Créfadet\\nseraient tous nés du même œuf."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6722
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6794
msgid "DIALGA"
msgstr "DIALGA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6725
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6797
msgid "Temporal"
msgstr "Temps"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6728
msgid ""
"A Pokémon spoken of in legend.\\nIt completely controls the flow of "
"time.\\nIt uses its power to travel at will\\nthrough the past and future."
msgstr ""
"Un Pokémon de légende. Il contrôle\\nentièrement le flux du temps et "
"peut\\nvoyager à sa guise dans le passé et le\\nfutur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6800
msgid ""
"Radiant light caused Dialga to take on a\\nform bearing a striking "
"resemblance to the\\ncreator Pokémon. It wields such a colossal\\nstrength "
"that this might be its true form."
msgstr ""
"Une lumière radieuse a donné à\\nDialga l’allure du Pokémon créateur.\\nSa "
"force est si colossale qu’il\\npourrait s’agir de sa vraie forme."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6872
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6944
msgid "PALKIA"
msgstr "PALKIA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6875
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6947
msgid "Spatial"
msgstr "Espace"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6878
msgid ""
"Palkia has the ability to distort space.\\nIts total control over the "
"boundaries of\\nspace enable it to transport itself to\\nfaraway places and "
"other dimensions."
msgstr ""
"Palkia peut distordre l’espace. Il en\\nmaîtrise si bien les limites qu’il "
"peut se\\nrendre en des lieux lointains ou dans\\nd’autres dimensions."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:6950
msgid ""
"It soars across the sky in a form that\\nresembles the creator of all "
"things.\\nPerhaps this imitation of appearance is a\\nstrategy for gaining "
"Arceus's powers."
msgstr ""
"Il fend le ciel sous une forme qui\\nrappelle le créateur de toute "
"chose.\\nIl l’imite peut-être pour obtenir\\nles pouvoirs d’Arceus."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7022
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7101
msgid "HEATRAN"
msgstr "HEATRAN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7025
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7108
msgid "Lava Dome"
msgstr "Caldeira"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7028
msgid ""
"Boiling blood, like magma, circulates\\nthrough its body. It dwells in "
"volcanic\\ncaves, using its cross-shaped feet\\nto crawl on ceilings and "
"walls."
msgstr ""
"Un sang bouillant comme le magma coule\\ndans ses veines. Il vit dans les "
"grottes\\nvolcaniques et rampe aux murs et aux\\nplafonds."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7111
msgid ""
"It's said that if it goes all out, it\\ncan heat its body up to "
"temperatures\\nover 1.8 million degrees Fahrenheit.\\nThis heat keeps "
"enemies at bay."
msgstr ""
"On dit qu’à pleine puissance, il peut\\nchauffer son corps à plus d’un "
"million\\nde degrés. Cette chaleur tient ses\\nennemis à distance."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7170
msgid "REGIGIGAS"
msgstr "REGIGIGAS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7173
msgid "Colossal"
msgstr "Prodigieux"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7176
msgid ""
"There is an enduring legend that\\nstates this Pokémon shaped "
"Regirock,\\nRegice, and Registeel out of clay, ice,\\nand magma."
msgstr ""
"Une légende tenace prétend que ce Pokémon\\na modelé Regirock, Regice et "
"Registeel dans\\nl’argile, la glace et le magma."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7249
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7322
msgid "GIRATINA"
msgstr "GIRATINA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7252
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7325
msgid "Renegade"
msgstr "Renégat"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7255
msgid ""
"This Pokémon is said to live in a world\\non the reverse side of ours, where"
" common\\nknowledge is distorted and strange.\\nIt was banished for its "
"violence."
msgstr ""
"Il vivrait dans un monde inversé, où les\\nlois de la nature sont étranges "
"et\\ndéformées. Il y fut banni pour sa violence."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7328
msgid ""
"Giratina loses its legs upon changing into\\nthis form. It's believed it "
"hails from a\\nworld where the heavens and the earth\\nare as one."
msgstr ""
"Giratina perd ses pattes sous cette\\nforme. Il viendrait d’un monde où\\nle"
" ciel et la terre ne font qu’un."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7409
msgid "CRESSELIA"
msgstr "CRESSELIA"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Lunaire
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7412
msgid "Lunar"
msgstr "Lunar"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel (adapté)
#. lot : B_soulsilver
#. preuve : 804:488 — Dormir avec une de ses plumes à la main\npermet de faire
#. de beaux rêves. On le\nsurnomme “avatar du croissant de lune”.
#. ancien (patch FR actuel) : Qui dort en tenant une de ses plumes fait\nde
#. beaux rêves. On dit qu’il incarne le\ncroissant de lune.
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7415
msgid ""
"Those who sleep holding one of\\nCresselia's feathers are assured "
"of\\njoyful dreams. It is said to represent\\nthe crescent moon."
msgstr ""
"Dormir avec une de ses plumes à la\\nmain permet de faire de beaux "
"rêves.\\nOn le surnomme “avatar du croissant\\nde lune”."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7491
msgid "PHIONE"
msgstr "PHIONE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7494
msgid "Sea Drifter"
msgstr "Dérivenmer"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7497
msgid ""
"When the water warms, they inflate the\\nflotation sac on their heads and "
"drift\\nlanguidly on the sea in packs.\\nIt always returns to where it was "
"born."
msgstr ""
"Quand l’eau se réchauffe, ils gonflent leur\\nflotteur et dérivent en bande "
"au gré des\\nflots. Il revient toujours là où il est né."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7569
msgid "MANAPHY"
msgstr "MANAPHY"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7572
msgid "Seafaring"
msgstr "Voyagenmer"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7575
msgid ""
"Water makes up 80% of its body.\\nIt starts its life with a wondrous "
"power\\nthat permits it to bond with any kind\\nof Pokémon."
msgstr ""
"Son corps est composé à 80 % d’eau. Il naît\\navec l’étrange pouvoir de se "
"lier à toutes\\nsortes de Pokémon."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7652
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7734
msgid "DARKRAI"
msgstr "DARKRAI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7655
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7741
msgid "Pitch-Black"
msgstr "Noirtotal"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7658
msgid ""
"It chases people and Pokémon from its\\nterritory by causing them to "
"experience\\ndeep, nightmarish slumbers. However,\\nit means no harm."
msgstr ""
"Il chasse de son territoire humains et\\nPokémon en les plongeant dans de "
"terribles\\ncauchemars. Pourtant, il ne leur veut aucun\\nmal."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7744
msgid ""
"Its dark power blocks out the sun,\\nplunging the surrounding area "
"into\\ndarkness. There is no escaping its\\nevil eye."
msgstr ""
"Son pouvoir ténébreux masque le\\nsoleil et plonge les environs "
"dans\\nl’obscurité. Nul n’échappe à son œil\\nmaléfique."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7809
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7889
msgid "SHAYMIN"
msgstr "SHAYMIN"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7812
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7892
msgid "Gratitude"
msgstr "Gratitude"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7815
msgid ""
"The flowers all over its body bloom if it is\\nlovingly hugged and senses "
"gratitude. It\\ndissolves toxins in the air to transform\\nruined land into "
"a lush field of flowers."
msgstr ""
"Les fleurs de son corps éclosent quand on\\nl’enlace avec tendresse. Il "
"dissout les\\ntoxines de l’air et change les terres\\ndévastées en champs "
"fleuris."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7895
msgid ""
"Upon taking in the scent of a particular\\nrare flower, Shaymin is enveloped"
" in light\\nand its tiny body transforms, confering\\nthe power of flight "
"upon it."
msgstr ""
"En respirant le parfum d’une fleur\\nrare, Shaymin s’entoure de lumière\\net"
" son petit corps se transforme,\\nlui conférant le don de voler."

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7982
msgid "ARCEUS"
msgstr "ARCEUS"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_4_families.h:7985
msgid "Alpha"
msgstr "Alpha"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:26
msgid "VICTINI"
msgstr "VICTINI"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:29
msgid "Victory"
msgstr "VICTOIRE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:32
msgid ""
"This Pokémon brings victory.\\nIt is said that Trainers with "
"Victini\\nalways win, regardless of the type\\nof encounter."
msgstr ""
"Un Pokémon qui amène la victoire. On dit que\\nles Dresseurs qui le "
"possèdent peuvent\\ngagner n’importe quel combat."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:98
msgid "SNIVY"
msgstr "VIPELIERRE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:101
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:170
msgid "Grass Snake"
msgstr "Serpenterbe"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:104
msgid ""
"It is very intelligent and calm.\\nBeing exposed to lots of sunlight "
"makes\\nits movements swifter. When they are\\nnot feeling well, their tails"
" droop."
msgstr ""
"Il est très intelligent et calme. Le soleil\\nrend ses gestes plus vifs. "
"Quand il ne va\\npas bien, sa queue retombe."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:167
msgid "SERVINE"
msgstr "LIANAJA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:173
msgid ""
"When it gets dirty, its leaves can't be\\nused in photosynthesis, so it "
"always keeps\\nclean. They avoid attacks by sinking into\\nthe shadows of "
"thick foliage."
msgstr ""
"Sale, ses feuilles ne peuvent plus faire la\\nphotosynthèse, alors il reste "
"toujours\\npropre. Il esquive en se fondant dans les\\nfeuillages."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:239
msgid "SERPERIOR"
msgstr "MAJASPIC"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:242
msgid "Regal"
msgstr "Majestueux"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:245
msgid ""
"They raise their heads to intimidate foes,\\nbut only give it their all when"
" fighting\\npowerful opponents who are not fazed\\nby the glare from its "
"noble eyes."
msgstr ""
"Il dresse la tête pour intimider. Il ne se\\ndonne à fond que contre les "
"adversaires\\nqui ne cillent pas devant son noble regard."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:310
msgid "TEPIG"
msgstr "GRUIKUI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:313
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:384
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:453
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:547
msgid "Fire Pig"
msgstr "Cochon Feu"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:316
msgid ""
"It loves to eat roasted berries, but\\nsometimes it gets too excited and "
"burns\\nthem to a crisp. It blows fire through\\nits nose."
msgstr ""
"Il adore les Baies grillées, mais parfois\\nl’excitation lui fait les "
"carboniser. Il\\ncrache du feu par le nez."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:381
msgid "PIGNITE"
msgstr "GROTICHON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:387
msgid ""
"The more it eats, the more fuel it has\\nto make the fire in its stomach "
"stronger.\\nWhen it is angered, the intensity of the\\nflame increases."
msgstr ""
"Plus il mange, plus il a de combustible pour\\nattiser le feu de son ventre."
" Quand il se\\nfâche, sa flamme s’intensifie."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:450
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:540
msgid "EMBOAR"
msgstr "ROITIFLAM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:456
msgid ""
"It is adept at using many different moves.\\nIt can throw a fire punch by "
"setting its\\nfists on fire with its fiery chin.\\nIt cares deeply about its"
" friends."
msgstr ""
"Il maîtrise de nombreuses capacités. Il\\nenflamme ses poings avec sa barbe "
"de feu\\npour frapper. Il tient beaucoup à ses amis."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:550
msgid ""
"Brandishing a blazing flame\\nshaped like a serpentine spear,\\nit rushes in"
" to save its\\nimperiled allies."
msgstr ""
"Brandissant une flamme ardente en\\nforme de lance sinueuse, il fonce "
"au\\nsecours de ses alliés en péril."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:601
msgid "OSHAWOTT"
msgstr "MOUSTILLON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:604
msgid "Sea Otter"
msgstr "Loutre"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:607
msgid ""
"The scalchop on its stomach isn't just\\nused for battle, it can be used to "
"break\\nopen hard berries as well. It is made\\nfrom the same element as its"
" claws."
msgstr ""
"Le coquillage de son ventre lui sert au\\ncombat, mais aussi à ouvrir les "
"Baies dures.\\nIl est fait de la même matière que ses\\ngriffes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:674
msgid "DEWOTT"
msgstr "MATELOUTRE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:677
msgid "Discipline"
msgstr "Entraînement"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:680
msgid ""
"Strict training and disclipine leads it\\nto master its flowing double-"
"scalchop\\ntechnique. Scalchop techniques differ\\nfrom one Dewott to "
"another."
msgstr ""
"À force d’entraînement, il maîtrise une\\ntechnique fluide à deux "
"coquillages.\\nChaque Mateloutre a son propre style."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:748
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:819
msgid "SAMUROTT"
msgstr "CLAMIRAL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:751
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:827
msgid "Formidable"
msgstr "Dignitaire"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:754
msgid ""
"One swing of the seamitars attached\\nto its armor can fell an opponent.\\nA"
" simple glare from one of them is\\nenough to intimidate most enemies."
msgstr ""
"Un seul coup des épées de son armure abat\\nun ennemi. Un simple regard de "
"sa part\\nsuffit à intimider la plupart des\\nadversaires."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:817
msgid "SAMUROTT-H"
msgstr "CLAMIRAL-H"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:830
msgid ""
"Hard of heart and deft of blade,\\nthis rare form of Samurott is a\\nproduct"
" of the Pokémon's evolution in the\\nregion of Hisui."
msgstr ""
"Cœur de pierre et lame habile, cette forme\\nrare de Clamiral est le fruit "
"de son\\névolution dans la région de Hisui."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:897
msgid "PATRAT"
msgstr "RATENTIF"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:903
msgid ""
"Extremely cautious, they take shifts to\\nmaintain a constant watch of their"
" nest.\\nUsing food stored in cheek pouches,\\nthey can keep watch for days."
msgstr ""
"Très prudents, ils montent la garde à tour\\nde rôle devant leur nid. Grâce "
"aux vivres\\nstockés dans leurs joues, ils veillent des\\njours."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:965
msgid "WATCHOG"
msgstr "MIRADAR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:968
msgid "Lookout"
msgstr "Vigilant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:971
msgid ""
"Using luminescent matter, it makes its\\neyes and body glow and stuns "
"attacking\\nopponents. Keen eyesight lets them see\\nin the dark."
msgstr ""
"Il fait briller ses yeux et son corps pour\\naveugler ses ennemis. Sa vue "
"perçante lui\\npermet de voir dans le noir."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1038
msgid "LILLIPUP"
msgstr "PONCHIOT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1044
msgid ""
"It faces strong opponents with great\\ncourage. Because it doesn't yelp, "
"it's\\nextremely popular with Trainers who live\\nin apartment buildings."
msgstr ""
"Il affronte les ennemis forts avec\\ncourage. Comme il n’aboie pas, il est "
"très\\nprisé des Dresseurs qui vivent en\\nappartement."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1111
msgid "HERDIER"
msgstr "PONCHIEN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1114
msgid "Loyal Dog"
msgstr "Chien Fidèle"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1117
msgid ""
"Its dense black fur grows continuously.\\nThe high cost of keeping its hard "
"fur\\nproperly groomed makes this a\\ntroublesome Pokémon to train."
msgstr ""
"Son poil noir et dur pousse sans cesse, et\\nson toilettage coûte un bras. "
"Une vraie\\nplaie à élever."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1188
msgid "STOUTLAND"
msgstr "MASTOUFFE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1191
msgid "Big-Hearted"
msgstr "Magnanime"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1194
msgid ""
"Intelligent, good-natured, and valiant,\\nthere could be no concern that it "
"would\\never attack people. Some parents even\\ntrust it to babysit."
msgstr ""
"Intelligent, gentil et courageux, il\\nn’attaque jamais les gens. "
"Certains\\nparents lui confient même la garde de leurs\\nenfants."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1259
msgid "PURRLOIN"
msgstr "CHACRIPAN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1262
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:4618
msgid "Devious"
msgstr "Scélérat"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1265
msgid ""
"Their deceptively cute act is the\\nperfect ruse. They steal from people "
"for\\nfun, but their victims can't help but\\nforgive them."
msgstr ""
"Ses airs mignons sont une ruse parfaite. Il\\nvole les gens pour s’amuser, "
"mais ses\\nvictimes ne peuvent s’empêcher de lui\\npardonner."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1328
msgid "LIEPARD"
msgstr "LEOPARDUS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1334
msgid ""
"Many Trainers are drawn to their\\nbeautiful form and fur. These "
"Pokémon\\nvanish and appear unexpectedly.\\nThey run silently in the night."
msgstr ""
"Bien des Dresseurs sont séduits par sa\\nsilhouette et son pelage. Il "
"apparaît et\\ndisparaît à l’improviste et court sans\\nbruit la nuit."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1397
msgid "PANSAGE"
msgstr "FEUILLAJOU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1400
msgid "Grass Monkey"
msgstr "Singe Herbe"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1403
msgid ""
"This Pokémon dwells deep in the forest.\\nIt's good at finding berries and "
"gathers\\nthem from all over. It's kind enough to\\nshare them with friends."
msgstr ""
"Il vit au fond des forêts. Doué pour\\ntrouver les Baies, il en récolte "
"partout et\\nles partage volontiers avec ses amis."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1468
msgid "SIMISAGE"
msgstr "FEUILOUTAN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1471
msgid "Thorn Monkey"
msgstr "Singépine"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1474
msgid ""
"Ill tempered, it attacks enemies by\\nswinging its barbed tail around "
"wildly.\\nThe leaf growing on its head is\\nvery bitter."
msgstr ""
"Colérique, il attaque en fouettant l’air de\\nsa queue épineuse. La feuille "
"qui pousse\\nsur sa tête est très amère."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1538
msgid "PANSEAR"
msgstr "FLAMAJOU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1541
msgid "High Temp"
msgstr "Brûlant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1544
msgid ""
"The fire within the tuft on its head can\\nreach up to 600ºF. Very "
"intelligent,\\nit roasts berries before eating them.\\nIt likes to help "
"people."
msgstr ""
"Le feu de sa houppe atteint 300 degrés.\\nTrès malin, il fait griller les "
"Baies avant de\\nles manger. Il aime aider les gens."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1607
msgid "SIMISEAR"
msgstr "FLAMOUTAN"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Braise
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1610
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1186
msgid "Ember"
msgstr "Flammèche"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1613
msgid ""
"It loves sweets because they become\\nenergy for the fire burning inside "
"its\\nbody. It scatters embers from its head\\nand tail to sear its "
"opponents."
msgstr ""
"Il adore les sucreries, qui nourrissent le\\nfeu de son corps. Il projette "
"des braises\\nde sa tête et de sa queue pour brûler ses\\nennemis."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1678
msgid "PANPOUR"
msgstr "FLOTAJOU"

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1681
msgid "Spray"
msgstr "Spray"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1684
msgid ""
"The water stored inside the tuft of its\\nhead is rich in nutrients. It "
"waters\\nplants using its tail, plants that\\nreceive its water grow large."
msgstr ""
"L’eau stockée dans sa houppe est très\\nnutritive. Il arrose les plantes "
"avec sa\\nqueue, et elles poussent alors très\\ngrandes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1747
msgid "SIMIPOUR"
msgstr "FLOTOUTAN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1750
msgid "Geyser"
msgstr "Drainage"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1753
msgid ""
"It can shoot highly-pressurised water\\nfrom its tail with enough power "
"to\\nbreak through a solid concrete wall.\\nIt prefers places with clean "
"water."
msgstr ""
"Il projette par la queue de l’eau sous\\npression capable de percer un mur "
"en béton.\\nIl aime les endroits où l’eau est pure."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1815
msgid "MUNNA"
msgstr "MUNNA"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Mangerêve
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1818
msgid "Dream Eater"
msgstr "Dévorêve"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1821
msgid ""
"This Pokémon appears before people\\nand Pokémon who are having "
"nightmares\\nand eats those dreams. Munna always\\nfloat in the air. "
msgstr ""
"Il apparaît devant les gens et les Pokémon\\nqui font des cauchemars pour "
"manger leurs\\nrêves. Munna flotte toujours dans les airs."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1890
msgid "MUSHARNA"
msgstr "MUSHANA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1893
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_7_families.h:4750
msgid "Drowsing"
msgstr "Rêveur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1896
msgid ""
"The mist emanating from their foreheads\\nis packed with the dreams of "
"people and\\nPokémon. It changes into different colors\\ndepending on the "
"dream that was eaten."
msgstr ""
"La brume de son front est pleine des rêves\\ndes gens et des Pokémon. Sa "
"couleur change\\nselon le rêve qu’il a mangé."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1962
msgid "PIDOVE"
msgstr "POICHIGEON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1965
msgid "Tiny Pigeon"
msgstr "Tipigeon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:1968
msgid ""
"This very forgetful Pokémon will wait for\\na new order from its Trainer "
"even though\\nit already has one. Flocks often gather\\nin parks and plazas."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon très étourdi attend un ordre de\\nson Dresseur même s’il en a "
"déjà reçu un. On\\nen voit souvent en groupe dans les parcs."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2032
msgid "TRANQUILL"
msgstr "COLOMBEAU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2035
msgid "Wild Pigeon"
msgstr "Sauvapigeon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2038
msgid ""
"No matter where in the world it goes,\\nit knows where its nest is, so it "
"can\\nalways return to its Trainer's location\\nregardless of the distance."
msgstr ""
"Où qu’il aille dans le monde, il sait où est\\nson nid et peut toujours "
"retrouver son\\nDresseur, quelle que soit la distance."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2106
msgid "UNFEZANT"
msgstr "DEFLAISAN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2109
msgid "Proud"
msgstr "Fier"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2112
msgid ""
"Males have plumage on their heads.\\nThe females' flying abilities "
"surpass\\nthose of the males. They will only let\\nthemselves feel close to "
"their Trainers."
msgstr ""
"Le mâle porte une parure sur la tête. La\\nfemelle vole mieux que lui. Ils "
"ne\\ns’attachent qu’à leur Dresseur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2194
msgid "BLITZLE"
msgstr "ZEBIBRON"

#. source : patch FR actuel (correspondance douteuse, à vérifier)
#. source : patch FR actuel (récupéré par pointeur)
#: src/battle_debug.c:371 src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2197
msgid "Electrified"
msgstr "Électrifié"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2200
msgid ""
"Its mane shines when it discharges\\nelectricity. They use the frequency "
"and\\nrhythm of these flashes to communicate\\nwith one another."
msgstr ""
"Sa crinière brille quand il produit de\\nl’électricité. Il communique grâce "
"à la\\nfréquence et au rythme de ces éclairs."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2266
msgid "ZEBSTRIKA"
msgstr "ZEBLITZ"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2272
msgid ""
"When Zebstrika run at full speed, the\\nsound of thunder reverberates. It "
"is\\ndangerous when it's angry as it shoots\\nlightning from its mane in all"
" directions."
msgstr ""
"Quand Zéblitz court à toute allure, on\\nentend gronder le tonnerre. En "
"colère, il\\nlance des éclairs de sa crinière dans tous\\nles sens."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2341
msgid "ROGGENROLA"
msgstr "NODULITHE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2344
msgid "Mantle"
msgstr "Manteau"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2347
msgid ""
"The hexagonal cavity is its ear.\\nIt walks in the direction of sounds "
"it\\nhears, but if the sounds cease, it panics\\nand topples over."
msgstr ""
"La cavité hexagonale qu’il arbore est son\\noreille. Il fonce vers tout ce "
"qu’il entend,\\nmais chute dès que le son s’arrête."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2417
msgid "BOLDORE"
msgstr "GEOLITHE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2420
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_9_families.h:4589
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_9_families.h:4655
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_9_families.h:4726
msgid "Ore"
msgstr "Minerai"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2423
msgid ""
"Its orange crystal is a mass of energy.\\nJust one crystal fragment would "
"provide\\nenough fuel for a hundred dump trucks.\\nWhen it is healthy, its "
"core sticks out."
msgstr ""
"Son cristal orange est une masse d’énergie.\\nUn seul fragment suffirait à "
"alimenter\\ncent camions. En forme, son noyau dépasse."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2502
msgid "GIGALITH"
msgstr "GIGALITHE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2505
msgid "Compressed"
msgstr "Surpression"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2508
msgid ""
"The blasts of energy it makes from\\nsunbeams have terrifying "
"power.\\nHowever, it's not able to fire its blasts\\nat night or on rainy "
"days."
msgstr ""
"Il absorbe le soleil pour tirer des boules\\nd’énergie terriblement "
"destructrices. Une\\narme inutilisable la nuit ou s’il pleut."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2571
msgid "WOOBAT"
msgstr "CHOVSOURIR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2577
msgid ""
"Its habitat is dark forests and caves.\\nSuction from its nostrils enables "
"it\\nto stick to cave walls during sleep.\\nIt leaves a heart-shaped mark "
"behind."
msgstr ""
"Il vit dans les forêts sombres et les\\ngrottes. Son nez-ventouse le colle "
"aux\\nparois pour dormir. Il y laisse une marque\\nen forme de cœur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2657
msgid "SWOOBAT"
msgstr "RHINOLOVE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2660
msgid "Courting"
msgstr "Cupidon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2663
msgid ""
"Anyone who comes into contact with\\nthe ultrasonic waves emitted by "
"a\\ncourting male experiences a positive\\nmood shift."
msgstr ""
"Le mâle courtise la femelle à l’aide\\nd’ultrasons. Les écouter met de très "
"bonne\\nhumeur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2731
msgid "DRILBUR"
msgstr "ROTOTAUPE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2737
msgid ""
"It can dig through the ground at a\\nspeed of 30 mph by spinning its "
"body.\\nIt could give a car running aboveground\\na good race."
msgstr ""
"Il creuse le sol à 50 km/h en tournoyant. Il\\npourrait faire la course avec"
" une voiture\\nroulant en surface."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2803
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2875
msgid "EXCADRILL"
msgstr "MINOTAUPE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2806
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2882
msgid "Subterrene"
msgstr "Souterrain"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2809
msgid ""
"More than 300 feet below the surface,\\nthey build mazelike nests. Their "
"activity\\ncan be destructive to subway tunnels,\\nbut it can also help with"
" construction."
msgstr ""
"Il creuse des nids labyrinthiques à cent\\nmètres sous terre. Il peut abîmer"
" les\\ntunnels de métro, mais aussi aider à les\\nconstruire."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2885
msgid ""
"If this Pokémon brings its arms and\\nhead together to form a "
"streamlined\\nshape and spins at high speeds,\\nit can destroy anything."
msgstr ""
"Quand ce Pokémon joint ses bras et sa\\ntête pour former une "
"silhouette\\nprofilée et tourne à grande vitesse,\\nil peut tout détruire."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2938
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3011
msgid "AUDINO"
msgstr "NANMEOUIE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2941
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3018
msgid "Hearing"
msgstr "Audition"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:2944
msgid ""
"Its auditory sense is astounding.\\nUsing the feelers on its ears, it can "
"tell\\nhow someone is feeling or when an egg\\nmight hatch."
msgstr ""
"Son ouïe est extraordinaire. Ses antennes\\nlui permettent de deviner "
"l’humeur des gens\\nou le moment où un Œuf va éclore."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3021
msgid ""
"Mega Audino emits a soothing pulse from\\nits body that reduces hostility in"
" others.\\nAnything that comes into contact with its\\nsecond feelers will "
"fall into a deep sleep."
msgstr ""
"MEGA-NANMEOUIE émet de son corps une\\nonde apaisante qui calme "
"l’hostilité.\\nQuiconque touche ses seconds palpeurs\\nsombre dans un "
"profond sommeil."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3088
msgid "TIMBURR"
msgstr "CHARPENTI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3091
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3160
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3234
msgid "Muscular"
msgstr "Costaud"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3094
msgid ""
"These Pokémon appear at building\\nsites and help out with "
"construction.\\nThey always carry squared logs.\\nAs they grow, they carry "
"bigger logs."
msgstr ""
"Il apparaît sur les chantiers pour aider à\\nla construction. Il porte "
"toujours une\\npoutre, de plus en plus grosse à mesure\\nqu’il grandit."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3157
msgid "GURDURR"
msgstr "OUVRIFIER"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3163
msgid ""
"They strengthen their bodies by carrying\\nsteel beams. This Pokémon is so "
"muscular\\nand strongly built that even a group of\\nwrestlers could not "
"make it budge an inch."
msgstr ""
"Il se muscle en portant des poutres\\nd’acier. Il est si costaud que même "
"une\\nbande de catcheurs ne parvient pas à le\\nfaire bouger."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3231
msgid "CONKELDURR"
msgstr "BETOCHEF"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3237
msgid ""
"They use concrete pillars as walking\\ncanes. Rather than rely solely on "
"force,\\nthey master moves that utilize the\\ncentrifugal force of spinning "
"concrete."
msgstr ""
"Il se sert de piliers de béton comme\\ncannes. Au lieu de la force brute, "
"il\\nmaîtrise des techniques utilisant leur\\nforce centrifuge."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3299
msgid "TYMPOLE"
msgstr "TRITONDE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3305
msgid ""
"By vibrating its cheeks, it emits sound\\nwaves imperceptible to humans. It "
"uses\\nthe rhythm of these sounds to talk and\\nwarns others of danger."
msgstr ""
"Il fait vibrer ses joues pour émettre des\\nsons inaudibles pour les "
"humains. Il s’en\\nsert pour parler et prévenir du danger."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3367
msgid "PALPITOAD"
msgstr "BATRACNE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3373
msgid ""
"It lives in the water and on land.\\nWhen they vibrate the bumps on "
"their\\nheads, they can make waves in water\\nor earthquake-like vibrations "
"on land."
msgstr ""
"Il vit dans l’eau et sur terre. En faisant\\nvibrer ses bosses, il crée des "
"vagues dans\\nl’eau et des secousses sur terre."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3443
msgid "SEISMITOAD"
msgstr "CRAPUSTULE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3449
msgid ""
"It increases the power of its punches\\nby vibrating the bumps on its "
"fists.\\nThey can also shoot paralyzing liquid\\nfrom their head bumps."
msgstr ""
"Il fait vibrer les bosses de ses poings\\npour frapper plus fort. Celles de "
"sa tête\\nprojettent un liquide paralysant."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3517
msgid "THROH"
msgstr "JUDOKRAK"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3520
msgid "Judo"
msgstr "Judo"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3523
msgid ""
"When it tightens its belt, it becomes\\nstronger. Wild Throh use vines to "
"weave\\ntheir own belts. It changes belts as it\\ngets more powerful."
msgstr ""
"Il devient plus fort en serrant sa\\nceinture, tressée de lianes. Il en "
"change à\\nmesure qu’il gagne en puissance."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3589
msgid "SAWK"
msgstr "KARACLEE"

#. source : patch FR actuel (récupéré par pointeur)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3592
msgid "Karate"
msgstr "Karaté"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3595
msgid ""
"The sound of Sawk punching boulders\\nand trees can be heard all the way "
"from\\nthe mountains where they train.\\nDisturbing their training angers "
"them."
msgstr ""
"On entend jusqu’au pied des montagnes\\nKaraclée frapper rochers et arbres. "
"Gare à\\nqui dérange son entraînement!"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3658
msgid "SEWADDLE"
msgstr "LARVEYETTE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3661
msgid "Sewing"
msgstr "Couture"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3664
msgid ""
"It chews up leaves and sews them with\\nsticky thread extruded from its "
"mouth.\\nSince this Pokémon makes its own clothes,\\nit is a mascot for "
"fashion designers."
msgstr ""
"Il mâche des feuilles et les coud avec le\\nfil gluant de sa bouche. Il fait"
" ses propres\\nhabits: c’est la mascotte des stylistes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3730
msgid "SWADLOON"
msgstr "COUVERDURE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3733
msgid "Leaf-Wrapped"
msgstr "Capefeuille"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3736
msgid ""
"Forests where Swadloon live have\\nsuperb foliage because the "
"nutrients\\nthey make from fallen leaves nourish\\nthe plant life."
msgstr ""
"Dans les forêts où il vit, la végétation\\npousse bien car il transforme les"
" feuilles\\nmortes en engrais."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3806
msgid "LEAVANNY"
msgstr "MANTERNEL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3809
msgid "Nurturing"
msgstr "Précepteur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3812
msgid ""
"It keeps its eggs warm with heat from\\nfermenting leaves. It also uses "
"leaves to\\nweave warm wrappings for Sewaddle by\\nusing the silk secreted "
"from its mouth."
msgstr ""
"Il couve ses œufs à la chaleur de feuilles\\nqui fermentent. Il tisse aussi "
"des langes\\nde feuilles pour les Larveyette avec sa\\nsoie."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3880
msgid "VENIPEDE"
msgstr "VENIPATTE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3883
msgid "Centipede"
msgstr "Chilopode"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3886
msgid ""
"Using the feelers on its head and tail,\\nit picks up vibrations in the air "
"to\\ndetermine its prey's location and state.\\nIt is brutally aggressive."
msgstr ""
"Ses antennes captent les vibrations de\\nl’air pour repérer ses proies et "
"leur état.\\nIl est d’une agressivité redoutable."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3958
msgid "WHIRLIPEDE"
msgstr "SCOBOLIDE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3961
msgid "Curlipede"
msgstr "Coconplopode"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:3964
msgid ""
"Storing energy for evolution, it sits.\\nBut when attacked, it spins its "
"body at\\nhigh speed like a wheel and then\\ncrashes furiously into its "
"opponent."
msgstr ""
"Immobile, il accumule de l’énergie pour\\névoluer. Attaqué, il tourne sur "
"lui-même\\ncomme une roue et fonce sur l’ennemi."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4040
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4110
msgid "SCOLIPEDE"
msgstr "BRUTAPODE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4043
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4117
msgid "Megapede"
msgstr "Mégaplopode"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4046
msgid ""
"With quick movements, it chases down\\nits foes, attacking relentlessly with"
" its\\nhorns until it prevails. Then it finishes\\nthem off with deadly "
"poison."
msgstr ""
"Il traque ses ennemis à toute vitesse et\\nles frappe sans relâche de ses "
"cornes, puis\\nles achève avec un poison mortel."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4120
msgid ""
"Its deadly venom gives off a faint\\nglow. The venom affects "
"Scolipede's\\nmind, honing its viciousness."
msgstr ""
"Son venin mortel émet une faible\\nlueur. Il agit sur l’esprit "
"de\\nBRUTAPODE et aiguise sa férocité."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4173
msgid "COTTONEE"
msgstr "DOUDOUVET"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4176
msgid "Cotton Puff"
msgstr "Boule Coton"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4179
msgid ""
"When it finds others of its kind, they all\\nstick together. When enough of "
"them\\nhave collected, the mass resembles a\\ncumulonimbus cloud."
msgstr ""
"Les Doudouvet se collent entre eux quand\\nils se rencontrent. Assez "
"nombreux, ils\\nforment de véritables cumulonimbus\\nvivants."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4249
msgid "WHIMSICOTT"
msgstr "FARFADUVET"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4252
msgid "Windveiled"
msgstr "Vole Vent"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4255
msgid ""
"It rides on the wind and slips into\\npeople's homes. After it has turned "
"a\\nroom into a cotton-filled mess, it giggles\\nto itself and takes off."
msgstr ""
"Il s’introduit chez les gens à la faveur\\nd’un courant d’air, répand du "
"coton partout\\ndans la pièce puis repart en riant."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4319
msgid "PETILIL"
msgstr "CHLOROBULE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4322
msgid "Bulb"
msgstr "Racine"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4325
msgid ""
"By pruning the leaves on its head with\\nregularity, this Pokémon can be "
"grown\\ninto a fine plump shape. These bitter\\nleaves refresh those who eat"
" them."
msgstr ""
"En taillant régulièrement les feuilles de sa\\ntête, on lui donne une jolie "
"forme ronde.\\nCes feuilles amères sont revigorantes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4397
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4472
msgid "LILLIGANT"
msgstr "FRAGILADY"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4400
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_8_families.h:1591
msgid "Flowering"
msgstr "Chef-Fleur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4403
msgid ""
"Even veteran Trainers face a challenge\\nin getting its beautiful flower to "
"bloom.\\nIt withers away if a trainer does not\\ntake good care of it."
msgstr ""
"Même les Dresseurs chevronnés peinent à\\nfaire éclore sa belle fleur. Il se"
" fane si on\\nne prend pas bien soin de lui."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4470
msgid "LILLIGANT-H"
msgstr "FRAGILADY-H"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4480
msgid "Spinning"
msgstr "Tournoyant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4483
msgid ""
"Its well-developed legs are the result of\\na life spent on mountains "
"covered in deep\\nsnow. The scent it exudes from its flower\\ncrown heartens"
" those in proximity."
msgstr ""
"Ses jambes puissantes sont le fruit d’une\\nvie passée dans des montagnes "
"enneigées.\\nLe parfum de sa couronne de fleurs ravive\\nle cœur de ceux qui"
" l’entourent."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4551
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4619
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4688
msgid "BASCULIN"
msgstr "BARGANTUA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4554
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4622
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12456
msgid "Hostile"
msgstr "Violent"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4557
msgid ""
"It used to be a common food source. The\\nmeat of red Basculin is on the "
"fatty side\\nand it's more popular with the youth.\\nIts temperament is "
"vicious and aggressive."
msgstr ""
"Il était autrefois très consommé. La chair\\ndu Bargantua rouge est grasse "
"et plaît aux\\njeunes. Il est d’un naturel violent."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4625
msgid ""
"They form schools with others of the same\\ncolor. The greatest foe of a "
"school of blue\\nBasculin is a school of red Basculin.\\nIts flavor is light"
" and inoffensive."
msgstr ""
"Ils forment des bancs de même\\ncouleur. Le pire ennemi d’un banc\\nde "
"Bargantua bleus est un banc de\\nrouges. Sa chair a un goût léger."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4691
msgid "Mellow"
msgstr "Violent"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4694
msgid ""
"While this ancient form of Basculin shares\\na vast array of qualities with "
"other forms,\\nit differs in several respects, including\\ndemeanor, being "
"much gentler than others."
msgstr ""
"Cette forme ancienne de Bargantua\\npartage bien des traits avec "
"les\\nautres, mais s’en distingue par un\\ntempérament bien plus doux."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4757
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4822
msgid "BASCULEGION"
msgstr "PARAGRUEL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4760
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4825
msgid "Big Fish"
msgstr "Poissigrand"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4763
msgid ""
"Clads itself in the souls of comrades that\\nperished before fulfilling "
"their goals of\\njourneying upstream. No other species in\\nall Hisui's "
"rivers is Basculegion's equal."
msgstr ""
"Il se revêt des âmes de ses camarades\\nmorts avant d’avoir pu remonter le "
"courant.\\nDans les rivières de Hisui, nul n’égale\\nParagruel."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4828
msgid ""
"The souls of its comrades cloak its\\nbody and propel it "
"effortlessly\\nthrough even raging rapids."
msgstr ""
"Les âmes de ses camarades\\nenveloppent son corps et le propulsent\\nmême "
"dans les rapides déchaînés."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4890
msgid "SANDILE"
msgstr "MASCAIMAN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4893
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4963
msgid "Desert Croc"
msgstr "Croco Sable"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4896
msgid ""
"It conceals itself in the sand and\\nchomps down on the legs of any "
"prey\\nthat unwarily walk over it. Its favorite\\nfood is Trapinch."
msgstr ""
"Tapi dans le sable, il attend qu’une proie\\npasse pour lui croquer la "
"patte. Il a un\\ngros faible pour les Kraknoix."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4960
msgid "KROKOROK"
msgstr "ESCROCO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:4966
msgid ""
"They move in groups of a few individuals.\\nThanks to the special membrane "
"covering\\nits eyes, it can see its surroundings\\nclearly, even in the dead"
" of night."
msgstr ""
"Il vit en petits groupes. Une membrane\\nspéciale protège ses yeux et lui "
"permet de\\nvoir clair même en pleine nuit."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5034
msgid "KROOKODILE"
msgstr "CROCORIBLE"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5037
msgid "Intimidate"
msgstr "Intimidation"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5040
msgid ""
"Very violent Pokémon, they never allow\\ntheir prey to escape. Their jaws "
"are so\\npowerful, they can crush the body of\\nan automobile."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon très violent ne laisse jamais sa\\nproie s’échapper. Ses "
"mâchoires peuvent\\nbroyer la carrosserie d’une voiture."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5105
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5308
msgid "DARUMAKA"
msgstr "DARUMAROND"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5108
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5316
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5396
msgid "Zen Charm"
msgstr "Daruma"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5111
msgid ""
"When its internal fire is burning, it\\ncannot calm down and it runs "
"around.\\nWhen the fire diminishes, it pulls its\\nlimbs into its body and "
"falls asleep."
msgstr ""
"Quand son feu intérieur brûle, il ne tient\\npas en place et court partout. "
"Quand il\\nfaiblit, il rentre ses membres et s’endort."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5175
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5245
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5388
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5468
msgid "DARMANITAN"
msgstr "DARUMACHO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5178
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5248
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5476
msgid "Blazing"
msgstr "Enflammé"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5181
msgid ""
"When one is injured in a fierce battle,\\nit transforms into a stone "
"statue.\\nThen it meditates and sharpens its\\nmind and fights on mentally."
msgstr ""
"Gravement blessé au combat, il se change\\nen statue de pierre. Il médite "
"alors pour\\naffûter son esprit et poursuivre la lutte."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5251
msgid ""
"When wounded, it stops moving. It\\ngoes as still as stone to "
"meditate,\\nsharpening its mind and spirit."
msgstr ""
"Blessé, il cesse de bouger et reste\\nimmobile comme une pierre "
"pour\\nméditer et aiguiser son esprit."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5306
msgid "DARUMAKA-G"
msgstr "DARUMAROND-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5319
msgid ""
"The colder they get, the more\\nenergetic they are. They freeze "
"their\\nbreath to make snowballs, using them\\nas ammo for playful snowball "
"fights."
msgstr ""
"Plus il fait froid, plus il est en forme. Il\\ngèle son souffle pour faire "
"des boules de\\nneige, qu’il utilise dans de joyeuses\\nbatailles."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5386
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5466
msgid "DARMANITAN-G"
msgstr "DARUMACHO-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5399
msgid ""
"On days when blizzards blow\\nthrough, it comes down to where people\\nlive."
" It stashes food in the snowball on\\nits head, taking it home for later."
msgstr ""
"Les jours de blizzard, il descend près des\\nvillages. Il cache de la "
"nourriture dans la\\nboule de neige sur sa tête pour la\\nrapporter chez "
"lui."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5479
msgid ""
"Darmanitan takes this form when\\nenraged. It won't stop spewing "
"flames\\nuntil its rage has settled, even if\\nits body starts to melt."
msgstr ""
"Darumacho prend cette forme quand il\\nenrage. Il crache des flammes "
"tant\\nque sa colère n’est pas retombée,\\nmême si son corps se met à "
"fondre."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5540
msgid "MARACTUS"
msgstr "MARACACHI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5546
msgid ""
"Arid regions are their habitat.\\nWhen it moves rhythmically, it makes "
"a\\nsound similar to maracas, making the\\nsurprised Pokémon flee."
msgstr ""
"Il vit dans les régions arides. En se\\ndéhanchant, il produit un son de "
"maracas\\nqui fait fuir les Pokémon surpris."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5615
msgid "DWEBBLE"
msgstr "CRABICOQUE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5618
msgid "Rock Inn"
msgstr "Lithicole"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5621
msgid ""
"It makes a hole in a stone of a suitable\\nsize. If that rock breaks, the "
"Pokémon\\nremains agitated until it locates\\na replacement."
msgstr ""
"Il creuse un trou dans une pierre à sa\\ntaille. Si elle se brise, il reste "
"agité\\njusqu’à ce qu’il en trouve une autre."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5691
msgid "CRUSTLE"
msgstr "CRABARAQUE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5694
msgid "Stone Home"
msgstr "Lapidicole"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5697
msgid ""
"Competing for territory, Crustle fight\\nviciously. The one whose boulder "
"is\\nbroken is the loser of the battle and\\nbegins to weaken."
msgstr ""
"Ils se battent férocement pour leur\\nterritoire. Celui dont le rocher se "
"brise a\\nperdu et commence à dépérir."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5764
msgid "SCRAGGY"
msgstr "BAGGIGUANE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5767
msgid "Shedding"
msgstr "Mue"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5770
msgid ""
"Its skin has a rubbery elasticity, so it\\ncan reduce damage by "
"defensively\\npulling its skin up to its neck.\\nIts skull is massively "
"thick."
msgstr ""
"Sa peau élastique lui permet d’amortir les\\ncoups en la remontant jusqu’au "
"cou. Son\\ncrâne est extrêmement épais."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5835
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5907
msgid "SCRAFTY"
msgstr "BAGGAID"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5838
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5914
msgid "Hoodlum"
msgstr "Gang"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5841
msgid ""
"Groups of them beat up anything that\\nenters their territory. The one with "
"the\\nbiggest crest is the group leader, and\\nis the most respected."
msgstr ""
"Ils rossent en groupe tout ce qui entre sur\\nleur territoire. Celui qui a "
"la plus grande\\ncrête est le chef, et le plus respecté."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5917
msgid ""
"Mega Evolution has caused Scrafty's\\nshed skin to turn white, "
"growing\\ntough and supple. Of course, this\\nPokémon is still as feisty as "
"ever."
msgstr ""
"La Méga-Évolution a rendu la mue de\\nBAGGAID blanche, résistante "
"et\\lsouple. Bien sûr, ce Pokémon est\\ltoujours aussi bagarreur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5968
msgid "SIGILYPH"
msgstr "CRYPTERO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5971
msgid "Avianoid"
msgstr "Similoiseau"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:5974
msgid ""
"The guardians of an ancient city, they\\nalways fly the same route while "
"keeping\\nwatch for invaders. They use their\\npsychic power to attack "
"enemies."
msgstr ""
"Gardiens d’une cité antique, ils survolent\\ntoujours le même trajet pour "
"guetter les\\nintrus et attaquent par la force\\npsychique."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6045
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6191
msgid "YAMASK"
msgstr "TUTAFEH"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : aire
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6048
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6199
msgid "Spirit"
msgstr "ESPRIT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6051
msgid ""
"These Pokémon arose from the spirits\\nof people interred in graves in past "
"ages.\\nEach of them carries a mask that used\\nto be its face when it was "
"human."
msgstr ""
"Ces Pokémon sont nés des âmes de gens\\nenterrés jadis. Ils portent tous un "
"masque,\\nqui était leur visage quand ils étaient\\nhumains."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6119
msgid "COFAGRIGUS"
msgstr "TUTANKAFER"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6122
msgid "Coffin"
msgstr "Cercueil"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6125
msgid ""
"Grave robbers who mistake them for\\nreal coffins and get too close end "
"up\\ntrapped inside their bodies. Their bodies\\nare covered in pure gold."
msgstr ""
"Les pilleurs de tombes qui le prennent pour\\nun vrai sarcophage finissent "
"piégés dans\\nson corps, recouvert d’or pur."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6189
msgid "YAMASK-G"
msgstr "TUTAFEH-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6202
msgid ""
"A clay slab with cursed engravings\\ntook possession of a Yamask. The\\nslab"
" is said to be absorbing the\\nYamask's dark power."
msgstr ""
"Une tablette d’argile gravée de\\nmalédictions s’est emparée d’un "
"Tutafeh.\\nElle absorberait son énergie maléfique."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6271
msgid "RUNERIGUS"
msgstr "TUTETEKRI"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#: src/battle_debug.c:386 src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6274
msgid "Grudge"
msgstr "Rancune"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6277
msgid ""
"A powerful curse was woven into an ancient\\npainting. After absorbing the "
"spirit of\\na Yamask, the painting began to move."
msgstr ""
"Ces motifs antiques gravés d’une\\npuissante malédiction ont aspiré l’âme "
"de\\nTutafeh avant de prendre vie."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6337
msgid "TIRTOUGA"
msgstr "CARAPAGOS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6340
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6410
msgid "Prototurtle"
msgstr "Tortantique"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6343
msgid ""
"Reputed to be the ancestor of most\\nturtle Pokémon, it lived in warm "
"seas\\nabout a hundred million years ago.\\nIt was restored from a fossil."
msgstr ""
"Ancêtre de la plupart des Pokémon tortues,\\nil vivait dans les mers chaudes"
" il y a 100\\nmillions d’années. Il a été ressuscité d’un\\nfossile."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6407
msgid "CARRACOSTA"
msgstr "MEGAPAGOS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6413
msgid ""
"They can live both in the ocean and\\non land. Incredible jaw strength "
"enables\\nthem to chew up steel beams and rocks\\nalong with their prey."
msgstr ""
"Il vit dans la mer comme sur terre. Ses\\nmâchoires surpuissantes broient "
"poutres\\nd’acier et rochers avec ses proies."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6483
msgid "ARCHEN"
msgstr "ARKEAPTI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6486
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6556
msgid "First Bird"
msgstr "Oisancien"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6489
msgid ""
"Said to be the ancestor of all bird\\nPokémon, Archen itself could not "
"actually\\nfly but moved by hopping from treetop\\nto treetop."
msgstr ""
"On dit qu’il est l’ancêtre des oiseaux.\\nIncapable de voler, il se "
"déplaçait en\\nsautant de cime en cime."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6553
msgid "ARCHEOPS"
msgstr "AEROPTERYX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6559
msgid ""
"They are intelligent and will cooperate\\nto catch prey. When one "
"Archeops\\nhad the prey cornered, another would\\nswoop on it."
msgstr ""
"Ils sont intelligents et chassent en\\néquipe. Quand un Aéroptéryx acculait "
"une\\nproie, un autre fondait sur elle."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6629
msgid "TRUBBISH"
msgstr "MIAMIASME"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6632
msgid "Trash Bag"
msgstr "Sac Poubelle"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6635
msgid ""
"It gorges on trash until its stomach\\nis full. Then it belches toxic "
"gas.\\nAn unlucky whiff of this gas will put\\na person in the hospital."
msgstr ""
"Il se gave d’ordures jusqu’à plus faim, puis\\nrote un gaz toxique. Une "
"bouffée suffit à\\nenvoyer quelqu’un à l’hôpital."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6701
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6774
msgid "GARBODOR"
msgstr "MIASMAX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6704
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6777
msgid "Trash Heap"
msgstr "Dépotoir"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6707
msgid ""
"Beware the poisonous liquid it shoots\\nfrom its right arm. If even a little"
" of it\\ngets on you, you'll experience the full\\neffects of this "
"unidentified toxin."
msgstr ""
"Gare au liquide toxique qu’il projette par\\nson bras droit! Une seule "
"goutte suffit à\\nsubir tous les effets de ce poison inconnu."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6780
msgid ""
"It sprays toxic gas from its mouth\\nand fingers. If the gas engulfs "
"you,\\nthe toxins will seep in all the way\\ndown to your bones."
msgstr ""
"Il crache un gaz toxique par la\\nbouche et les doigts. Si ce gaz "
"vous\\nenveloppe, les toxines s’infiltrent\\njusqu’aux os."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6835
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6981
msgid "ZORUA"
msgstr "ZORUA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6838
msgid "Tricky Fox"
msgstr "Sombrenard"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6841
msgid ""
"To protect themselves from danger, they\\nhide their true identities by "
"transforming\\ninto people and Pokémon. Apparently, it\\noften transforms "
"into a silent child."
msgstr ""
"Pour se protéger, ils cachent leur identité\\nen prenant l’apparence de gens"
" ou de\\nPokémon. Il se change souvent en enfant\\nsilencieux."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6907
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7062
msgid "ZOROARK"
msgstr "ZOROARK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6910
msgid "Illusion Fox"
msgstr "Polymorfox"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6913
msgid ""
"Bonds between these Pokémon are very\\nstrong. It protects the safety of "
"its\\npack by tricking its opponents. They\\ndefend their lair with illusory"
" scenery."
msgstr ""
"Très solidaires, ils protègent la meute en\\ndupant leurs ennemis. Ils "
"défendent leur\\ntanière avec des paysages illusoires."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6979
msgid "ZORUA-H"
msgstr "ZORUA-H"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6989
msgid "Spiteful Fox"
msgstr "Renard Rogue"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:6992
msgid ""
"Derives power from resentment,\\nwhich rises as energy atop its head "
"and\\ntakes on the forms of foes. In this\\nway, Zorua vents lingering "
"malice."
msgstr ""
"Il puise sa force dans la rancune, qui\\ns’élève au-dessus de sa tête et "
"prend la\\nforme de ses ennemis. Ainsi, Zorua exprime\\nsa malveillance "
"tenace."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7060
msgid "ZOROARK-H"
msgstr "ZOROARK-H"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7070
msgid "Baneful Fox"
msgstr "Renard Fatal"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7073
msgid ""
"Heedless of its own safety,\\nZoroark attacks its nemeses with a "
"bitter\\nenergy so intense, it lacerates\\nZoroark's own body."
msgstr ""
"Insouciant du danger, Zoroark attaque ses\\nennemis avec une rancœur si "
"intense\\nqu’elle lacère son propre corps."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7140
msgid "MINCCINO"
msgstr "CHINCHIDOU"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7143
msgid "Chinchilla"
msgstr "Chinchilla"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7146
msgid ""
"These Pokémon prefer a tidy habitat.\\nThey greet one another by rubbing "
"each\\nother with their tails, which are always\\nkept well groomed and "
"clean."
msgstr ""
"Ces Pokémon aiment la propreté. Ils se\\nsaluent en se frottant avec leur "
"queue,\\ntoujours bien entretenue."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7209
msgid "CINCCINO"
msgstr "PASHMILLA"

#. nom propre/fragment conservé (le patch FR actuel donnait un morceau d’un
#. autre texte)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7212
msgid "Scarf"
msgstr "Scarf"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7215
msgid ""
"Their white fur feels amazing to touch.\\nCinccino's body is coated in a "
"special\\noil that repels dust and helps it deflect\\nattacks, such as "
"punches."
msgstr ""
"Son pelage blanc est merveilleusement\\ndoux. Une huile spéciale le protège "
"de la\\npoussière et fait glisser les coups de\\npoing."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7284
msgid "GOTHITA"
msgstr "SCRUTELLA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7287
msgid "Fixation"
msgstr "Dévisageur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7290
msgid ""
"They intently observe both Trainers and\\nPokémon. Apparently, Gothita are "
"looking\\nat something that only they can see. Their\\nribbonlike feelers "
"increase their power."
msgstr ""
"Ils observent intensément Dresseurs et\\nPokémon. On dirait qu’ils voient "
"des choses\\ninvisibles aux autres. Leurs rubans\\ndécuplent leur force."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7358
msgid "GOTHORITA"
msgstr "MESMERELLA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7364
msgid ""
"Starlight is the source of their power.\\nThey use hypnosis to control "
"people and\\nPokémon. Tales of Gothorita leading them\\nastray are told in "
"every corner."
msgstr ""
"La lumière des étoiles leur donne leur\\nforce. Ils hypnotisent humains et "
"Pokémon.\\nPartout, on raconte qu’ils égarent les\\ngens."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7432
msgid "GOTHITELLE"
msgstr "SIDERELLA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7435
msgid "Astral Body"
msgstr "Cosmique"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7438
msgid ""
"Starry skies thousands of light-years\\naway are visible in the space "
"distorted by\\ntheir intense psychic power. When it learns\\nits Trainer's "
"life span, it cries in sadness."
msgstr ""
"Sa puissance psychique distord l’espace et\\nrévèle des cieux à des années-"
"lumière. Il\\npleure en apprenant l’espérance de vie de\\nson Dresseur."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7503
msgid "SOLOSIS"
msgstr "NUCLEOS"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Cellule
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7506
msgid "Cell"
msgstr "Cell"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7509
msgid ""
"Because their bodies are enveloped\\nin a special liquid, they are fine in "
"any\\nenvironment, no matter how severe. They\\ncan use telepathy to talk "
"with others."
msgstr ""
"Enveloppés d’un liquide spécial, ils\\nsupportent les milieux les plus "
"hostiles.\\nIls communiquent par télépathie."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7574
msgid "DUOSION"
msgstr "MEIOS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7577
msgid "Mitosis"
msgstr "Divisé"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7580
msgid ""
"When their brains, now divided in two,\\nare thinking the same "
"thoughts,\\nthese Pokémon exhibit their maximized\\npsychic power."
msgstr ""
"Quand ses deux moitiés de cerveau ont la\\nmême pensée, ce Pokémon déploie "
"toute sa\\npuissance psychique."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7644
msgid "REUNICLUS"
msgstr "SYMBIOS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7647
msgid "Multiplying"
msgstr "Multiplié"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7650
msgid ""
"They use psychic power to control their\\narms, which are made of a special "
"liquid.\\nWhen Reuniclus shake hands, a network\\nforms between their "
"brains."
msgstr ""
"Ils contrôlent par psychokinèse leurs bras\\nfaits d’un liquide spécial. "
"Quand deux\\nSymbios se serrent la main, leurs cerveaux\\nse relient."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7716
msgid "DUCKLETT"
msgstr "COUANETON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7722
msgid ""
"These bird Pokémon are excellent divers.\\nThey are better at swimming than "
"flying,\\nand they happily eat their favorite food,\\npeat moss, as they "
"dive underwater."
msgstr ""
"Ces Pokémon oiseaux plongent à merveille.\\nIls nagent mieux qu’ils ne "
"volent et\\ndégustent sous l’eau leur mets favori: la\\ntourbe."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7790
msgid "SWANNA"
msgstr "LAKMECYGNE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7793
msgid "White Bird"
msgstr "Cygne"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7796
msgid ""
"Despite their elegant appearance, they\\ncan flap their wings strongly and "
"fly for\\nthousands of miles. The one in the middle\\nis the leader of the "
"flock."
msgstr ""
"Malgré leur air élégant, leurs puissantes\\nailes leur font parcourir des "
"milliers de\\nkilomètres. Celui du milieu guide la nuée."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7863
msgid "VANILLITE"
msgstr "SORBEBE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7869
msgid ""
"The temperature of their breath is -58ºF.\\nThey create snow crystals and "
"make snow\\nfall in the areas around them. Vanillite is\\ntreasured by "
"households in warm regions."
msgstr ""
"Son souffle est à -50 degrés et fait\\ntomber la neige autour de lui. Les "
"foyers\\ndes régions chaudes adorent les Sorbébé."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7939
msgid "VANILLISH"
msgstr "SORBOUL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7942
msgid "Icy Snow"
msgstr "Grêle"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:7945
msgid ""
"Vanillish has existed since the Ice Age.\\nIt controls particles of ice, "
"freezes its\\nopponents, and then shatters them with\\na headbutt."
msgstr ""
"Sorboul existe depuis l’ère glaciaire. Il\\ncontrôle des particules de "
"glace, gèle ses\\nennemis, puis les brise d’un coup de tête."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8013
msgid "VANILLUXE"
msgstr "SORBOUBOUL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8016
msgid "Snowstorm"
msgstr "Congère"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8019
msgid ""
"Each of its two heads has a brain, and\\nwhen they are in agreement, it "
"attacks\\nits enemies by exhaling a violent blizzard.\\nIt makes snow clouds"
" inside its body."
msgstr ""
"Chacune de ses deux têtes a un cerveau.\\nQuand elles sont d’accord, il "
"souffle un\\nviolent blizzard. Il crée des nuages de\\nneige en lui."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8082
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8149
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8216
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8283
msgid "DEERLING"
msgstr "VIVALDAIM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8085
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8152
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8219
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8286
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8353
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8418
msgid "Season"
msgstr "Saison"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8088
msgid ""
"Deerling have different scents\\ndepending on the season. In early\\nspring,"
" these Pokémon give off a\\ndelicate, sweet, and calming scent."
msgstr ""
"Leur odeur change selon la saison. Au début\\ndu printemps, ils dégagent un "
"parfum\\ndélicat, sucré et apaisant."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8155
msgid ""
"To prevent Deerling from entering\\ntheir fields, many farmers will "
"have\\nseveral Lycanroc stand guard, as\\nthey are its natural enemy."
msgstr ""
"Pour tenir les Vivaldaim loin de\\nleurs champs, bien des fermiers "
"les\\nfont garder par des Lougaroc, leurs\\nprédateurs naturels."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8222
msgid ""
"Deerling have different scents\\ndepending on the season. In this "
"form,\\nDeerling have a softly sweet scent\\nthat lingers in the nose."
msgstr ""
"L’odeur de Vivaldaim varie selon la\\nsaison. Sous cette forme, il "
"dégage\\nun parfum doux et sucré qui reste\\nlongtemps dans le nez."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8289
msgid ""
"Deerling's scent changes with the\\nseasons, but when the Pokémon is "
"in\\nits Winter Form, it has hardly any\\nscent at all."
msgstr ""
"L’odeur de Vivaldaim change selon\\nla saison, mais sous sa Forme "
"Hiver,\\nil n’en a presque aucune."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8350
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8415
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8480
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8545
msgid "SAWSBUCK"
msgstr "HAYDAIM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8356
msgid ""
"Some people call Sawsbuck the harbingers\\nof spring because the plants "
"growing on\\nits horns change according to the season.\\nThe leader "
"possesses magnificent horns."
msgstr ""
"On les dit messagers du printemps, car les\\nplantes de leurs bois changent "
"au fil des\\nsaisons. Le chef porte des bois\\nmagnifiques."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8421
msgid ""
"The thicker and larger the\\nbranches and leaves on its antlers, the\\nmore "
"majestic the Sawsbuck is thought\\nto be."
msgstr ""
"Plus les branches et feuilles de ses\\nbois sont épaisses et grandes, "
"plus\\nce Haydaim est jugé majestueux."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8486
msgid ""
"Sawsbuck in their Autumn Form are\\nknown for having very short\\ntempers. "
"The males fight each other\\nincessantly."
msgstr ""
"Les Haydaim en Forme Automne sont\\nconnus pour leur caractère\\ncolérique. "
"Les mâles se battent\\nsans cesse."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8551
msgid ""
"Though there are many enthusiasts\\nfor Sawsbuck as a species, "
"this\\nseasonal form in particular is not\\nvery popular."
msgstr ""
"Si Haydaim a de nombreux fans en\\ntant qu’espèce, cette forme\\nsaisonnière"
" n’est guère\\npopulaire."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8613
msgid "EMOLGA"
msgstr "EMOLGA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8616
msgid "Sky Squirrel"
msgstr "Pteromys"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8619
msgid ""
"It glides using its cape-like membrane.\\nIt grills berries and bug Pokémon "
"with\\nelectric shocks from the pouches on its\\ncheeks and makes a meal of "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Il plane grâce à sa membrane en forme de\\ncape. Il grille Baies et Pokémon "
"insectes\\navec l’électricité de ses joues et s’en\\nrégale."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8685
msgid "KARRABLAST"
msgstr "CARABING"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8688
msgid "Clamping"
msgstr "Carabe"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8691
msgid ""
"When they feel threatened, they spit an\\nacidic liquid to drive attackers "
"away.\\nFor some reason they evolve while they\\nare in the same place as "
"Shelmet."
msgstr ""
"Menacé, il crache un liquide acide pour\\nfaire fuir ses ennemis. Pour une "
"raison\\nobscure, il évolue en présence d’un\\nEscargaume."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8754
msgid "ESCAVALIER"
msgstr "LANCARGOT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8757
msgid "Cavalry"
msgstr "Chevalier"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8760
msgid ""
"Wearing the shell covering they stole\\nfrom Shelmet, they defend themselves"
" and\\nattack with two lances. The steel armor\\nprotects their whole body."
msgstr ""
"Revêtus de la coquille volée à un\\nEscargaume, ils se défendent et "
"attaquent\\navec deux lances. Leur armure d’acier les\\nprotège tout "
"entiers."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8825
msgid "FOONGUS"
msgstr "TROMPIGNON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8831
msgid ""
"It lures Pokémon in with its pattern that\\nlooks just like a Poké Ball, "
"then releases\\nits poison spores. Why it resembles a\\nPoké Ball is "
"unknown."
msgstr ""
"Il attire les Pokémon avec son motif de\\nPoké Ball, puis libère ses spores "
"toxiques.\\nOn ignore pourquoi il ressemble à une Poké\\nBall."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8899
msgid "AMOONGUSS"
msgstr "GAULET"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8905
msgid ""
"It lures prey close by dancing and waving\\nits arm caps, which resemble "
"Poké Balls,\\nin a swaying motion, but very few Pokémon\\nare fooled by "
"this."
msgstr ""
"Il attire ses proies en dansant et en\\nagitant ses bras en forme de Poké "
"Ball,\\nmais très peu de Pokémon s’y laissent\\nprendre."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8971
msgid "FRILLISH"
msgstr "VISKUSE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8974
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9063
msgid "Floating"
msgstr "Flottaison"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:8977
msgid ""
"If its veil-like arms stun and wrap an\\nopponent, that foe will be "
"dragged\\nfive miles below the surface to its lair,\\nnever to return."
msgstr ""
"Si ses bras en voile paralysent et enlacent\\nun ennemi, celui-ci est "
"entraîné à huit\\nkilomètres sous l’eau, dans son repaire, à\\njamais."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9060
msgid "JELLICENT"
msgstr "MOYADE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9066
msgid ""
"They propel themselves by expelling\\nabsorbed seawater from their "
"bodies.\\nIt's said there's a castle of ships\\nJellicent have sunk on the "
"seafloor."
msgstr ""
"Il se propulse en expulsant l’eau de mer\\nqu’il absorbe. Les Moyade "
"auraient un\\nchâteau fait de navires coulés au fond des\\nmers."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9150
msgid "ALOMOMOLA"
msgstr "MAMANBO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9153
msgid "Caring"
msgstr "Soigneur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9156
msgid ""
"When they find a wounded Pokémon,\\nthey embrace it and bring it to "
"shore.\\nThe special membrane enveloping\\nAlomomola has the ability to heal"
" wounds."
msgstr ""
"Quand il trouve un Pokémon blessé, il\\nl’enlace et le ramène au rivage. La "
"membrane\\nqui l’enveloppe a le pouvoir de guérir."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9220
msgid "JOLTIK"
msgstr "STATITIK"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9223
msgid "Attaching"
msgstr "Crampon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9226
msgid ""
"Since they can't generate their own\\nelectricity, they attach themselves "
"to\\nlarge-bodied Pokémon and absorb static\\nelectricity, which they store "
"in a pouch."
msgstr ""
"Incapable de produire de l’électricité, il\\ns’accroche à de gros Pokémon "
"pour absorber\\nleur électricité statique et la stocker."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9291
msgid "GALVANTULA"
msgstr "MYGAVOLT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9294
msgid "EleSpider"
msgstr "Araclectrik"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9297
msgid ""
"It creates barriers from electrified silk\\nthat stun foes. This works as a "
"weapon as\\nwell as a defense. While it is immobilized\\nby shock, they "
"leisurely consume it."
msgstr ""
"Il tisse des toiles de soie électrifiée qui\\nparalysent ses ennemis, à la "
"fois arme et\\ndéfense. Il dévore ensuite sa proie sans se\\npresser."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9366
msgid "FERROSEED"
msgstr "GRINDUR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9369
msgid "Thorn Seed"
msgstr "Graine Épine"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9372
msgid ""
"It absorbs the iron it finds in the rock\\nwhile clinging to the ceiling of "
"caves.\\nWhen threatened, it attacks by shooting\\na barrage of spikes."
msgstr ""
"Accroché au plafond des grottes, il\\nabsorbe le fer de la roche. Menacé, "
"il\\nattaque en tirant une salve de pointes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9442
msgid "FERROTHORN"
msgstr "NOACIER"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9445
msgid "Thorn Pod"
msgstr "Boule Épine"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9448
msgid ""
"It fights by swinging around its three\\nspiky feelers and shooting "
"spikes.\\nA hit from these steel spikes can reduce\\na boulder to rubble."
msgstr ""
"Il combat en faisant tournoyer ses trois\\ntentacules et en tirant des "
"pointes\\nd’acier capables de réduire un rocher en\\nmiettes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9515
msgid "KLINK"
msgstr "TIC"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9518
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9589
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9660
msgid "Gear"
msgstr "Engrenage"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9521
msgid ""
"Two bodies comprise a fixed pair.\\nThe two minigears that mesh "
"together\\nare predetermined. Each will rebound from\\nother minigears "
"without meshing."
msgstr ""
"Ses deux corps forment un duo inséparable.\\nLeurs engrenages ne s’emboîtent"
" qu’entre\\neux et rebondissent sur tous les autres."

#. source : patch FR actuel (correspondance douteuse, à vérifier)
#. source : patch FR actuel (récupéré par pointeur)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9586
msgid "KLANG"
msgstr "ICLIC"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9592
msgid ""
"A minigear and big gear comprise its\\nbody. Spinning minigears are "
"rotated\\nat high speed and repeatedly fired away.\\nIt is dangerous if the "
"gears don't return."
msgstr ""
"Son corps est formé d’un petit et d’un\\ngrand engrenage. Il lance le petit "
"en le\\nfaisant tourner très vite. Gare s’il ne\\nrevient pas!"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9657
msgid "KLINKLANG"
msgstr "CLITICLIC"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9663
msgid ""
"Its red core functions as an energy tank.\\nIt is rotated at high speed for "
"a rapid\\nenergy charge. It fires the charged energy\\nthrough its spikes "
"into an area."
msgstr ""
"Son noyau rouge lui sert de réservoir\\nd’énergie. Il le fait tourner très "
"vite pour\\nse recharger, puis libère l’énergie par ses\\npointes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9728
msgid "TYNAMO"
msgstr "ANCHWATT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9731
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9814
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9885
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9963
msgid "EleFish"
msgstr "Électrophore"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9734
msgid ""
"These Pokémon move in schools.\\nOne alone can emit only a trickle "
"of\\nelectricity, so a group of them gathers\\nto unleash a powerful "
"electric shock."
msgstr ""
"Ils se déplacent en bancs. Seul, il ne\\nproduit qu’un filet d’électricité, "
"alors ils\\nse regroupent pour lancer de puissantes\\ndécharges."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9811
msgid "EELEKTRIK"
msgstr "LAMPEROIE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9817
msgid ""
"These Pokémon have a big appetite.\\nIt wraps itself around its prey "
"and\\nparalyzes it with electricity from the\\nround spots on its sides. "
"Then it chomps."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon est très vorace. Il s’enroule\\nautour de sa proie, la paralyse "
"avec les\\ntaches rondes de ses flancs, puis la\\ncroque."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9882
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9956
msgid "EELEKTROSS"
msgstr "OHMASSACRE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9888
msgid ""
"They crawl out of the ocean using their\\narms. They will attack prey on "
"shore and\\nimmediately drag it into the ocean, with\\ntheir sucker mouths."
msgstr ""
"Il sort de l’océan à la force des bras. Il\\nattaque les proies sur le "
"rivage et les\\nentraîne aussitôt sous l’eau avec sa\\nbouche-ventouse."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:9966
msgid ""
"It now generates 10 times the\\nelectricity it did before Mega\\nEvolving. "
"It discharges this energy\\nfrom its false Eelektrik made of mucus."
msgstr ""
"Il produit maintenant 10 fois plus\\nd’électricité qu’avant sa\\nMéga-"
"Évolution. Il la décharge par son\\nfaux LAMPEROIE fait de mucus."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10018
msgid "ELGYEM"
msgstr "LEWSOR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10021
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10095
msgid "Cerebral"
msgstr "Cerveau"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10024
msgid ""
"It psychically squeezes the brain of\\nits foe, causing unendurable "
"headaches.\\nRumors of its origin are linked to a UFO\\ncrash site in the "
"desert 50 years ago."
msgstr ""
"Il compresse le cerveau de ses ennemis par\\ntélékinésie, causant d’atroces "
"migraines.\\nOn le lie à un crash d’OVNI dans le désert."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10092
msgid "BEHEEYEM"
msgstr "NEITRAM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10098
msgid ""
"It can manipulate an opponent's memory.\\nApparently, it communicates by "
"flashing\\nits three fingers, but those patterns\\nhaven't been decoded. "
msgstr ""
"Il peut manipuler la mémoire de ses ennemis.\\nIl communiquerait en faisant "
"clignoter ses\\ntrois doigts, mais nul n’a percé ce code."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10165
msgid "LITWICK"
msgstr "FUNECIRE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10168
msgid "Candle"
msgstr "Chandelle"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10171
msgid ""
"While Litwick shines a light and pretends\\nto be a guide, it absorbs the "
"life force of\\nany who follow it, which becomes the fuel\\nthat it burns."
msgstr ""
"Funécire fait mine de guider les gens avec\\nsa lumière, mais absorbe "
"l’énergie vitale de\\nceux qui le suivent pour nourrir sa flamme."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10239
msgid "LAMPENT"
msgstr "MELANCOLUX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10242
msgid "Lamp"
msgstr "Lampe"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10245
msgid ""
"This ominous Pokémon is feared.\\nThrough cities it wanders, searching\\nfor"
" the spirits of the fallen. The spirits\\nit absorbs fuel its baleful fire."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon sinistre erre dans les villes en\\nquête d’âmes défuntes. Les "
"âmes qu’il\\nabsorbe alimentent son feu funeste."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10313
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10385
msgid "CHANDELURE"
msgstr "LUGULABRE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10316
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10392
msgid "Luring"
msgstr "Invitation"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10319
msgid ""
"Being consumed in Chandelure's flame burns\\nup the spirit, leaving the body"
" behind.\\nBy waving the flames on its arms, it puts\\nits foes into a "
"hypnotic trance."
msgstr ""
"Sa flamme brûle l’âme et ne laisse que le\\ncorps. En agitant les flammes de"
" ses bras,\\nil plonge ses ennemis dans une transe\\nhypnotique."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10395
msgid ""
"One of its eyes is a window linking\\nour world with the afterlife.\\nThis "
"Pokémon draws in hatred and\\nconverts it into power."
msgstr ""
"L’un de ses yeux est une fenêtre qui\\nrelie notre monde à l’au-delà. "
"Ce\\nPokémon absorbe la haine et la change\\nen puissance."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10447
msgid "AXEW"
msgstr "COUPENOTTE"

#. source : relu et corrigé à la main
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10450
msgid "Tusk"
msgstr "Défense"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10453
msgid ""
"They mark their territory by leaving\\ngashes in trees with their tusks. If "
"a\\ntusk breaks, a new one grows in quickly,\\nharder and sturdier than the "
"last."
msgstr ""
"Il marque son territoire en entaillant les\\narbres de ses défenses. Si "
"l’une casse, une\\nnouvelle repousse vite, encore plus solide."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10515
msgid "FRAXURE"
msgstr "INCISACHE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10518
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10585
msgid "Axe Jaw"
msgstr "Hachomenton"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10521
msgid ""
"Their tusks can shatter rocks.\\nA broken tusk will not grow back,\\nso it "
"diligently sharpens its tusks on\\nriver rocks after the end of a battle."
msgstr ""
"Ses défenses brisent la roche. Une défense\\ncassée ne repousse pas, alors "
"il les aiguise\\navec soin sur les rochers des rivières."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10582
msgid "HAXORUS"
msgstr "TRANCHODON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10588
msgid ""
"They are kind but can be relentless\\nwhen defending territory. Their "
"sturdy\\ntusks will stay sharp even if used to cut\\nsteel beams."
msgstr ""
"Gentils mais impitoyables quand ils\\ndéfendent leur territoire, ils ont "
"des\\ndéfenses qui restent tranchantes même sur\\ndes poutres d’acier."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10656
msgid "CUBCHOO"
msgstr "POLARHUME"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10659
msgid "Chill"
msgstr "Gelé"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10662
msgid ""
"Its nose is always running.\\nTheir snot is a barometer of health.\\nWhen "
"healthy, their snot is sticky and\\nthe power of their ice moves increases."
msgstr ""
"Son nez coule sans arrêt et sa morve trahit\\nsa santé: quand il va bien, "
"elle est collante\\net ses capacités Glace sont plus fortes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10729
msgid "BEARTIC"
msgstr "POLAGRIFFE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10732
msgid "Freezing"
msgstr "Congelé"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10735
msgid ""
"It freezes its breath to create fangs\\nand claws of ice to fight "
"with.\\nVery able in the water, it swims around\\nin northern seas and "
"catches prey."
msgstr ""
"Il gèle son souffle pour se faire des crocs\\net des griffes de glace. Très "
"à l’aise dans\\nl’eau, il chasse dans les mers du Nord."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10800
msgid "CRYOGONAL"
msgstr "HEXAGEL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10803
msgid "Crystallize"
msgstr "Cristal"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10806
msgid ""
"They are born in snow clouds. When\\nits body temperature goes up, it "
"turns\\ninto steam and vanishes. When its\\ntemperature lowers, it returns "
"to ice."
msgstr ""
"Il naît dans les nuages de neige. Si sa\\ntempérature monte, il se change en"
" vapeur\\net disparaît. Quand elle baisse, il\\nredevient glace."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10872
msgid "SHELMET"
msgstr "ESCARGAUME"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10875
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:5376
msgid "Snail"
msgstr "Escargot"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10878
msgid ""
"When attacked, it defends itself by\\nclosing the lid of its shell. It "
"evolves\\nwhen bathed in an electric-like energy\\nalong with Karrablast."
msgstr ""
"Attaqué, il se défend en fermant le\\ncouvercle de sa coquille. Il évolue "
"s’il\\nreçoit une énergie électrique avec\\nCarabing."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10944
msgid "ACCELGOR"
msgstr "LIMASPEED"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10947
msgid "Shell Out"
msgstr "Exuviateur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:10950
msgid ""
"When its body dries out, it weakens. So, to\\nprevent dehydration, it wraps "
"itself in\\nlayers of thin membrane. It is very light\\nand fights with "
"ninja-like movements."
msgstr ""
"Quand il se dessèche, il faiblit. Pour\\nl’éviter, il s’enveloppe de fines "
"membranes.\\nTrès léger, il combat comme un ninja."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11013
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11086
msgid "STUNFISK"
msgstr "LIMONDE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11016
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11094
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_9_families.h:873
msgid "Trap"
msgstr "Piège"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11019
msgid ""
"It conceals itself in the mud of the\\nseashore. Then it waits. When prey "
"touch\\nit, it delivers a jolt of electricity.\\nIt smiles when transmitting"
" electricity."
msgstr ""
"Il se cache dans la boue du rivage et\\nattend. Quand une proie le touche, "
"il\\nl’électrocute. Il sourit quand il envoie du\\ncourant."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11084
msgid "STUNFISK-G"
msgstr "LIMONDE-G"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11097
msgid ""
"Its conspicuous lips lure prey in\\nas it lies in wait in the mud. "
"When\\nprey gets close, Stunfisk clamps its\\njagged steel fins down on "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Tapi dans la boue, il attire ses proies avec\\nses lèvres voyantes. Quand "
"elles\\napprochent, Limonde les broie entre ses\\nnageoires d’acier "
"dentelées."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11165
msgid "MIENFOO"
msgstr "KUNGFOUINE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11168
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11236
msgid "Martial Arts"
msgstr "Art Martial"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11171
msgid ""
"They have mastered elegant combos.\\nAs they concentrate, their battle "
"moves\\nbecome swifter and more precise. What it\\nlacks in power, it makes "
"up for in quantity."
msgstr ""
"Il maîtrise d’élégants enchaînements, plus\\nvifs et précis à mesure qu’il "
"se concentre.\\nIl compense son manque de force par le\\nnombre."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11233
msgid "MIENSHAO"
msgstr "SHAOFOUINE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11239
msgid ""
"They use the long fur on their arms as\\na whip to strike their opponents. "
"Its arm\\nattacks come with such rapidity that they\\ncannot even be seen."
msgstr ""
"Il fouette ses ennemis avec les longs poils\\nde ses bras. Ses attaques sont"
" si rapides\\nqu’elles en deviennent invisibles."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11307
msgid "DRUDDIGON"
msgstr "DRAKKARMIN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11313
msgid ""
"It warms its body by absorbing sunlight\\nwith its wings. When its body "
"temperature\\nfalls, it can no longer move. It uses its\\nsharp claws to "
"catch prey."
msgstr ""
"Il se réchauffe en absorbant le soleil avec\\nses ailes. Si sa température "
"baisse, il ne\\npeut plus bouger. Ses griffes attrapent\\nses proies."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11383
msgid "GOLETT"
msgstr "GRINGOLEM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11386
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11456
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11531
msgid "Automaton"
msgstr "Golem Ancien"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11389
msgid ""
"These Pokémon are thought to have\\nbeen created by the science of "
"an\\nancient and mysterious civilization.\\nIt's been active for thousands "
"of years."
msgstr ""
"Ces Pokémon auraient été créés par la\\nscience d’une mystérieuse "
"civilisation\\nantique. Ils sont actifs depuis des\\nmillénaires."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11453
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11524
msgid "GOLURK"
msgstr "GOLEMASTOC"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11459
msgid ""
"Golurk were created to protect people\\nand Pokémon by an ancient "
"civilisation.\\nRemoving the seal on its chest makes its\\ninternal energy "
"go out of control."
msgstr ""
"Une civilisation antique l’a créé pour\\nprotéger les gens et les Pokémon. "
"Si on\\nretire le sceau de son torse, son énergie\\nse déchaîne."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11534
msgid ""
"The energy within Golurk has been\\nstimulated by Mega Evolution.\\nThe "
"Pokémon could explode at any moment."
msgstr ""
"L’énergie de GOLEMASTOC a été stimulée\\npar la Méga-Évolution. Ce "
"Pokémon\\npourrait exploser à tout moment."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11584
msgid "PAWNIARD"
msgstr "SCALPION"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11587
msgid "Sharp Blade"
msgstr "Coupant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11590
msgid ""
"Ignoring their injuries, groups attack by\\nsinking the blades that cover "
"their bodies\\ninto their prey. If battling dulls them, it\\nsharpens them "
"on stones by the river."
msgstr ""
"Insensibles aux blessures, ils attaquent\\nen groupe et plantent leurs lames"
" dans\\nleurs proies. Ils les aiguisent sur les\\npierres des rivières."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11659
msgid "BISHARP"
msgstr "SCALPROIE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11662
msgid "Sword Blade"
msgstr "Tranchant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11665
msgid ""
"This pitiless Pokémon commands a group\\nof Pawniard to hound prey into "
"immobility.\\nIt battles to become the boss, but will be\\ndriven from the "
"group if it loses."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon sans pitié commande des\\nScalpion qui traquent ses proies. Il se"
" bat\\npour être le chef et est chassé du groupe\\ns’il perd."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11730
msgid "KINGAMBIT"
msgstr "SCALPEREUR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11733
msgid "Big Blade"
msgstr "Pourfendant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11736
msgid ""
"Though it commands a massive army\\nin battle, it's not skilled "
"at\\ndevising complex strategies. It just uses\\nbrute strength to keep "
"pushing."
msgstr ""
"Il commande une immense armée, mais\\nn’est pas doué pour les "
"stratégies\\ncomplexes. Il se contente d’avancer\\npar la force brute."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11796
msgid "BOUFFALANT"
msgstr "FRISON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11799
msgid "Bash Buffalo"
msgstr "Coup d’Bœuf"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11802
msgid ""
"Their fluffy fur absorbs damage, even\\nif they strike foes with a fierce "
"headbutt.\\nTheir headbutts have enough destructive\\nforce to derail a "
"train."
msgstr ""
"Son pelage touffu amortit les chocs de ses\\nviolents coups de tête, assez "
"puissants\\npour faire dérailler un train."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11866
msgid "RUFFLET"
msgstr "FURAIGLON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11869
msgid "Eaglet"
msgstr "Aiglon"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11872
msgid ""
"With its sharp claws, this Pokémon pierces\\nits prey, and then it pecks at "
"them.\\nAlthough it also consumes berries, it's a\\ncarnivore at heart."
msgstr ""
"Il agrippe ses proies avec ses serres\\neffilées et les picore. Il lui "
"arrive de\\nmanger des Baies, mais au fond c’est un\\ncarnivore."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11941
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12014
msgid "BRAVIARY"
msgstr "GUERIAIGLE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11944
msgid "Valiant"
msgstr "Vaillant"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:11947
msgid ""
"For the sake of its friends, this brave\\nwarrior of the sky will not stop "
"battling,\\neven if it is injured. One can carry a car\\nwhile flying."
msgstr ""
"Pour ses amis, ce brave guerrier du ciel\\ncombat même blessé. Il peut "
"soulever une\\nvoiture en plein vol."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12012
msgid "BRAVIARY-H"
msgstr "GUERIAIGLE-H"

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12022
msgid "Battle Cry"
msgstr "Cri Guerrier"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12025
msgid ""
"Screaming a bloodcurdling battle\\ncry, this huge and ferocious "
"bird\\nPokémon goes out on the hunt."
msgstr ""
"Ce grand oiseau féroce part à la chasse en\\npoussant un cri de guerre à "
"glacer le sang."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12092
msgid "VULLABY"
msgstr "VOSTOURNO"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12095
msgid "Diapered"
msgstr "Couche"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12098
msgid ""
"It can't fly yet and must wait until its\\nwings have developed more. They "
"guard\\ntheir posteriors with bones that were\\ngathered by Mandibuzz."
msgstr ""
"Il ne sait pas encore voler et attend que\\nses ailes poussent. Il protège "
"son derrière\\navec des os rassemblés par Vaututrice."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12162
msgid "MANDIBUZZ"
msgstr "VAUTUTRICE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12165
msgid "Bone Vulture"
msgstr "Vostour"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12168
msgid ""
"They adorn themselves beautifully with\\nbones. This is supposedly an effort"
" to\\nattract males, but no male Mandibuzz\\nhave ever been found."
msgstr ""
"Les Vaututrice se parent d’ossements pour\\nleur parade nuptiale. On attend "
"toujours\\nde découvrir si les mâles existent."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12231
msgid "HEATMOR"
msgstr "AFLAMANOIR"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12234
msgid "Anteater"
msgstr "Tamanoir"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12237
msgid ""
"It draws in air through its tail,\\ntransforms it into fire, and uses it "
"like\\na tongue. They burn through Durant's steel\\nbodies and consume their"
" insides."
msgstr ""
"Il aspire l’air par la queue et le change en\\nflammes qui lui servent de "
"langue. Il perce\\nl’armure des Fermite pour les dévorer."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12300
msgid "DURANT"
msgstr "FERMITE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12303
msgid "Iron Ant"
msgstr "Fourmi Dure"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12306
msgid ""
"Durant dig nests in mountains.\\nIndividuals each play different roles "
"in\\ndriving Heatmor, their natural predator,\\naway from their colony."
msgstr ""
"Les Fermite creusent leurs nids en\\nmontagne. Chacun joue un rôle "
"pour\\nrepousser Aflamanoir, leur prédateur\\nnaturel."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12384
msgid "DEINO"
msgstr "SOLOCHI"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12387
msgid "Irate"
msgstr "Rude"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12390
msgid ""
"Lacking sight, it's unaware of its\\nsurroundings, so it bumps into things "
"and\\neats anything that moves. Approaching\\nit carelessly is dangerous."
msgstr ""
"Aveugle, il se cogne partout et mord tout\\nce qui bouge. Il est dangereux "
"de\\nl’approcher sans précaution."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12453
msgid "ZWEILOUS"
msgstr "DIAMAT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12459
msgid ""
"After it has eaten up all the food in its\\nterritory, it moves on to "
"another area.\\nWhichever head eats more than the other\\ngets to be the "
"leader."
msgstr ""
"Après avoir dévoré toute la nourriture de\\nson territoire, il part "
"ailleurs. La tête qui\\nmange le plus devient le chef."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12520
msgid "HYDREIGON"
msgstr "TRIOXHYDRE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12526
msgid ""
"This brutal Pokémon travels the skies on\\nits six wings. The heads on their"
" arms do\\nnot have brains. They use all three heads\\nto consume and "
"destroy everything."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon brutal sillonne le ciel sur ses\\nsix ailes. Les têtes de ses "
"bras n’ont pas\\nde cerveau. Ses trois têtes dévorent tout."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12595
msgid "LARVESTA"
msgstr "PYRONILLE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12598
msgid "Torch"
msgstr "Torche"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12601
msgid ""
"This Pokémon was believed to have\\nbeen born from the sun. It spews fire "
"from\\nits horns and encases itself in a cocoon\\nof fire when it evolves."
msgstr ""
"On pensait que ce Pokémon était né du\\nsoleil. Il crache du feu par ses "
"cornes et\\ns’enferme dans un cocon de feu pour\\névoluer."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12674
msgid "VOLCARONA"
msgstr "PYRAX"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12680
msgid ""
"When volcanic ash darkened the\\natmosphere, it appeared and saved "
"Pokémon\\nfrom freezing, Volcarona's fire provided a\\nreplacement for the "
"sun."
msgstr ""
"Quand des cendres volcaniques ont\\nobscurci le ciel, son feu a remplacé "
"le\\nsoleil et sauvé les Pokémon du froid."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12745
msgid "COBALION"
msgstr "COBALTIUM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12748
msgid "Iron Will"
msgstr "Cœur de Fer"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12751
msgid ""
"It has a body and heart of steel. This\\nlegendary Pokémon battled against "
"humans\\nto protect Pokémon. Its personality\\nis calm and composed."
msgstr ""
"Il a un corps et un cœur d’acier. Ce Pokémon\\nlégendaire a combattu les "
"humains pour\\nprotéger les Pokémon. Il est calme et posé."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12816
msgid "TERRAKION"
msgstr "TERRAKIUM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12819
msgid "Cavern"
msgstr "Grotte"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12822
msgid ""
"Spoken of in legend, this Pokémon used\\nits phenomenal power to destroy a "
"castle\\nin its effort to protect Pokémon that had\\nlost their homes in a "
"war among humans."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon légendaire a détruit un château\\nde sa force colossale pour "
"protéger les\\nPokémon privés de foyer par une guerre\\nhumaine."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12891
msgid "VIRIZION"
msgstr "VIRIDIUM"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Plaine Verte
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12894
msgid "Grassland"
msgstr "Grassland"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12897
msgid ""
"Its head sprouts horns as sharp as blades.\\nLegends say this Pokémon "
"used\\nwhirlwind-like movements to confound\\nand swiftly cut its opponents."
msgstr ""
"Sa tête porte des cornes affûtées comme\\ndes lames. Selon la légende, il "
"déroutait et\\ntranchait ses ennemis tel un tourbillon."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12961
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13052
msgid "TORNADUS"
msgstr "BOREAS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12964
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13055
msgid "Cyclone"
msgstr "Tornade"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:12967
msgid ""
"Tornadus expels massive energy from\\nits tail, causing severe storms.\\nIts"
" power can blow entire houses away.\\nIt zooms through the sky at 200 mph."
msgstr ""
"Boréas libère une immense énergie par la\\nqueue et déclenche des tempêtes "
"qui\\nemportent les maisons. Il vole à 300 km/h."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13058
msgid ""
"An example of what is known as a\\n“form change”. Tornadus has "
"been\\nsighted crossing the ocean while in this\\nform."
msgstr ""
"Un exemple de ce qu’on appelle un\\n“changement de forme”. On a vu\\nBoréas "
"traverser l’océan sous\\ncette forme."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13128
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13219
msgid "THUNDURUS"
msgstr "FULGURIS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13134
msgid ""
"The spikes on its tail discharge immense\\nbolts of lightning. Countless "
"charred\\nremains mar the landscape of places\\nthrough which Thundurus has "
"passed."
msgstr ""
"Les pointes de sa queue lancent de\\nterribles éclairs. Des débris "
"calcinés\\njonchent les lieux où Fulguris est passé."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13225
msgid ""
"It pulverizes foes into nothingness\\nwith showers of "
"devastatingly\\npowerful lightning bolts launched\\nfrom the string of orbs "
"on its tail."
msgstr ""
"Il réduit ses ennemis à néant sous\\nune pluie d’éclairs "
"dévastateurs\\nlancés depuis le chapelet d’orbes\\nde sa queue."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13307
msgid "RESHIRAM"
msgstr "RESHIRAM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13310
msgid "Vast White"
msgstr "Blanc Réel"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13313
msgid ""
"This Pokémon appears in legends. It\\nsends flames into the air from its "
"tail,\\nburning up everything around it. It helps\\nthose who want to build "
"a world of truth."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon légendaire crache des flammes\\npar la queue et brûle tout "
"alentour. Il aide\\nceux qui veulent bâtir un monde de vérité."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13378
msgid "ZEKROM"
msgstr "ZEKROM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13381
msgid "Deep Black"
msgstr "Noir Idéal"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13384
msgid ""
"This legendary Pokémon can scorch the\\nworld with lightning. It has a "
"generator\\nthat creates electricity in its tail. It\\nassists those with "
"strong ideals."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon légendaire peut embraser le\\nmonde d’éclairs grâce au générateur"
" de sa\\nqueue. Il aide ceux qui ont de grands\\nidéaux."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13449
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13540
msgid "LANDORUS"
msgstr "DEMETEROS"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13452
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13543
msgid "Abundance"
msgstr "Fertilité"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13455
msgid ""
"The energy that comes pouring from its\\ntail increases the nutrition in the"
" soil,\\ngranting bountiful crops. It has been\\nhailed as “The Guardian of "
"the Fields.”"
msgstr ""
"L’énergie qui jaillit de sa queue fertilise\\nla terre et donne de belles "
"récoltes. On le\\nsurnomme “le Gardien des Champs”."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13546
msgid ""
"Landorus soars through the sky in\\nthis form, bestowing "
"plentiful\\nharvests upon the land and earning the\\npeople's reverence."
msgstr ""
"Sous cette forme, Démétéros parcourt\\nle ciel en offrant aux terres "
"des\\nrécoltes abondantes, ce qui lui vaut\\nla vénération des gens."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13619
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13693
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13766
msgid "KYUREM"
msgstr "KYUREM"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13622
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13696
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13769
msgid "Boundary"
msgstr "Frontière"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13625
msgid ""
"This legendary ice Pokémon waits for a\\nhero to fill in the missing parts "
"of its\\nbody with truth or ideals. Its body became\\nfrozen when its energy"
" leaked out."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon légendaire attend un héros qui\\ncomblera son corps de vérité ou "
"d’idéal. Il\\na gelé quand son énergie s’est échappée."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13699
msgid ""
"The sameness of Reshiram's and\\nKyurem's genes allowed Kyurem to\\nabsorb "
"Reshiram. Kyurem can now use the\\npower of both fire and ice."
msgstr ""
"RESHIRAM et KYUREM ont les mêmes\\ngènes. KYUREM a donc pu "
"absorber\\lRESHIRAM. Il peut désormais user du\\lfeu et de la glace."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13772
msgid ""
"The sameness of Zekrom's and\\nKyurem's genes allowed Kyurem to "
"absorb\\nZekrom. Kyurem can now use the\\npower of both electricity and ice."
msgstr ""
"ZEKROM et KYUREM ont les mêmes\\ngènes. KYUREM a donc pu absorber\\lZEKROM. "
"Il peut désormais user de\\ll’électricité et de la glace."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13841
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13913
msgid "KELDEO"
msgstr "KELDEO"

#. source : SoulSilver FR officiel
#. patch FR actuel : Poulain
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13844
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13916
msgid "Colt"
msgstr "Craig"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13847
msgid ""
"When it is resolute, its body fills with\\npower and it becomes swifter. It "
"crosses\\nthe world, running over the surfaces of\\noceans and rivers."
msgstr ""
"Quand il est déterminé, son corps déborde\\nd’énergie et il devient plus "
"rapide. Il\\nparcourt le monde en courant sur l’eau."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13919
msgid ""
"The power that lay hidden in its\\nbody now covers its horn, turning "
"it\\ninto a sword that can slice through\\nanything."
msgstr ""
"La force cachée dans son corps\\nrecouvre désormais sa corne, qui\\ndevient "
"une épée capable de tout\\ntrancher."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13984
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:14066
msgid "MELOETTA"
msgstr "MELOETTA"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13987
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:14069
msgid "Melody"
msgstr "Mélodie"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:13990
msgid ""
"The melodies sung by Meloetta have the\\npower to make Pokémon that hear "
"them\\nhappy or sad. Many famous songs have been\\ninspired by the tunes "
"that Meloetta plays."
msgstr ""
"Les mélodies de Meloetta rendent joyeux ou\\ntristes les Pokémon qui les "
"entendent.\\nElles ont inspiré de nombreuses chansons\\ncélèbres."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:14072
msgid ""
"Meloetta's melodies are sung with\\na special vocalization method that "
"can\\ncontrol the feelings of those who hear it."
msgstr ""
"Meloetta chante ses mélodies avec\\nune technique vocale qui contrôle\\nles "
"émotions de ceux qui l’écoutent."

#. source : traduction manuelle (style SoulSilver)
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:14146
msgid "GENESECT"
msgstr "GENESECT"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_5_families.h:14149
msgid "Paleozoic"
msgstr "Paléozoïque"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:26
msgid "CHESPIN"
msgstr "MARISSON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:29
msgid "Spiny Nut"
msgstr "Bogue"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:32
msgid ""
"The quills on its head are usually soft.\\nWhen it flexes them, the points "
"become\\nso hard and sharp that they can pierce\\nrock without any effort."
msgstr ""
"Les piquants de sa tête sont souples.\\nQuand il les contracte, ils "
"deviennent si\\ndurs qu’ils percent la roche sans effort."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:97
msgid "QUILLADIN"
msgstr "BOGUERISSE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:100
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:170
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:244
msgid "Spiny Armor"
msgstr "Épinarmure"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:103
msgid ""
"They strengthen the sturdy shell covering\\ntheir bodies by running into one"
" another.\\nThey are very kind and won't start fights,\\nbut will "
"counterattack with sharp quills."
msgstr ""
"Ils renforcent leur carapace en se\\nrentrant dedans. Très gentils, ils "
"ne\\ncherchent pas la bagarre, mais ripostent\\navec leurs piquants."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:167
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:237
msgid "CHESNAUGHT"
msgstr "BLINDEPIQUE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:173
msgid ""
"It shields its allies from danger with\\nits own body. When it takes a "
"defensive\\nposture with its fists guarding its face,\\nit can withstand a "
"bomb blast."
msgstr ""
"Il protège ses alliés de son propre corps.\\nLorsqu’il se met en garde, "
"poings devant le\\nvisage, il résiste même à une bombe."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:247
msgid ""
"It has fortified armor and a\\nwill to defend at all costs.\\nBoth are "
"absurdly strong."
msgstr ""
"Il a une armure renforcée et la\\nvolonté de défendre coûte que coûte.\\nLes"
" deux sont d’une force absurde."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:297
msgid "FENNEKIN"
msgstr "FEUNNEC"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:303
msgid ""
"As it walks, it munches on a twig to fill\\nitself with energy in place of a"
" snack.\\nIt intimidates opponents by puffing hot\\nair out of its roomy "
"ears."
msgstr ""
"En marchant, il grignote une brindille en\\nguise d’en-cas. Il intimide ses "
"ennemis en\\nsoufflant de l’air chaud par ses oreilles."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:370
msgid "BRAIXEN"
msgstr "ROUSSIL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:376
msgid ""
"Braixen has a twig stuck in its tail.\\nWhen the twig is plucked from its "
"tail,\\nfriction sets the twig alight. The flame\\nis used to send signals "
"to its allies."
msgstr ""
"Il garde une brindille dans sa queue. Quand\\nil la retire, la friction "
"l’enflamme. Il s’en\\nsert pour faire des signaux à ses alliés."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:438
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:512
msgid "DELPHOX"
msgstr "GOUPELIN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:444
msgid ""
"It gazes into the flame at the tip of its\\nbranch to achieve a focused "
"state, which\\nallows it to see into the future. It uses\\npsychic power to "
"incinerate its foes."
msgstr ""
"En fixant la flamme au bout de sa branche,\\nil entre en transe et lit "
"l’avenir. Il brûle\\nses ennemis par la force psychique."

#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:522
msgid ""
"It wields flaming branches to\\ndazzle its opponents before\\nincinerating "
"them with a\\nhuge fireball."
msgstr ""
"Il manie des branches enflammées\\npour éblouir ses adversaires avant "
"de\\nles incinérer d’une énorme boule de\\nfeu."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:574
msgid "FROAKIE"
msgstr "GRENOUSSE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:577
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:650
msgid "Bubble Frog"
msgstr "Crapobulle"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:580
msgid ""
"It protects its skin by covering its body\\nin bubbles it secretes from its "
"chest and\\nback. Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it\\nkeeps a watchful eye "
"on its surroundings."
msgstr ""
"Il protège sa peau avec des bulles\\nsécrétées par son torse et son dos. "
"Sous\\nson air insouciant, il reste toujours sur\\nses gardes."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:647
msgid "FROGADIER"
msgstr "CROAPORAL"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:653
msgid ""
"It can throw bubble-covered pebbles with\\nprecise control, hitting empty "
"cans up to\\na hundred feet away. Frogadier's swiftness\\nis unparalleled."
msgstr ""
"Il lance avec précision des cailloux\\nenrobés de bulles sur des canettes "
"à\\ntrente mètres. Sa rapidité est sans égale."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:715
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:777
