#. source : traduction nouvelle
#. lot : E_menus_donnees
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:922
msgid ""
"This Pokémon spins a giant\\nshuriken at high speed to make it\\nfloat, then"
" clings to it upside\\ndown to catch opponents unawares."
msgstr ""
"Il fait tourner un shuriken géant\\ntrès vite pour le faire flotter, "
"puis\\ls’y accroche tête en bas pour\\lsurprendre ses adversaires."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:974
msgid "BUNNELBY"
msgstr "SAPEREAU"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:977
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1045
msgid "Digging"
msgstr "Fouisseur"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:980
msgid ""
"It has ears like shovels. Digging holes\\nstrengthens its ears so much that "
"they\\ncan sever thick roots effortlessly.\\nBunnelby dig the whole night "
"through."
msgstr ""
"Ses oreilles sont comme des pelles. À force\\nde creuser, elles tranchent "
"sans effort de\\ngrosses racines. Il creuse toute la nuit."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1042
msgid "DIGGERSBY"
msgstr "EXCAVARENNE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1048
msgid ""
"With its powerful ears it reduces dense\\nbedrock to rubble. It can be a big"
" help\\nat construction sites. When it's finished\\ndigging, it lounges "
"about lazily."
msgstr ""
"Ses puissantes oreilles réduisent la roche\\nen miettes. Il rend de grands "
"services sur\\nles chantiers, puis paresse une fois le\\ntravail fini."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1110
msgid "FLETCHLING"
msgstr "PASSEROUGE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1113
msgid "Tiny Robin"
msgstr "Rougegorge"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1116
msgid ""
"This amiable Pokémon is easy to train.\\nBut when battle is joined, it shows"
" its\\nferocious side. It's merciless to\\nintruders that enter its "
"territory."
msgstr ""
"Ce Pokémon aimable est facile à dresser.\\nMais au combat, il se montre "
"féroce et\\nimpitoyable envers les intrus sur son\\nterritoire."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1183
msgid "FLETCHINDER"
msgstr "BRAISILLON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1189
msgid ""
"From its beak, it expels embers that set\\nthe tall grass on fire. Then it "
"pounces on\\nany bewildered Pokémon that pop out of\\nthe grass."
msgstr ""
"Il crache des braises qui embrasent les\\nhautes herbes, puis bondit sur les"
" Pokémon\\naffolés qui en sortent."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1257
msgid "TALONFLAME"
msgstr "FLAMBUSARD"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1260
msgid "Scorching"
msgstr "Fournaise"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1263
msgid ""
"In the fever of an exciting battle, it\\nshowers embers from the gaps "
"between its\\nfeathers and takes to the air. It finishes\\nits prey off with"
" a colossal kick."
msgstr ""
"Grisé par un combat palpitant, il projette\\ndes braises entre ses plumes et"
" s’envole.\\nIl achève ses proies d’un coup de serre\\ncolossal."

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1326
msgid "SCATTERBUG"
msgstr "LEPIDONILLE"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1329
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1414
msgid "Scatterdust"
msgstr "Exhalécaille"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1411
msgid "SPEWPA"
msgstr "PEREGRAIN"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1496
msgid "VIVILLON"
msgstr "PRISMILLON"

#. source : patch FR actuel
#: src/data/pokemon/species_info/gen_6_families.h:1499
msgid "Scale"
